      "name": "ReleaseAllMultiplayerCelFiles",
      "signature": "void ReleaseAllMultiplayerCelFiles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases all CelFile graphics resources used by the multiplayer lobby.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Destructor - called during module shutdown to free graphics memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. For each of 53 global CelFile pointers (g_pCelFileLobbySprite01-53):\n   a. Check if pointer is non-NULL\n   b. If non-NULL, call ReleaseCelFile() to free the graphics resource\n   c. Set the global pointer to NULL to prevent double-free\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nCaller Context:\n- Called by FUN_6fa04270 during D2Multi module shutdown sequence\n- Part of cleanup path after ShutdownSoundSystem, ReleaseAllCompositeUnits\n- Immediately before UnloadStringTable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointers are safely skipped (no release needed)\n- Uses __thiscall convention for ReleaseCelFile (pCelFile in ECX)\n- Note: At 0x6fa01c5a, assembly writes to g_pCelFileLobbySprite40 instead of g_pCelFileLobbySprite41 (possible bug or intentional reuse)\n\nMemory Model:\n- All 53 globals are CelFile* pointers to graphics sprite data\n- Ownership transferred to this function for cleanup\n- After return, all pointers are guaranteed NULL",
