      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Restores the current input pointer to the default stored in g_pDefaultInputPointer.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Thin wrapper that restores input context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the default input pointer from global g_pDefaultInputPointer\n2. Call SetCurrentInputPointer to set it as active\n3. Return\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nCallers:\n  - FUN_6fa10090: Called after dispatching inventory item handlers and setting current input item\n  - FUN_6fa11510: Called after initializing dialog UI elements\n  - FUN_6fa117b0: Called after cleaning up dialog state and setting current input item\n\nPurpose:\n  After changing input context via SetCurrentInputItem, this function restores the\n  input pointer to its default state stored in g_pDefaultInputPointer (0x6fa218d0).\n  This ensures consistent input handling after UI operations complete.",
