      "name": "ScrollAutomapUp",
      "signature": "int ScrollAutomapUp(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Scrolls the automap display up by 10 lines.\n\nClassification: Public API (UI callback handler)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load ECX with scroll delta value 10 (0x0A)\n2. Call AdjustAutomapScrollPosition (FUN_6fa0a950) to update scroll position\n3. Return 1 to indicate success\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns:\n- Always returns 1 (success)\n\nCalled By: UI system for automap scroll up button/key\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fa01f30: ScrollAutomapDown (passes ECX=-1)\n- FUN_6fa0a950: AdjustAutomapScrollPosition (helper that clamps position and updates arrow states)\n\nGlobals Accessed (via callee):\n- DAT_6fa21aa0: Current scroll position\n- DAT_6fa21a9c: Content line count\n- DAT_6fa216d4-DAT_6fa216e0: Scroll arrow UI bit masks\n\nNotes:\n- Scroll delta of 10 allows quick navigation through automap content\n- Position is clamped to valid range [0, lineCount-11] by helper\n- Helper updates UI arrow visibility based on scroll position",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:bcf5d077ac352e8f6e2f1a60c443b97a",
