      "name": "CloseInventoryPanelAndResetState",
      "signature": "bool CloseInventoryPanelAndResetState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Closes the inventory/create game panel and resets all associated state.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Reset function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if panel is active via GetUnitBitMask on g_dwInventorySlot5\n2. Early return 0 if panel not active\n3. Get edit box text from D2Win_GetEditBoxChild(g_dwInventorySlot7)\n4. Early return 1 if no edit box text exists\n5. Convert Unicode text to ANSI via Unicode::unicode2Win\n6. Call vtable callback at offset 0x1C with parameter 0\n7. Call FUN_6fa10090 and FUN_6fa0f490 (internal state reset)\n8. Dispatch inventory item handlers for slots 1-10\n9. Reset g_nNumSubChildren loop: iterate pdwCurrentSlot through g_apSubChildrenArray\n10. Set g_nNumSubChildren = 0\n11. Call SetCurrentInputItem and reset g_dwInventorySubState = 0\n12. Call FUN_6fa117b0 and reset g_dwInventoryExtraState = 0\n13. Dispatch handlers for slots 9-10\n14. If g_dwSpecialModeFlag == 1, call FUN_6fa127f0\n15. If g_dwInventoryPanelMode == 3, reset to 0\n16. If g_pInventoryPanelState != NULL, call SetOrClearBitMask with flag 1\n17. Reset button frame values for 3 button frames\n18. Set g_dwInventoryPanelMode = 0\n19. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None - this function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  bool - TRUE (1) if panel was closed successfully, FALSE (0) if panel not active\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early with 0 if GetUnitBitMask returns 0 (panel not active)\n  - Returns early with 1 if edit box child is NULL\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_nNumSubChildren, g_dwInventorySubState, g_dwInventoryExtraState,\n  g_dwInventoryPanelMode, button frame states",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:e4c303dc089ec9078b4efdc61bf38ed1",
