      "name": "InvokeCallbackOnArrayElements",
      "signature": "void InvokeCallbackOnArrayElements(void * pArrayBase, dword dwElementStride, int nElementCount, void * pfnCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Iterates over array elements and invokes callback function on each.\n\nClassification: Worker function - array callback iterator\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement element count and check if negative (skip if count <= 0)\n2. Save registers (EBX, EBP, ESI, EDI)\n3. Load callback pointer into EBX\n4. Load stride into EBP\n5. Load array base into ESI (current element pointer)\n6. Set loop counter EDI = count\n7. Loop: Set ECX = current element pointer, CALL callback\n8. Advance pointer: ESI += stride\n9. Decrement counter, repeat until zero\n10. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters:\n  pArrayBase (void *) - Base address of array to iterate\n  dwElementStride (dword) - Byte offset between elements (e.g., 2 for Unicode chars)\n  nElementCount (int) - Number of elements to process\n  pfnCallback (void *) - Function pointer called with ECX = element address\n\nReturns: void\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (callee cleans 0x10 bytes)\n\nUsage Context:\nCalled by FUN_6fa07aa0 to initialize Unicode arrays:\n  InvokeCallbackOnArrayElements(local_c0, 2, 0x10, _default_constructor_closure)\nThis calls default constructor on 16 Unicode elements with 2-byte stride.\n\nRegister Usage in Callback:\n  ECX = pointer to current array element (passed as this pointer)\n  Callback is responsible for initializing/processing that element",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d47a1859ed399da15e916c49ad1e466c",
