      "name": "PasswordSubPanelCallback",
      "signature": "void PasswordSubPanelCallback(int nEventCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Callback invoked when user cancels the password input sub-panel.\n\nClassification: Callback - Invoked by UI message pump when password dialog is dismissed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_fPasswordDialogCancelled flag to true (1)\n2. Return to caller (message pump will check flag and exit)\n\nParameters:\n- nEventCode (int): Event code from sub-panel system (ignored)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Parameter is ignored; function always sets cancelled flag regardless of event type\n- Called via _g_pfnSubPanelCallback function pointer set in RestoreMcpConnectionState\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_fPasswordDialogCancelled: Set to true to signal password entry was cancelled\n\nCaller Context:\n- Registered as callback in RestoreMcpConnectionState before password dialog loop\n- MessagePumpPasswordCallback checks g_fPasswordDialogCancelled to exit pump",
