      "name": "EnterBattleNetMultiplayerUI",
      "signature": "int EnterBattleNetMultiplayerUI(int pGameListData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes and runs the Battle.net multiplayer UI main loop.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Record start tick count for timing measurement\n2. Log \"D2MULTI: Start entering\" with timestamp\n3. Check if expansion MPQ exists and get data file path\n4. Initialize string tables; return 1 on failure\n5. Reset sub-panel and inventory panel states to 0\n6. Retrieve callback vtable from pGameListData+0x21d; assert if NULL\n7. Call vtable[0x74](fLoadExpansion) to validate; goto cleanup if fails\n8. Load Battle.net front-end cel images\n9. Set game state cursor and background configuration\n10. Create 17 UI objects from descriptor array (0x6fa1b150, stride 0x30)\n11. Create game list, character select, and input field controls\n12. Set up input field callbacks and max length (200 chars)\n13. Enable scroll arrow buttons (up/down for 2 lists)\n14. Create 11 game slot buttons (Y positions 0x28 to 0x2b4, stride 0x3c)\n15. Create scroll list control and clear visibility\n16. Clear 10 channel name buffers (256 bytes each at 0x6fa20aa4)\n17. Reset channel selection index to -1 and update flag to 0\n18. Initialize inventory slots 1-8, dispatch handlers\n19. Process sub-children array if count > 0\n20. Reset inventory sub-state and extra-state\n21. Handle special mode flag (call FUN_6fa127f0 if flag == 1)\n22. Handle inventory panel mode 3 -> 0 transition\n23. Set inventory panel visibility if exists\n24. Reset all button frame values to 0\n25. Create character info panel, MOTD text box, and chat text box controls\n26. Call Ordinal_10048 and Ordinal_10049 (D2Win UI setup)\n27. Initialize Unicode string array (512 elements)\n28. Build and display MOTD from linked list if chat box exists\n29. Create additional UI panels for character info display\n30. Check game list flags (bits 0x8 and 0x4) to disable buttons\n31. Initialize slot array and load cursor button WAV\n32. Play music if music options enabled (Ordinal_10034)\n33. Check character slot state at pGameListData+0x356\n34. Restore MCP connection state\n35. On success: format connection info and call vtable[0x54] callback\n36. On failure: log error and call vtable[0x10] callback\n37. Call vtable[0x74] again; if fails set state to 4\n38. On success: run message pump loop (MessagePumpLoop) with callback\n39. Check Ordinal_10052 result; if non-zero call 10054/10053\n40. Call vtable[0x58] cleanup callback\n41. Call Ordinal_10001 if state != 4\n42. CLEANUP PHASE: Log \"D2MULTI: Start closing\"\n43. Shutdown sound system and release composite units\n44. Dispatch inventory handlers for slots 1-10\n45. Process sub-children array again\n46. Release MOTD message linked list nodes\n47. Dispatch handlers for all created UI controls\n48. Clear global config and game state\n49. Release multiplayer cel files\n50. Unload string table\n51. Log \"D2MULTI: Finish closing\" with elapsed time\n\nParameters:\n  pGameListData (ECX) - Pointer to game list data structure containing:\n    +0x1ea: ushort flags (bits 0x4, 0x8, 0x20 used)\n    +0x21d: Callback vtable pointer\n    +0x356: Character slot state byte\n    +0x359: Connection info offset\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early with 1 if InitStringTables fails\n  - Jumps to cleanup (state=4) if vtable[0x74] returns 0\n  - MCP restore failure logs error but continues to cleanup\n\nOrdinal References:\n  Ordinal_10048, 10049 - D2Win UI initialization\n  Ordinal_10052 - Check pending operations\n  Ordinal_10053 - Set UI mode (param=0)\n  Ordinal_10054 - Finalize pending operations\n  Ordinal_10034 - Play background music\n  Ordinal_10001 - Final cleanup if not state 4\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x21d - Offset to callback vtable in game list data\n  0x1ea - Offset to flags word in game list data\n  0x356 - Offset to character slot state byte\n  0x359 - Offset to connection info in game list data\n  0x30  - Stride between UI object descriptors (48 bytes)\n  0x3c  - Stride between game slot buttons (60 pixels Y)\n  0x100 - Channel name buffer size (256 bytes)\n  0x200 - Unicode array element count (512)\n  0x204 - Offset to next pointer in MOTD linked list node",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:80f19d26851956fb873954fe406a8f77",
