      "name": "InitializePanelDisplayText",
      "signature": "void InitializePanelDisplayText(char * lpszDisplayText, int nTextMode, int nPanelType)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes panel display text and sets display mode flags based on text mode and panel type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwInventoryExtraState is non-zero (panel system active)\n2. If inactive, return immediately (early exit)\n3. Copy display text string to global buffer g_szPanelDisplayText\n4. Calculate display flags based on nTextMode and nPanelType:\n   - nPanelType=0, nTextMode=0: flags = 0x09\n   - nPanelType=0, nTextMode!=0: flags = 0x00\n   - nPanelType!=0, nTextMode=0: flags = 0x1b (27)\n   - nPanelType!=0, nTextMode!=0: flags = 0x23 (35)\n5. Store flags to g_byPanelDisplayFlags and g_byPanelDisplayMode\n6. Reset panel state values (g_dwPanelStateA, g_dwPanelStateB = -1)\n7. Call Ordinal_10059 with nPanelType parameter\n8. Set display timeout to GetTickCount() + 1000ms\n\nParameters:\n  lpszDisplayText (ECX) - char* - Text string to display on panel\n  nTextMode (EDX) - int - Text display mode (0=standard, non-zero=alternate)\n  nPanelType (Stack+4) - int - Panel type (0=simple panel, non-zero=extended panel)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns immediately if g_dwInventoryExtraState == 0 (panel system inactive)\n  - Flag calculation uses NEG/SBB/AND pattern for branchless conditional assignment\n\nCaller Context:\n  - Called from FUN_6fa118b0 after selecting panel display functions based on DAT_6fa3e9f0/DAT_6fa3e9f4 flags",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
