      "name": "InitializeCharacterClassSelectionPanel",
      "signature": "void InitializeCharacterClassSelectionPanel(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the character class selection panel UI for Diablo II.\n\nCreates and configures button controls for each character class (Amazon, Sorceress,\nNecromancer, Paladin, Barbarian, and conditionally Druid/Assassin for expansion).\nAlso sets up game mode indicator text boxes (Hardcore, Expansion, Ladder, Classic).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 7 Unicode string buffers for class abbreviations\n2. Convert ANSI class codes (AMA, SOR, NEC, PAL, BAR, DRU, ASN) to Unicode\n3. Create class selection buttons (descriptors 0x6B-0x72):\n   - Slot 1 (0x6B): First class button, frame value 1 (selected)\n   - Slots 2-6 (0x6C-0x70): Class buttons, frame value 0 (unselected)\n   - Slots 7-8 (0x71-0x72): Druid/Assassin (expansion only)\n4. Create corresponding text labels (descriptors 0x73-0x7A)\n5. Add sub-child objects for game mode labels with bounds checking (max 32)\n6. Create character info text field (descriptor 0x69) with column formatting\n7. Configure stat display columns via Ordinal_10059 calls\n8. Call FUN_6fa09350 for additional panel setup\n9. Create selection timer (descriptor 0x7D) and set handler\n10. Clear panel display text global\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Druid/Assassin buttons only created if g_dwPanelResetFlag != 0 (expansion mode)\n- Asserts if g_nNumSubChildren >= 32 (0x20) before adding child objects\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6B-0x72: Character class button descriptor indices\n- 0x73-0x7A: Character class label descriptor indices\n- 0x67: Character info label descriptor\n- 0x69: Character stats text field descriptor\n- 0x7D: Selection timer descriptor\n- 0x14CE: String ID for first class label\n- 0x14C8-0x14CC: String IDs for game mode labels (Hardcore/Expansion/Ladder/Classic)\n- 0xFD9: String ID for character info label\n- 0x10: Unicode buffer size (16 wide chars)\n- 0x1086: Assert line number for max children check\n\nOrdinal Functions:\n- Ordinal_10056: D2Win.SetTextColor - Sets text rendering color\n- Ordinal_10059: D2Win.AddStatValue - Adds stat value to display column",
