      "name": "ResetInventoryPanelAndShowSelection",
      "signature": "int ResetInventoryPanelAndShowSelection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Resets inventory panel state and displays character selection or special mode UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fa10090 and FUN_6fa0f490 for pre-reset cleanup\n2. Dispatch inventory item handlers for slots 1-8 to reset each slot\n3. Restore current input item and pointer from globals\n4. Loop through sub-children array (up to g_nNumSubChildren) dispatching handlers\n5. Clear sub-children count and inventory sub-state\n6. Call FUN_6fa117b0 for additional cleanup\n7. Clear inventory extra state, dispatch handlers for slots 9-10\n8. If special mode flag is 1, call FUN_6fa127f0\n9. Reset panel mode to 0 if it was 3\n10. Set bit mask on panel state if valid pointer exists\n11. Clear panel reset flag and panel state slots 1-8\n12. Set command buffer end to 1000 (0x3E8)\n13. Branch A - Special Mode Path:\n    - If game list data offset 0x225 non-zero AND Ordinal_10002 returns 0:\n    - Validate string ID 0x1413, reset panel state\n    - Clear bit mask, set button frame values to 0\n    - Create text box object, add text, set display flags to 9\n    - Return 1\n14. Branch B - Normal Path:\n    - Assert sub-children count less than 32 (0x20)\n    - Create first text box object from g_TextBoxObjectType1\n    - Add to sub-children array, increment count\n    - Assert count still less than 32\n    - Create second text box object from g_TextBoxObjectType2\n    - Add to array, increment count\n    - Validate string ID 0x14C5, add text to second object\n    - Initialize character class selection panel\n    - Set scroll offset to -2, display mode to 0x23, decrement to 0x10\n    - Set timer value to 1000, call Ordinal_10012\n    - Set state A to 0, display flags to 9\n    - Return 1\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns 1 on success\n- Does not return: On assertion failure (sub-children >= 32)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure triggers FogAssert and FUN_6fa12bdd(-1) which does not return\n- Special mode path taken when game list data offset 0x225 is non-zero AND Ordinal_10002 returns 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1413: String ID for special mode display text\n- 0x14C5: String ID for character selection panel text\n- 0x225: Offset into game list data structure for mode flag\n- 0x20 (32): Maximum sub-children array capacity\n- 0x3E8 (1000): Timer/command buffer end value\n- 0x23 (35): Panel display mode for character selection\n- 0x10 (16): Panel state decrement value\n- 0xFFFFFFFE (-2): Panel scroll offset initial value\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert called with file/line info if sub-children count exceeds 31\n- FUN_6fa12bdd(-1) terminates execution after assertion",
