      "name": "InitializeClassSelectionTextDefault",
      "signature": "void InitializeClassSelectionTextDefault(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the character class selection text field with default \"-\" placeholder text.\n\nCalled during character class selection panel initialization to set up the text\ndisplay area with a placeholder dash character before any class is selected.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear existing text data from g_dwInventoryExtraState text field\n2. Initialize 2 Unicode string buffers via default constructor loop (4 wide chars total)\n3. Copy ANSI \"-\" string from data section to local buffer via FUN_6fa12b5e\n4. Convert ANSI buffer to Unicode using win2Unicode (2 chars including null)\n5. Add text line to text field with flags=4, unknown=0\n6. Navigate scrollbar to index 0 (top of list)\n7. Set g_nPanelScrollOffset to -2 (0xFFFFFFFE) indicating no selection\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_dwInventoryExtraState - Text field cleared and populated with \"-\"\n  g_nPanelScrollOffset - Set to -2 (no selection state)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6fa1d728 - Address of \"-\" string (szNotificationsEnabled + 0xa0)\n  2 - Loop count for Unicode buffer initialization\n  4 - Text line flags parameter\n  0xFFFFFFFE - Scroll offset value indicating no selection (-2 signed)",
