      "name": "ShowProfileSexSelectionPanel",
      "signature": "bool ShowProfileSexSelectionPanel(char * lpszProfileData, char * lpszField1, char * lpszField2, char * lpszField3, char * lpszField4)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Displays the profile sex/gender selection panel for user input.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store profile dialog context data to globals (_DAT_6fa208e4-f0)\n2. Call vtable function to display \"profile_sex\" panel configuration\n3. Clear dialog cancel flag (g_fDialogCancelRequested = 0)\n4. Validate string ID 0x147B for panel text\n5. Cleanup existing sub-children by dispatching handlers\n6. Reset sub-children array count to 0\n7. Set current input item to BnetUI object #10\n8. Reset inventory sub-state to 0\n9. Assert sub-children count < 32 (max children)\n10. Create button UI element via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n11. Add button to sub-children array, increment count\n12. Configure button with SetLastInventoryItem and SetUnitFlags\n13. Assert sub-children count < 32\n14. Create label UI element\n15. Add label to sub-children array, increment count\n16. Set label flags\n17. Assert sub-children count < 32\n18. Create textbox UI element\n19. Add textbox to sub-children array, increment count\n20. Set textbox flags and add text content\n21. Set sub-panel callback to FUN_6fa0a3e0\n22. Store GetTickCount() in g_dwInventorySubState\n23. Enter message pump loop (CheckProfileDialogInputAndStopLoop)\n24. On exit: cleanup sub-children by dispatching handlers\n25. Reset sub-children count and inventory sub-state\n26. Return TRUE if dialog not cancelled, FALSE otherwise\n\nParameters:\n  lpszProfileData (ECX): Profile data string pointer\n  lpszField1 (EDX): First profile field string\n  lpszField2 (Stack+4): Second profile field string\n  lpszField3 (Stack+8): Third profile field string\n  lpszField4 (Stack+C): Fourth profile field string\n\nReturns:\n  TRUE (1) - User confirmed selection (g_fDialogCancelRequested == 0)\n  FALSE (0) - User cancelled dialog\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if sub-children count >= 32 (calls FogAssert then terminates)\n  - Uses __fastcall: first 2 params in ECX/EDX, rest on stack\n  - Unreachable block at 0x6fa0a36b removed by decompiler\n\nCalled By:\n  FUN_6fa11510 - Profile creation flow\n  FUN_6fa111c0 - Profile edit flow",
