      "name": "SetProfileDialogCancelFlag",
      "signature": "void SetProfileDialogCancelFlag(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Callback to signal profile dialog cancellation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set g_fDialogCancelRequested flag to 1 (TRUE)\n2. Return (RET 4 - __stdcall cleanup)\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler\nCalled by: Assigned to g_pfnSubPanelCallback in ShowProfileSexSelectionPanel\nPurpose: When this callback is invoked, it sets the cancel flag which causes\n         CheckProfileDialogInputAndStopLoop to call StopMessageLoop()\n\nParameters:\n  None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_fDialogCancelRequested (0x6fa20a18) - WRITE - Set to 1 to signal cancellation\n\nNote: Function boundary incomplete in Ghidra - actual code is:\n  MOV EAX, 1\n  MOV [g_fDialogCancelRequested], EAX\n  RET 4",
