      "name": "InvokeProfileSexCallback",
      "signature": "void InvokeProfileSexCallback(void * pContext, char * lpszField1, char * lpszField2, char * lpszField3, char * lpszField4)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Invokes the profile sex/gender callback via vtable dispatch.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Marshals parameters and invokes vtable callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 16-byte local array on stack (SUB ESP, 0x10)\n2. Copy EDX (lpszField1) to array[0]\n3. Copy stack param lpszField2 to array[1]\n4. Copy stack param lpszField3 to array[2]\n5. Copy stack param lpszField4 to array[3]\n6. Load vtable pointer from g_pCallbackVtable\n7. Push pointer to local array as second argument\n8. Push g_ProfileSexPanelConfig as first argument\n9. Set EDX = 4 (parameter count)\n10. Call vtable[0x80] - profile sex callback dispatcher\n11. Cleanup stack and return\n\nParameters:\n  pContext (ECX): Unused callback context (ignored in this function)\n  lpszField1 (EDX): First profile field string, stored in array[0]\n  lpszField2 (Stack+4): Second profile field string, stored in array[1]\n  lpszField3 (Stack+8): Third profile field string, stored in array[2]\n  lpszField4 (Stack+C): Fourth profile field string, stored in array[3]\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses __fastcall with RET 0xC (cleans 12 bytes = 3 stack params)\n  - ECX parameter is unused but required by calling convention\n  - EDX is overwritten with value 4 before callback invocation\n\nCalled By:\n  Address 0x6fa119e2 - Profile handling code\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_pCallbackVtable @ 0x6fa20a1c: Pointer to callback interface vtable\n  g_ProfileSexPanelConfig @ 0x6fa1b030: Profile sex panel configuration struct",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
