      "name": "AddMotdMessageAndUpdateDisplay",
      "signature": "void AddMotdMessageAndUpdateDisplay(void * this, int nMessageId, char * lpszMessageText)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Adds or updates a Message of the Day (MOTD) entry in the sorted linked list and refreshes the display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search g_pMotdMessageList for existing node with matching nMessageId\n2. If found, skip to step 6 to update text\n3. If not found, allocate new 0x208-byte node via FogMemAlloc\n4. Store nMessageId at node+0x200\n5. Insert node into sorted position (ascending by nMessageId):\n   - If list empty or nMessageId < first node's ID, prepend to list\n   - Otherwise, traverse to find correct sorted position and insert\n6. Copy lpszMessageText to node buffer (max 0x200 bytes) with null terminator\n7. Initialize 512-element Unicode array on stack\n8. If g_pInventoryPanelState is NULL, return early\n9. Concatenate all MOTD messages from linked list into szConcatBuffer (max 0x200 bytes):\n   - Traverse linked list appending each message\n   - Calculate strlen via manual loop after each append\n   - Stop if total length exceeds 0x1ff\n10. Set visibility of g_pMotdTextBox (hide if has content, show if empty)\n11. Convert concatenated ANSI string to Unicode via win2Unicode\n12. Display Unicode text in g_pInventoryPanelState text box\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX) - IMPLICIT: Message ID (int cast as void* due to __thiscall)\n  nMessageId - Message ID for sorting (unused due to ECX mapping)\n  lpszMessageText - ANSI message text to store (max 512 chars)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns early if g_pInventoryPanelState is NULL (no UI to update)\n  - Existing entries are updated in place, not duplicated\n  - Messages are sorted by ID in ascending order\n  - Total concatenated length capped at 0x200 bytes\n\nStructure Layout (MOTD Node - 0x208 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type      Description\n  0x000   0x200 szMessage   char[512] ANSI message text\n  0x200   0x4   nMessageId  int       Message sort key\n  0x204   0x4   pNext       char*     Next node pointer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x208 - MOTD node allocation size (512 + 4 + 4)\n  0x200 - Message buffer size and Unicode array count\n  0x1780 - Source file line number for FogMemAlloc debug",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:5b05faab3f01641182dc56aea7582651",
