      "name": "ExtractPrefixBeforeWildcard",
      "signature": "void ExtractPrefixBeforeWildcard(char * lpszSource, char * lpszDestination)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "ExtractPrefixBeforeWildcard - Extract substring from source up to first '*' wildcard character\n\nClassification: Worker function - String manipulation utility for wildcard prefix extraction\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if source string starts with '*' character\n2. If source starts with '*', jump to full string copy (no prefix extraction needed)\n3. Search for '*' character in source string using strchr\n4. If '*' not found, copy entire source to destination using SStrCopy\n5. If '*' found, calculate prefix length (pointer difference)\n6. Copy prefix bytes using optimized DWORD copy (4 bytes at a time via MOVSD.REP)\n7. Copy remaining bytes individually (0-3 bytes via MOVSB.REP)\n8. Null-terminate destination string at prefix length position\n\nParameters:\n  lpszSource (char *) [ECX] - Source ANSI string potentially containing wildcard '*'\n  lpszDestination (char *) [EDX] - Destination buffer for extracted prefix substring\n\nReturns:\n  void - Destination buffer contains extracted prefix or full copy of source\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Source starting with '*': Full string copy (no prefix exists)\n  - No '*' in source: Full string copy\n  - Empty source: Copies empty string\n  - Memory copy optimization: Uses REP MOVSD/MOVSB for efficient byte copying\n\nCaller Context:\n  EditBoxKeyHandler (0x6fa04a50) - Called to extract history text prefix before wildcard\n  for chat autocomplete insertion, splitting history entry from suffix pattern",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:f9c607bf4e28c5f2b566b4fd41d8d871",
