      "name": "HandleGameSlotButtonClick",
      "signature": "dword HandleGameSlotButtonClick(dword * pEventData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Handles click events on game slot buttons in the Battle.net multiplayer game list UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search g_apGameSlotButtons array to find which button triggered the event\n2. Calculate absolute slot index = scroll position + button array index\n3. If button not found in array, return 0 (event not handled)\n4. Branch based on event type (pEventData[1]):\n   - 0x205 (WM_RBUTTONUP): Show user profile panel\n   - Other: Select game slot\n\nRIGHT-CLICK PATH (0x205 - Show Profile):\n5. Traverse game list linked list to find node at slot index\n6. Call FUN_6fa117b0 to clean up any existing profile panel\n7. Extract username from node+0x4, find '*' separator (strchr)\n8. Compare extracted name with current user's name (g_pGameListData+0x88)\n9. If names differ: Call FUN_6fa11510 to show OTHER user's profile (read-only)\n10. If names match: Call FUN_6fa111c0 to show OWN profile (editable)\n\nLEFT-CLICK PATH (Select Slot):\n11. Get current tick count for double-click detection\n12. If clicking already-selected slot (g_nSelectedSlotIndex == index):\n    - Deselect current slot, clear selection bit mask\n    - Reset g_pChatHistoryBuffer and g_nSelectedSlotIndex to null/-1\n    - Update UI button states based on input field and selection\n13. If clicking new slot (index < g_dwAutomapLineCount):\n    - Deselect previous selection if any\n    - Traverse list to target node\n    - Set selection bit mask on target node\n    - Update g_pChatHistoryBuffer, g_nSelectedSlotIndex, g_dwSlotSelectionTickCount\n    - Update all UI button visibility states\n\nParameters:\n  pEventData (dword *) - Event structure pointer:\n    +0x00: Button handle (dword) - matches g_apGameSlotButtons entry\n    +0x04: Event type (dword) - 0x205 = WM_RBUTTONUP (right-click)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Event handled successfully\n  0 - Event not handled (button not found in array)\n\nGame List Node Structure (stride 0xa0 = 160 bytes):\n  +0x04: char[] Username (may contain '*' separator for display name)\n  +0x36: char[] Profile description field\n  +0x88: char[] Current user's display name (in g_pGameListData)\n  +0x8a: ushort Flags - bit 2 (0x04) and bit 5 (0x20) control profile display\n  +0x9c: uint * Unit handle pointer (must not be NULL)\n  +0xa0: Node * pNext - linked list next pointer\n\nUI Object Indices (g_apBnetUIObjects):\n  [0]: Send button - enabled when input has text\n  [1]: Reply button - enabled when chat history selected and input has text  \n  [3]: Squelch button - enabled when selection has no squelch flag\n  [4]: Unsquelch button - enabled when selection has squelch flag\n  [5]: Unknown button - mirrors [0] state\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_pChatHistoryBuffer - Points to selected game list node (or 0)\n  g_nSelectedSlotIndex - Current slot index (or -1 if none)\n  g_dwSlotSelectionTickCount - Tick count when slot was selected\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x205 - WM_RBUTTONUP message (right mouse button up)\n  0x2a - ASCII '*' character for strchr search\n  0xa0 - Game list node stride (160 bytes)\n  0x88 - Offset to username in g_pGameListData\n  0x9c - Offset to unit handle pointer in node\n  0x8a - Offset to flags word in node\n\nError Handling:\n  Asserts if unit handle (node+0x9c) is NULL when accessing selection",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:36648155077b2fa0240e6701e322d5bb",
