      "name": "SubmitChatEditBoxInput",
      "signature": "int SubmitChatEditBoxInput(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Submits the current chat edit box input for processing.\n\nCLASSIFICATION: Callback/Handler - UI callback invoked when user submits chat input\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. Get Unicode text from current input edit box via D2Win_GetEditBoxChild\n2. If edit box child is NULL, return success (1)\n3. Get length of Unicode text via Unicode::strlen\n4. If text is empty (length 0), return success (1)\n5. Convert Unicode text to ANSI (Windows code page) via Unicode::unicode2Win\n   - Destination buffer: 256 bytes on stack\n   - Max conversion size: 0x100 (256) characters\n6. Call ProcessChatCommandAndUIMessage with converted ANSI text and nWhisperMode=0\n7. Return result from ProcessChatCommandAndUIMessage\n\nPARAMETERS:\n  None (parameterless callback)\n\nRETURNS:\n  int - Always 1 on empty/null input; otherwise result from ProcessChatCommandAndUIMessage\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n  - Empty input text silently returns 1 (success)\n  - NULL edit box child returns 1 (success)\n  - Conversion uses fixed 256-byte buffer (max input length limitation)\n\nGLOBALS ACCESSED:\n  g_pCurrentInputPointer (0x6fa218d0) - Current input edit box control pointer\n\nCROSS-REFERENCES:\n  - Referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fa1b170\n  - Called by UI system as submit callback for chat input\n\nSTACK FRAME:\n  [ESP+0x4] to [ESP+0x103] - acAnsiBuffer[256]: ANSI conversion buffer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
