      "name": "RemovePlayerFromChannelList",
      "signature": "int RemovePlayerFromChannelList(char * lpszPlayerName)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Removes a player from the Battle.net channel player list.\n\nSearches the linked list starting at g_pGameListHead for a player matching\nthe given name. When found, displays a notification message if enabled,\nunlinks the node from the list, and releases associated resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pPrevNode = NULL, pCurrentNode = g_pGameListHead\n2. Loop through linked list comparing player name at offset +0x04\n3. If match found (strcmp returns 0):\n   a. If notifications enabled (g_fPlayerNotificationsEnabled != 0):\n      - Format \"[name] has left the channel\" message\n      - Convert to Unicode and display in chat text box\n   b. Unlink node: if pPrevNode == NULL, update head; else update prev->next\n   c. If removed node was selected in chat history:\n      - Clear selection (g_pChatHistoryBuffer = 0, g_nSelectedSlotIndex = -1)\n      - Call UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange()\n   d. Release composite unit at node offset +0x9C\n   e. Call ReleasePoolAllocation()\n4. Decrement g_dwAutomapLineCount (player count)\n5. Update game list text with new count\n6. Adjust scroll position:\n   a. If count < 12, reset scroll to 0\n   b. Otherwise clamp scroll to valid range [0, count - 11]\n7. Update scroll arrow UI elements based on scroll position\n8. Call RenderBnetListVisibleItems() to refresh display\n9. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  lpszPlayerName - Pointer to null-terminated player name string to remove\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success\n\nStructure Layout (Player Node at iVar9):\n  Offset | Size | Field              | Type    | Description\n  -------+------+--------------------+---------+---------------------------\n  +0x00  | 4    | dwNodeType         | uint    | Node type or flags\n  +0x04  | 50   | szPlayerName       | char[]  | Player name string\n  +0x36  | ?    | szDisplayName      | char *  | Display name pointer\n  +0x9C  | 4    | pCompositeUnit     | void *  | Associated unit pointer\n  +0xA0  | 4    | pNextNode          | Node *  | Next node in linked list\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0C (12) - Visible row count threshold for scroll handling\n  0x0B (11) - Visible rows minus one (count - 11 = max scroll)\n  0x05      - Text color/style for chat notification\n  0x240 (576) - Unicode buffer size in characters\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_pGameListHead           - Head of player linked list\n  g_fPlayerNotificationsEnabled - Enable/disable leave notifications\n  g_pChatHistoryBuffer      - Currently selected chat entry\n  g_nSelectedSlotIndex      - Selected slot index (-1 = none)\n  g_dwAutomapLineCount      - Total player count in list\n  g_dwAutomapScrollPosition - Current scroll position\n  g_apBnetUIObjects[]       - Array of UI element pointers (indices 0xB-0xE)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:ce68e09dd2275d10e5eaa3feb2e63d18",
