      "name": "ParseChatPlayerNameAndTitle",
      "signature": "void ParseChatPlayerNameAndTitle(char * lpszInputName, char * lpszTitleOut, char * lpszNameOut)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Parses a chat player name string to extract the display name and character title.\n\nCLASSIFICATION: Worker function - called by DisplayFormattedChatPlayerName\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. Initialize output buffers (pszNameOut and pszTitleOut) to empty strings\n2. If input starts with '*' (system message), copy entire input to name output and return\n3. Search for '@' and '*' characters in input to detect email-style or prefixed names\n4. If '@' found before '*', copy input up to '*' as name (handles \"user@realm*channel\" format)\n5. Walk g_pChannelListHead linked list, comparing each entry name against input\n6. On channel match, check g_pGameListHead for matching game entry\n7. If game entry found:\n   a. Get unit ID from game entry offset +0x9c\n   b. Check character flags against gdwBitMasks (offsets +0x18, +0x1c) for title eligibility\n   c. If eligible, compute title index from flag bits:\n      - Bit 5 (0x20): hardcore multiplier (*3)\n      - Bit 7 (0x80): expansion multiplier (*2)  \n      - Bit 6 (0x40): ladder bonus (+1)\n      - Bit 12 (0x1000): female character flag\n   d. Call GetCharacterTitleString with class, title index, and female flag\n   e. Copy title string to pszTitleOut\n8. Copy matched channel name (offset +0x32) to pszNameOut\n9. If no channel match but '*' found in input, extract name portion before '*'\n10. Otherwise copy entire input to name output\n\nPARAMETERS:\n  pszInputName (ECX) - Input player name string, may contain '@', '*' delimiters\n  pszTitleOut (EDX) - Output buffer for character title (e.g., \"Matriarch\")\n  pszNameOut (Stack+0x4) - Output buffer for display name\n\nRETURNS:\n  void - Results returned via output buffer parameters\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n  - Input starting with '*': System message, copied verbatim\n  - \"name@realm*channel\" format: Extracts \"name@realm\" as display name\n  - No channel/game match: Falls back to input string processing\n\nSTRUCTURE OFFSETS:\n  Channel Entry (g_pChannelListHead):\n    +0x00: Channel name for comparison (via FUN_6fa13750)\n    +0x32: Display name string (50 bytes into structure)\n    +0x44: Next pointer in linked list\n  \n  Game Entry (g_pGameListHead):\n    +0x04: Player name string\n    +0x86: Character class byte\n    +0x9c: Pointer to unit for GetUnitIdFromPointer\n    +0xa0: Next pointer in linked list\n\nMAGIC NUMBERS:\n  0x2a - ASCII '*' character\n  0x40 - ASCII '@' character\n  0x7fffffff - Max string copy length (SStrCopy)\n  0x32 - Offset to display name in channel entry (50 decimal)\n  0x44 - Offset to next pointer in channel entry (68 decimal)\n  0x86 - Offset to character class in game entry (134 decimal)\n  0x9c - Offset to unit pointer in game entry (156 decimal)\n  0xa0 - Offset to next pointer in game entry (160 decimal)\n\nFLAG BITS (from GetUnitIdFromPointer result):\n  Bit 5 (0x20): Hardcore mode\n  Bit 6 (0x40): Ladder character\n  Bit 7 (0x80): Expansion character\n  Bit 12 (0x1000): Female character\n\nGLOBALS ACCESSED:\n  g_pChannelListHead (0x6fa21a94) - Head of channel entry linked list\n  g_pGameListHead (0x6fa21a90) - Head of game entry linked list\n  gdwBitMasks_exref (0x6fa1922c) - Pointer to character flag bitmasks",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:7467c7aa83e4655420f464e51620fa50",
