      "name": "FormatIncomingWhisperWithTitle",
      "signature": "int FormatIncomingWhisperWithTitle(char * lpszRawWhisperMessage)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Formats an incoming whisper message with optional player title for display.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Called from whisper message handling table at 0x6fa1d7c4\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse raw whisper message to extract player name and title using ParseChatPlayerNameAndTitle\n2. Check if title (acStack_974) is empty by measuring string length\n3. If title is empty:\n   a. Check if player name (acStack_774) is also empty\n   b. If player name is empty, format message using szFmtNameWithTitleConcat template\n   c. If player name exists, copy title to acStack_874 buffer\n   d. Format output using \"You whisper to %s: %s\" template\n4. If title exists:\n   a. Look for '*' character in message (strchr with 0x2a)\n   b. Format output using \"You whisper to %s: %s\" template\n5. Initialize Unicode buffer (aUStack_674) with 0x240 (576) wide characters\n6. Convert formatted ANSI string to Unicode using Unicode::win2Unicode\n7. Validate Unicode string length does not exceed 499 characters\n   - If exceeded, trigger FogAssert with szAssertUnicodeStrlenLimit\n8. Retrieve string ID 0xf9a using ValidateStringId\n9. Search for and remove placeholder substrings using Unicode::strstr/memmove loop\n10. Add formatted text to chat display via CharSelectTextBoxAddText with color 2\n\nParameters:\n  lpszRawWhisperMessage (char *): Raw incoming whisper message containing player name, title, and text\n\nReturns:\n  int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nStack Frame (0x974 bytes):\n  -0x974 to -0x874: acStack_974 [256] - Extracted player title\n  -0x874 to -0x774: acStack_874 [256] - Formatted name with title\n  -0x774 to -0x674: acStack_774 [256] - Extracted player name\n  -0x674 to -0x1F4: aUStack_674 [1152 bytes / 576 wchar_t] - Unicode output buffer\n  -0x1F4 to -0x000: acStack_1f4 [500] - Formatted ANSI message buffer\n\nString References:\n  s__s____s__whispers___s_You_whispe_6fa1daac + 0x18 = \"You whisper to %s: %s\" at 0x6fa1dac4\n  szFmtNameWithTitleConcat - Format string for name with title concatenation\n\nCross-References:\n  From: 0x6fa1d7c4 (DATA) - Function pointer table entry\n\nCallees:\n  ParseChatPlayerNameAndTitle - Extract name/title from raw message\n  FormatStringToBuffer - sprintf-like formatting\n  Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ - Initialize Unicode character\n  Unicode::win2Unicode - Convert ANSI to Unicode\n  Unicode::strlen - Get Unicode string length  \n  Unicode::strstr - Find substring in Unicode string\n  Unicode_memmove - Move memory in Unicode strings\n  ValidateStringId - Retrieve localized string by ID\n  CharSelectTextBoxAddText - Add text to chat display\n  FogAssert - Debug assertion handler\n  FUN_6fa12bdd - Exit handler (called on assert failure)\n\nNote: Function boundaries appear corrupted in Ghidra (shows 1-byte body).\nActual code spans approximately 0x6fa0e150 to 0x6fa0e40d (RETN 8).",
