      "name": "ReturnFalseStdcall2Params",
      "signature": "int ReturnFalseStdcall2Params(void * pUnused1, void * pUnused2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Stub callback function that always returns FALSE (0).\n\nClassification: Stub/Placeholder callback - used in multiplayer dispatch table\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear EAX register (XOR EAX, EAX) - sets return value to 0\n2. Return to caller with stack cleanup (RET 8)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnused1 (void *): IMPLICIT, first parameter - completely unused\n- pUnused2 (void *): IMPLICIT, second parameter - completely unused\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 0 (FALSE/failure)\n\nNotes:\n- __stdcall convention with 2 parameters (RET 8 = 2 parameters * 4 bytes)\n- Referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fa1d7bc (6 xrefs)\n- Used as placeholder/no-op callback in multiplayer message dispatch\n- Parameters typed as void* because they are completely unused\n- Function body is 5 bytes: 33 C0 C2 08 00 (XOR EAX,EAX + RET 8)\n\nCross-References:\n- Data xref from 0x6fa1d7bc (dispatch table entry)\n- Data xref from 0x6fa1d7c8\n- Data xref from 0x6fa1d7cc\n- Data xref from 0x6fa1d7dc\n- Data xref from 0x6fa1d7e0\n- Data xref from 0x6fa1d7ec",
