      "name": "PopulateGameListDetails",
      "signature": "void PopulateGameListDetails(GameListEntry * pGameInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Populates the game list secondary control with detailed game information.\n\nDisplays game name, elapsed time, level restrictions, max players, and\ncharacter roster with class names for a selected multiplayer game entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pGameListSecondaryControl exists, return if null\n2. Clear existing text data from the control\n3. Check game name at offset +0x2C for non-empty string\n4. If game name exists, add game name and newline to control\n5. Calculate elapsed time from seconds at offset +0x0C:\n   - Hours = seconds / 3600\n   - Minutes = (seconds % 3600) / 60\n   - Seconds = seconds % 60\n6. Format and display \"Elapsed Time: H:MM:SS\"\n7. Check level restriction byte at offset +0x11 (max level diff)\n   - If 0: Display single level from offset +0x10\n   - If 1-99: Display level range \"Level X to Y\"\n   - If >= 100: Skip level display\n8. Check max players byte at offset +0x12\n   - If 1-7: Display \"Up to N Players\"\n9. Add newline separator\n10. Loop through player roster (count at offset +0x14):\n    - Character names at offset +0x8C (16-byte stride)\n    - Character class at offset +0x4C (2-byte stride)\n    - Character level at offset +0x6C (2-byte stride)\n    - Format class-specific string based on class ID (0-6)\n    - Display using StringAsciiToUnicode with style 5\n11. Reset scrollbar to top position\n\nParameters:\n  pGameInfo (ECX) - Pointer to GameListEntry structure containing:\n    +0x0C: dwElapsedSeconds - Elapsed time in seconds\n    +0x10: byMinLevel - Minimum character level\n    +0x11: byMaxLevelDiff - Maximum level difference (0=single, 1-99=range)\n    +0x12: byMaxPlayers - Maximum players (1-7)\n    +0x14: dwPlayerCount - Player count in game\n    +0x2C: szGameName[32] - Game name string\n    +0x4C: awCharClass[8] - Character class IDs (0-6)\n    +0x6C: awCharLevel[8] - Character levels\n    +0x8C: aszCharName[8][16] - Character names (16 bytes each)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty game name (length 0): Skips game name display\n  - Level diff >= 100: Skips level restriction display\n  - Max players 0 or >= 8: Skips player count display\n  - Empty character name: Skips that player entry\n\nCharacter Class IDs:\n  0 = Amazon, 1 = Sorceress, 2 = Necromancer, 3 = Paladin\n  4 = Barbarian, 5 = Druid, 6 = Assassin",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
