      "name": "NormalizeBnetMaxPlayersInput",
      "signature": "int NormalizeBnetMaxPlayersInput(int nUnknownParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Normalizes max players input from Battle.net game creation edit box.\n\nCallback function that reads user-entered text, parses it as an integer,\nthen reformats and writes it back to ensure clean numeric display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get Unicode text from max players edit box (g_pBnetMaxPlayersLabel)\n2. Convert Unicode to UTF-8 into local buffer (max 5 chars)\n3. Parse ASCII string to integer using string-to-int helper\n4. Format integer back to string using \"%d\" format\n5. Convert formatted string to Unicode and set edit box text\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  nUnknownParam - Stack parameter, purpose unclear (may be event type or ignored)\n  IMPLICIT pThis (ECX) - Not meaningfully used in this function\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_pBnetMaxPlayersLabel [0x6fa3e938] - Pointer to max players label/edit box control\n  g_szFormatBuffer [0x6fa1daec] - Temporary buffer for formatted string output\n  szFmtNumber [0x6fa1d938] - \"%d\" format string for integer formatting\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function body shows single instruction due to Ghidra analysis issue\n  - Decompiler correctly shows full function logic\n  - Input text limited to 5 characters for buffer safety\n\nCalled Functions:\n  D2Win_GetEditBoxChild - Gets Unicode child text from edit box\n  Unicode::toUtf - Converts Unicode to UTF-8\n  FUN_6fa138ab - Thunk to string-to-int converter (atoi-like)\n  FormatStringToBuffer - sprintf-like formatting to buffer\n  ConvertCharToUnicodeAndSetEditData - Sets edit box with converted text",
