      "name": "IncrementMaxPlayersInput",
      "signature": "int IncrementMaxPlayersInput(int nEventParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Increments the max players value in the TCP/IP game creation input field.\n\nCallback handler for the increment button on the max players edit box.\nReads current value, increments if below maximum (99), and updates display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get Unicode text from g_pMaxPlayersInputField edit box control\n2. Convert Unicode to UTF-8 into 8-byte local buffer (max 5 chars)\n3. Parse ASCII string to integer via FUN_6fa138ab (atoi-like)\n4. Compare parsed value against 99 (0x63) maximum\n5. If value < 99, increment by 1; otherwise keep at 99\n6. Format integer back to string using \"%d\" format\n7. Convert formatted string to Unicode and update edit box\n8. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  nEventParam - Stack parameter from UI callback system (typically event type, ignored here)\n  IMPLICIT ECX - this pointer, passed to FUN_6fa138ab but may be unused\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_pMaxPlayersInputField [0x6fa3e93c] - Pointer to max players edit box control\n  DAT_6fa1dae8 - Temporary buffer for formatted string output\n  szFmtNumber [0x6fa1d938] - \"%d\" format string\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function body shows single MOV instruction due to Ghidra analysis boundary issue\n  - Actual code spans 0x6fa103e0 to ~0x6fa10428 (RET 4 at 0x6fa10425)\n  - Maximum player count capped at 99 (CMP EAX, 0x63; JGE skip_inc)\n  - Input limited to 5 characters for buffer safety\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - FUN_6fa10440: DecrementMaxPlayersInput (same pattern, decrements with floor at 0)\n  - IncrementBnetMaxPlayers: Similar for Battle.net label field\n  - NormalizeBnetMaxPlayersInput: Normalizes without increment/decrement",
