      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Callback handler that checks vtable method and conditionally stops message loop.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - invoked from MessagePumpLoop during UI event processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pCallbackVtable global pointer\n2. Call vtable method at offset 0x98 with nParam argument\n3. If method returns non-zero, call StopMessageLoop()\n4. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\n  nParam (stack+4) - Parameter passed through to vtable[0x98] method\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1\n\nCallers:\n  - Referenced as callback from EnterBattleNetMultiplayerUI via MessagePumpLoop\n\nVtable Method:\n  g_pCallbackVtable + 0x98: Unknown callback method, return non-zero signals stop\n\nNote: Function body truncated in Ghidra analysis - actual bytes span 0x6fa10710-0x6fa10729.\nCalling convention is __stdcall (RET 4 cleanup).",
