      "name": "CheckMcpClientStatusAndStopIfError",
      "signature": "int CheckMcpClientStatusAndStopIfError(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Checks MCP client connection status and stops message loop if any error detected.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fa10af4.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call Ordinal_10003 (D2MCPCLIENT) - Initialization/preparation call, result ignored\n2. Call Ordinal_10052 (D2MCPCLIENT) - Check status, non-zero indicates error\n3. If step 2 returned 0, call Ordinal_10017 (D2MCPCLIENT) - Secondary status check\n4. If step 3 returned 0, call Ordinal_10046 (D2MCPCLIENT) - Tertiary status check\n5. If all status checks returned 0 AND g_fMcpErrorState is 0, return 1 (success)\n6. Otherwise, call StopMessageLoop() to halt UI event processing\n7. Always return 1 regardless of path taken\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Short-circuit evaluation: Status checks stop at first non-zero result\n- Message loop stops on ANY error condition (status check failure OR global flag set)\n- Function always returns success even when stopping message loop\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n- g_fMcpErrorState (0x6fa3e9d0): Error state flag, non-zero triggers message loop stop\n\nOrdinal Function Reference (D2MCPCLIENT.DLL):\n- Ordinal_10003: MCP client preparation/init call\n- Ordinal_10052: Primary MCP status check (0 = OK)\n- Ordinal_10017: Secondary MCP status check (0 = OK)\n- Ordinal_10046: Tertiary MCP status check (0 = OK)",
