      "signature": "void GetProfileCharacterName(char * lpszDestBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Copies the current profile character name to the specified destination buffer.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - wraps SStrCopy for g_szProfileCharacterName access.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push max length parameter (0x7FFFFFFF) onto stack\n2. Push source address (g_szProfileCharacterName) onto stack\n3. Push destination buffer (lpszDestBuffer from ECX) onto stack\n4. Call SStrCopy to perform the string copy\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- lpszDestBuffer (ECX, char *): Destination buffer to receive the character name string.\n  Caller must ensure buffer is large enough to hold the character name.\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value. String copied to lpszDestBuffer on success.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_szProfileCharacterName is empty/NULL, destination receives empty string\n- Maximum copy length is 0x7FFFFFFF (effectively unlimited - 2GB)\n- No bounds checking on destination buffer size\n\nRelated Globals:\n- g_szProfileCharacterName (0x6FA3E9E0): Global string buffer storing current profile\n  character name. Populated by InitializeProfileEditPanel or InitializeProfileCreationPanel.",
