      "name": "FormatStringToBuffer",
      "signature": "int FormatStringToBuffer(char * szOutputBuffer, byte * pbFormatString, ...)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Formats a string using printf-style format specifiers into an output buffer.\nThis is a wrapper around the internal format processing function (FUN_6fa13b77)\nthat initializes a format context structure and handles output termination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize format context on stack with output buffer pointer\n2. Set dwFormatFlags to 0x42 (default format state: 'B' character code)\n3. Set nRemainingChars to INT_MAX (0x7FFFFFFF) for unlimited buffer\n4. Call FUN_6fa13b77 to process format string with variadic arguments\n5. Decrement remaining character count (tracks overflow)\n6. If overflow occurred (nRemainingChars < 0), call FUN_6fa13a5f error handler\n7. Else null-terminate output buffer at current position\n8. Return number of characters written (excluding null terminator)\n\nParameters:\n- szOutputBuffer: Destination buffer for formatted output string (char *)\n- pbFormatString: Printf-style format string, ANSI (byte *)\n- ...: Variadic arguments matching format specifiers\n\nReturns:\n- Number of characters written to buffer (excluding null terminator)\n- Return value from format processor; negative indicates error\n\nFormat Context Structure (stack layout):\nOffset  Size  Field            Description\n-0x20   4     szCurrentPos     Current write position in buffer\n-0x1C   4     nRemainingChars  Characters remaining before overflow\n-0x18   4     szOutputStart    Original buffer start address\n-0x14   4     dwFormatFlags    Format processing state flags\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x42: Default format flags ('B' = 66 decimal, initial state)\n- 0x7FFFFFFF: INT_MAX, unlimited buffer capacity marker\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fa13b77: Core format string processor (handles %d, %s, %x, etc.)\n- FUN_6fa13a5f: Buffer overflow error handler\n\nCallers: UI formatting functions (chat, game lists, panel initialization)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:679e7391cc431bfbfb578a6a70c8d79c",
