      "comment": "CRT global initializer dispatcher - invokes C and C++ static constructors.\n\nClassification: Initialization function - part of CRT startup sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load optional pre-init callback pointer (g_pfnCrtPreInitCallback)\n2. If pre-init callback is non-NULL, invoke it\n3. Invoke C initializers: iterate g_apfnCInitStart to g_apfnCInitEnd array\n4. Invoke C++ initializers: iterate g_apfnCppInitStart to g_apfnCppInitEnd array\n5. Return to CRT startup\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nCaller Context:\n- Called from DLL entry point initialization (FUN_6fa138b6) during DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH\n- Executes after version detection, heap initialization, command line setup\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n- g_pfnCrtPreInitCallback (0x6fa40104): Optional pre-init callback, usually NULL\n- g_apfnCInitStart (0x6fa1b008): Start of C initializer function pointer array\n- g_apfnCInitEnd (0x6fa1b014): End marker for C initializer array\n- g_apfnCppInitStart (0x6fa1b000): Start of C++ constructor pointer array  \n- g_apfnCppInitEnd (0x6fa1b004): End marker for C++ constructor array\n\nMemory Layout:\nC++ init section:   0x6fa1b000 - 0x6fa1b004 (1 slot, terminators only)\nC init section:     0x6fa1b008 - 0x6fa1b014 (3 slots with function pointers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Pre-init callback is typically NULL (used for special CRT configurations)\n- Initializer arrays may contain NULL entries which are skipped\n- Order matters: C initializers run before C++ constructors",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:91b5192dddb89e963abc2be4471149da",
