      "name": "ExitWithErrorCode",
      "signature": "void ExitWithErrorCode(UINT dwExitCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Terminates the process with the specified exit code.\n\nWrapper function that calls the internal exit handler (FUN_6fa12c0e) with simplified parameters.\nPasses 0 for both param_2 (skip cleanup flag) and param_3 (thread exit flag), ensuring full\nprocess termination with cleanup routines executed.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push 0 for param_3 (fThreadExit = FALSE, triggers ExitProcess not thread exit)\n2. Push 0 for param_2 (fSkipCleanup = FALSE, executes atexit handlers)\n3. Push dwExitCode from caller's stack\n4. Call internal exit handler FUN_6fa12c0e\n5. Clean up stack and return (though callee typically does not return)\n\nParameters:\n  dwExitCode (uint) - Process exit code passed to ExitProcess/TerminateProcess\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return under normal circumstances\n\nCalled By:\n  90+ call sites across UI initialization, error handling, and cleanup functions including:\n  InitializeInventorySubPanel, EnterBattleNetMultiplayerUI, RestoreMcpConnectionState,\n  CreateBnetUIObjectByDescriptorIndex, ProcessGameJoinRequest, and many others.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - When internal flag DAT_6fa3ea40 == 1, uses TerminateProcess for immediate exit\n  - Otherwise executes registered atexit callbacks before ExitProcess",
