      "name": "CrtInitiateCleanupNoExit",
      "signature": "void CrtInitiateCleanupNoExit(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "CRT cleanup wrapper that initiates process termination without calling ExitProcess.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CrtDoExit with exitCode=0, bSkipAtexitCallbacks=0, bDoNotExit=1\n2. Return to caller (process continues running after cleanup)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- bDoNotExit=1 means cleanup runs but ExitProcess is NOT called\n- Called during DLL_PROCESS_DETACH during normal shutdown\n- Allows DLL cleanup to complete before process termination\n\nCalled By:\n- DLL entry point handler during DLL_PROCESS_DETACH\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fa12c0e (CrtDoExit) - Main CRT exit handler with full parameter control",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
