      "name": "CrtExitCleanup",
      "signature": "void CrtExitCleanup(UINT dwExitCode, int nSkipDestructors, int nReturnFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT Exit Cleanup - Performs C runtime cleanup and process termination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire CRT exit lock via CrtAcquireExitLock (FUN_6fa12cb3)\n2. If g_dwCrtExitState == 1 (recursive exit), terminate process immediately\n3. Set g_dwCrtCleanupStarted = 1 to mark cleanup in progress\n4. Store return flag in g_byCrtReturnFlag\n5. If nSkipDestructors == 0:\n   a. Iterate atexit callback table in reverse (g_pAtexitTableEnd-4 down to g_pAtexitTableStart)\n   b. Call each non-null callback function pointer\n   c. Invoke pre-terminator array (DAT_6fa1b018 to DAT_6fa1b020)\n6. Invoke C terminator array (DAT_6fa1b024 to DAT_6fa1b028)\n7. If nReturnFlag == 0: Set g_dwCrtExitState = 1, call ExitProcess(dwExitCode) - does not return\n8. Release CRT exit lock via CrtReleaseExitLock (FUN_6fa12cbc) and return\n\nParameters:\n  dwExitCode (UINT) - Process exit code passed to ExitProcess/TerminateProcess\n  nSkipDestructors (int) - If non-zero, skip atexit callbacks and pre-terminators\n  nReturnFlag (int) - If 0, terminate process; if non-zero, return to caller\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function returns only if nReturnFlag != 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Recursive exit detection: If cleanup already started (g_dwCrtExitState==1), \n    calls TerminateProcess immediately to avoid infinite recursion\n  - Thread safety: Uses CRT exit lock around cleanup sequence\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_dwCrtExitState (0x6fa3ea40) - 1 if exit sequence started, prevents recursion\n  g_dwCrtCleanupStarted (0x6fa3ea3c) - 1 when cleanup begins\n  g_byCrtReturnFlag (0x6fa3ea38) - Stores nReturnFlag for later reference\n  g_pAtexitTableStart (0x6fa40100) - Start of atexit callback array\n  g_pAtexitTableEnd (0x6fa400fc) - End of atexit callback array",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:eb17d7abe573793d4b67d9aac794697b",
