      "comment": "Acquires the CRT exit critical section (index 0xd/13).\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - wraps CRT lock function with fixed index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push lock index 0xd (exit critical section) onto stack\n2. Call CRT critical section lock function (FUN_6fa14416)\n3. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Index 0xd corresponds to the CRT exit lock used during process termination\n- Paired with FUN_6fa12cbc (UnlockExitCriticalSection) which calls unlock with same index\n- Called by CRT exit handler to synchronize termination sequence\n\nCRT Lock Index Reference:\n- 0xd (13): Exit critical section - protects process exit/termination code\n- 0x11 (17): Used by critical section allocation itself (recursive guard)\n\nCross-References:\n- Caller: CRT exit handler (performs process termination with TerminateProcess/ExitProcess)\n- Callee: CRT critical section lock function (allocates and enters critical section)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
