      "name": "CrtUnlockExitSection",
      "signature": "void CrtUnlockExitSection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Unlocks the CRT exit critical section (index 0xD/13).\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - wraps CrtLeaveCriticalSection with hardcoded index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push critical section index 0xD (exit section) onto stack\n2. Call CrtLeaveCriticalSection to release the lock\n3. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Called at end of CRT exit sequence in FUN_6fa12c0e after cleanup\n- Index 0xD is specifically used for exit synchronization\n- Paired with CrtLockExitSection (0x6fa12cb3) which acquires the same lock\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CrtLockExitSection (0x6fa12cb3): Acquires exit critical section\n- CrtEnterCriticalSection (0x6fa14416): Generic enter with lazy init\n- CrtLeaveCriticalSection (0x6fa14477): Generic leave\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xD (13): CRT exit critical section index in g_apCrtCriticalSections array",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
