      "name": "__alloca_probe",
      "signature": "void __alloca_probe(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Stack probing function for large stack allocations (MSVC _chkstk/__alloca_probe).\n\nCalled by compiler-generated code when a function needs more than 4KB of stack space.\nProbes each page of the requested stack allocation to ensure the guard page is touched,\nwhich triggers the OS to commit more stack memory if needed.\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT in_EAX - Number of bytes to allocate on the stack (uint)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ECX (clobbered by this function)\n2. Load ECX with address just above current return address\n3. If requested size >= 0x1000 (4KB page size):\n   a. Loop: subtract 0x1000 from ECX, touch memory at [ECX] to probe page\n   b. Subtract 0x1000 from EAX (remaining allocation)\n   c. Continue until remaining < 0x1000\n4. Subtract remaining bytes from ECX\n5. Touch final page at [ECX]\n6. Set ESP = ECX (allocate the stack space)\n7. Restore original ECX from old stack location\n8. Push original return address and return (effectively jumping back to caller)\n\nReturns:\n  ESP adjusted down by requested allocation size\n  EAX preserved as new stack pointer value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If allocation < 4KB, skips the page-probing loop\n- Guard page touch triggers STATUS_STACK_OVERFLOW if stack limit exceeded\n\nDecompiler Variables:\n- unaff_retaddr: Return address from caller (implicit, not a real variable)\n- puVar1: SSA temporary for stack pointer arithmetic during probing\n\nClassification: Compiler Helper / Stack Management",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2a518bd4b0b93e6cf2e2d91eb6ff7bf6",
