      "name": "Unicode_memmove",
      "signature": "pointer Unicode_memmove(byte * pbDest, byte * pbSrc, dword cbCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Copies cbCount bytes from pSrc to pDest with overlap handling (memmove semantics).\n\nClassification: Leaf function (no callees) - core memory utility\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check for overlapping regions: if (pSrc < pDest < pSrc + cbCount)\n2. If overlap detected, copy BACKWARD from end to start to prevent corruption\n3. If no overlap, copy FORWARD from start to end\n4. Align destination pointer to 4-byte boundary by copying leading bytes\n5. Bulk copy aligned DWORDs using REP MOVSD for efficiency (8+ DWORDs)\n6. For fewer than 8 DWORDs, use unrolled copy switch (cases 1-7)\n7. Copy trailing bytes (0-3) via switch case\n\nParameters:\n  pDest - Destination buffer pointer (returned unchanged)\n  pSrc - Source buffer pointer\n  cbCount - Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n  pDest - Original destination pointer (for call chaining)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero-length copy: Returns immediately\n  - Small copies (1-3 bytes): Handled directly without alignment\n  - Non-overlapping regions: Uses forward copy (faster)\n  - Overlapping regions: Uses backward copy to prevent data corruption\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3 - Alignment mask (dest & 3 checks DWORD alignment)\n  0x4 - DWORD size in bytes\n  0x8 - Threshold for REP MOVSD vs unrolled copy\n\nRegister Usage (x86):\n  ESI - Source pointer cursor\n  EDI - Destination pointer cursor\n  ECX - DWORD count / loop counter\n  EDX - Remainder bytes (0-3)\n\nControl Flow:\n  Forward path: 0x6fa12f60-0x6fa130d6 (non-overlap)\n  Backward path: 0x6fa130d8-0x6fa13274 (overlap detected)\n  Jump tables at: 0x6fa13088, 0x6fa13098, 0x6fa1301c, 0x6fa13220, 0x6fa131d0",
