      "name": "TokenizeStringByDelimiters",
      "signature": "char * TokenizeStringByDelimiters(char * lpszString, char * lpszDelimiters)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Tokenizes a string by delimiter characters (strtok-like behavior).\n\nParses a string into tokens separated by any character in the delimiter set.\nUses thread-local storage to maintain state between calls for sequential tokenization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get thread-local CRT data via GetThreadLocalCrtData() for state persistence\n2. Initialize 32-byte delimiter bitmap to zero (REP STOSD clears 8 DWORDs)\n3. Build delimiter set bitmap: for each byte in lpszDelimiters\n   - Array index = byte >> 3 (divide by 8)\n   - Bit position = byte & 7 (modulo 8)\n   - Set corresponding bit in abDelimiterBitmap\n4. If lpszString is NULL, retrieve saved position from TLS+0x18 (continue previous tokenization)\n5. Skip leading delimiters: advance lpszString while current char is in delimiter set\n6. Save token start position to lpszTokenEnd\n7. Scan for token end: find next delimiter or null terminator\n8. If delimiter found, replace with null terminator and advance pointer past it\n9. Save current scan position to TLS+0x18 for next call\n10. Return token start pointer, or NULL if no token found\n\nParameters:\n  lpszString - String to tokenize. Pass NULL to continue tokenizing previous string.\n  lpszDelimiters - Null-terminated string of delimiter characters.\n\nReturns:\n  char * - Pointer to next token, or NULL if no more tokens.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First call: pass string pointer and delimiters\n- Subsequent calls: pass NULL and same delimiters\n- Returns NULL when string exhausted\n- Modifies original string by inserting null terminators\n\nMemory Model:\n- Uses TLS offset +0x18 (pTlsData[6]) to store continuation pointer\n- Delimiter bitmap is stack-local (32 bytes for 256-bit coverage)\n\nDecompiler Discrepancies:\n- Return expression -(uint)(lpszString != lpszTokenEnd) & (uint)lpszString\n  simplifies to: return (lpszString != lpszTokenEnd) ? lpszString : NULL",
