      "name": "ToUpperChar",
      "signature": "uint ToUpperChar(uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a character to uppercase, using locale-aware conversion when available.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if locale code page (g_dwLocaleCodePage) is set\n2. If no locale: Use fast ASCII path\n   a. Check if character is in range 'a'-'z' (0x61-0x7a)\n   b. If yes, subtract 0x20 to convert to uppercase\n   c. Return converted or original character\n3. If locale set: Use thread-safe locale conversion\n   a. Increment lock reference count (g_nLocaleLockRefCount)\n   b. Check if multi-threaded mode (g_fLocaleMultiThreaded)\n   c. If multi-threaded: decrement ref count, enter critical section 0x13\n   d. Call FUN_6fa13388 for locale-aware uppercase conversion\n   e. If multi-threaded: leave critical section\n   f. Otherwise: decrement lock reference count\n4. Return uppercase character\n\nParameters:\n  dwChar - Character code point to convert (uint for extended character support)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Uppercase equivalent of input character, or original if not lowercase\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - ASCII lowercase 'a'-'z' (0x61-0x7a): Fast path converts to 'A'-'Z' (0x41-0x5a)\n  - Non-lowercase characters: Returned unchanged\n  - Extended characters (>0x7F): Handled by locale-aware conversion path\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x60 (96) - One less than 'a' (0x61), lower bound check\n  0x7b (123) - One more than 'z' (0x7a), upper bound check  \n  0x20 (32) - ASCII offset between lowercase and uppercase letters\n  0x13 (19) - Critical section index for locale operations\n\nThread Safety:\n  Uses InterlockedIncrement/Decrement for reference counting and\n  critical section for multi-threaded locale access",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
