      "name": "IntToStringDecimal",
      "signature": "char * IntToStringDecimal(int nValue, char * szBuffer, uint dwRadix)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts signed integer to string representation in specified radix.\n\nWrapper function for IntToStringRadix that detects negative values when using\ndecimal (base 10) conversion. For negative decimal values, sets the negative\nflag so IntToStringRadix prepends a minus sign.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if radix is 10 (decimal) AND value is negative (signed comparison)\n2. If both true: set nIsNegative=1 to signal negative handling\n3. If false: set nIsNegative=0 for unsigned conversion\n4. Call IntToStringRadix(nValue, szBuffer, dwRadix, nIsNegative)\n5. Return pointer to buffer\n\nParameters:\n  nValue   - Signed integer value to convert (treated as signed for decimal)\n  szBuffer - Output buffer for null-terminated string result\n  dwRadix  - Numeric base for conversion (2-36, typically 10 or 16)\n\nReturns:\n  char * - Pointer to szBuffer (allows chaining)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Radix 10 with negative value: Prepends '-' sign via nIsNegative flag\n  - Radix != 10: Value treated as unsigned regardless of sign bit\n  - Radix 16: Produces hex digits 0-9, a-f (lowercase)\n\nCalled By:\n  FinalizeFilteredGameListDisplay - Convert player count to string",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
