      "name": "IntToStringRadix",
      "signature": "void IntToStringRadix(uint dwValue, char * szBuffer, uint dwRadix, int nIsNegative)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts an unsigned integer to a string representation in any radix (base).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nIsNegative is non-zero, write '-' prefix and negate dwValue\n2. Save start position of digit string for later reversal\n3. Loop: Extract least significant digit via modulo dwRadix\n4. Convert digit to character: 0-9 for values 0-9, a-z for values 10-35\n5. Store character and divide dwValue by dwRadix\n6. Repeat until dwValue becomes zero\n7. Null-terminate the string\n8. Reverse the digit portion in-place (digits were produced LSB-first)\n\nParameters:\ndwValue - uint: The unsigned integer value to convert\nszBuffer - char *: Output buffer for resulting string (must be large enough)\ndwRadix - uint: Base for conversion (e.g., 10 for decimal, 16 for hex)\nnIsNegative - int: Non-zero if value should be treated as negative (prepends '-')\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result written to szBuffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\nRadix 16 produces lowercase hex (a-f, not A-F)\nBuffer must accommodate sign + digits + null terminator\nMaximum length for base 2: 33 chars (32 bits + null)\nMaximum length for base 10: 12 chars (sign + 10 digits + null)\n\nCalled By:\nFUN_6fa13454 - Integer to string wrapper that determines sign and calls this",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:c147e94384608ec25ec11bdc009b5d4a",
