      "name": "ToLowerChar",
      "signature": "uint ToLowerChar(uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a character to lowercase, using locale-aware conversion when available.\n\nClassification: Worker function - counterpart to ToUpperChar for case conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if locale code page (g_dwLocaleCodePage) is set to 0 (no locale)\n2. If no locale configured: Use fast ASCII path\n   a. Check if character is in range 'A'-'Z' (0x41-0x5a)\n   b. If uppercase ASCII, add 0x20 to convert to lowercase\n   c. Return converted or original character\n3. If locale configured: Use thread-safe locale conversion\n   a. Increment lock reference count (g_nLocaleLockRefCount) atomically\n   b. Check if multi-threaded mode enabled (g_fLocaleMultiThreaded != 0)\n   c. If multi-threaded: decrement ref count, enter critical section 0x13\n   d. Call ToLowerCharLocale for locale-aware lowercase conversion\n   e. If multi-threaded: leave critical section\n   f. Otherwise: decrement lock reference count\n4. Return lowercase character\n\nParameters:\n  dwChar - Character code point to convert (uint for extended character support)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Lowercase equivalent of input character, or original if not uppercase\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - ASCII uppercase 'A'-'Z' (0x41-0x5a): Fast path converts to 'a'-'z' (0x61-0x7a)\n  - Non-uppercase characters: Returned unchanged\n  - Extended characters (>0x7F): Handled by locale-aware conversion path\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x40 (64) - One less than 'A' (0x41), lower bound check\n  0x5b (91) - One more than 'Z' (0x5a), upper bound check\n  0x20 (32) - ASCII offset between uppercase and lowercase letters\n  0x13 (19) - Critical section index for locale operations\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwLocaleCodePage @ 0x6fa3eacc - Active locale code page (0 = no locale)\n  g_nLocaleLockRefCount @ 0x6fa400e8 - Interlocked reference count for locale lock\n  g_fLocaleMultiThreaded @ 0x6fa400e4 - Multi-threaded locale mode flag\n\nThread Safety:\n  Uses InterlockedIncrement/Decrement for reference counting and\n  critical section 0x13 for multi-threaded locale access.\n\nCross-Reference:\n  Called by ProcessBnetAdvertisementData to normalize file extension characters.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
