      "name": "StrChr_ReturnMatchByteAligned",
      "signature": "char * StrChr_ReturnMatchByteAligned(int nUnused, char * lpszStrPlusOne)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Shared epilogue block for _strchr byte-aligned match return.\n\nClassification: Internal utility / Shared code fragment\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute result pointer as (lpszStrPlusOne - 1) via LEA EAX,[EDX + -0x1]\n2. Restore EBX from stack via POP EBX\n3. Return pointer to matched character via RET\n\nParameters:\nnUnused (ECX) - int - Not used, passed through from _strchr caller\nlpszStrPlusOne (EDX) - char * - String pointer after INC instruction, needs -1 adjustment\n\nReturns:\nchar * - Pointer to the matched character in the source string\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis is a shared return block within the _strchr library function.\nThe main _strchr function at 0x6fa13690 jumps here when a character\nmatch is found during the initial byte-by-byte alignment loop\n(before DWORD-aligned scanning begins).\n\nThe LEA EAX,[EDX + -0x1] compensates for the INC EDX at 0x6fa136aa\nthat advanced the pointer before the character comparison.\n\nCaller:\n_strchr (0x6fa13690) via conditional jump JZ at 0x6fa136ad",
