      "name": "CompareStringsLocaleAware",
      "signature": "int CompareStringsLocaleAware(void * this, byte * pbString1, byte * pbString2)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Case-insensitive string comparison with locale awareness.\n\nCLASSIFICATION: Worker function - called by ParseChatPlayerNameAndTitle\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. Check g_dwLocaleCodePage to determine comparison mode\n2. If code page is 0 (ASCII/no locale):\n   a. Loop through both strings character by character\n   b. If characters match, continue to next pair\n   c. If mismatch, convert both to uppercase using inline ASCII trick:\n      - Subtract 0x41 ('A'), check if < 0x1a (26), add 0x20 if so\n      - This maps 'a'-'z' to 'A'-'Z' without affecting other chars\n   d. Compare uppercase versions; if equal, continue loop\n   e. Return -1 if string1 < string2, +1 if string1 > string2\n3. If code page is non-zero (locale-aware):\n   a. Increment g_nLocaleLockRefCount atomically (LOCK prefix)\n   b. If g_fLocaleMultiThreaded > 0, enter critical section 0x13\n   c. Loop through both strings character by character\n   d. On mismatch, call ToLowerCharLocale for each char\n   e. Compare lowercase versions; if equal, continue loop\n   f. Return -1 if string1 < string2, +1 if string1 > string2\n4. Release lock: decrement ref count or leave critical section\n5. Return 0 if strings are equal (reached null terminator)\n\nPARAMETERS:\n  this (ECX) - Unused locale context (thiscall convention artifact)\n  pbString1 (Stack+0x4) - First null-terminated string to compare\n  pbString2 (Stack+0x8) - Second null-terminated string to compare\n\nRETURNS:\n  int - Comparison result:\n    -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): pbString1 < pbString2\n     0: pbString1 == pbString2 (case-insensitive)\n    +1: pbString1 > pbString2\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n  - Empty strings: Returns 0 immediately (null terminator check)\n  - ASCII path: Uses inline uppercase conversion, no function calls\n  - Locale path: Uses ToLowerCharLocale for proper locale handling\n\nMAGIC NUMBERS:\n  0xBF (-65) - Subtracting 0x41 then checking against 0x1a\n  0x1A (26)  - Number of letters in alphabet\n  0x20 (32)  - ASCII case difference (lowercase = uppercase + 0x20)\n  0x41 (65)  - ASCII 'A' character\n  0x13 (19)  - Critical section index for locale operations\n  0xFF       - Initial loop sentinel / terminator check value\n\nGLOBALS ACCESSED:\n  g_dwLocaleCodePage (0x6fa3eacc) - Current locale code page (0 = ASCII)\n  g_nLocaleLockRefCount (0x6fa400e8) - Locale lock reference count\n  g_fLocaleMultiThreaded (0x6fa400e4) - Multi-threaded locale flag\n\nTHREAD SAFETY:\n  Uses LOCK prefix for atomic increment/decrement of ref count.\n  Enters critical section 0x13 when multi-threaded locale is enabled.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:8c1ef08c13327b78f680f81ff5d26364",
