      "name": "StringToIntLocale",
      "signature": "int StringToIntLocale(byte * lpszInput)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a string to an integer with locale-aware character classification.\nSimilar to atoi() but uses locale-specific whitespace and digit detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace using char type mask 0x08 (CT_SPACE)\n2. Check for optional sign character (0x2d='-' or 0x2b='+')\n3. If sign present, advance to next character\n4. Initialize accumulator to 0\n5. Loop while current character is a digit (mask 0x04 = CT_DIGIT):\n   a. Multiply accumulator by 10\n   b. Add (current char - 0x30) to accumulator\n   c. Advance to next character\n6. If original sign was '-', negate the result\n7. Return accumulated integer value\n\nParameters:\n  lpszInput - Pointer to null-terminated input string\n\nReturns:\n  int - Parsed integer value, or 0 if no digits found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Leading whitespace is skipped per locale settings\n  - Empty string returns 0\n  - String with only whitespace returns 0\n  - No overflow checking is performed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x08 - CT_SPACE mask for whitespace detection in char type table\n  0x04 - CT_DIGIT mask for digit detection\n  0x2d - ASCII minus sign '-'\n  0x2b - ASCII plus sign '+'\n  0x30 - ASCII '0' (subtracted to convert char to digit value)\n\nLocale Handling:\n  If g_nLocaleVersion >= 2, uses GetCharTypeWithMask for extended locale support\n  Otherwise uses direct lookup in g_pCharTypeTable (index = char * 2)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
