      "name": "ParseStringToInt",
      "signature": "int ParseStringToInt(byte * lpszInput)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Thunk wrapper for StringToIntLocale - parses ASCII decimal string to integer.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - simple forwarding to StringToIntLocale.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push lpszInput parameter onto stack\n2. Call StringToIntLocale to parse string\n3. Clean up stack and return integer result in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  lpszInput (byte *) - Null-terminated ASCII string containing decimal number\n                       May have leading whitespace, optional +/- sign\n\nReturns:\n  int - Parsed integer value from string\n        Negative values supported via '-' prefix\n        Returns 0 for empty or non-numeric strings\n\nCallers:\n  ValidateGameCreationFields - parses max players count from UI edit boxes\n\nNotes:\n  - Return value passed through from StringToIntLocale in EAX\n  - Decompiler incorrectly shows __thiscall with void return; actual is __cdecl with int return\n  - Locale-aware: uses g_nLocaleVersion and g_pCharTypeTable for character classification",
