      "name": "CRT_flsbuf",
      "signature": "int CRT_flsbuf(int nChar, int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT _flsbuf - Flush FILE stream buffer and write character\n\nStandard C runtime library function that flushes the internal buffer\nof a FILE stream and writes a single character. Called when the stream\nbuffer is full or needs to be flushed before writing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load stream flags from pStream[3] and file descriptor from pStream[4]\n2. Validate stream state: if not readable/writable (0x82) or error (0x40), set error\n3. If stream in read mode (flag 0x1), reset buffer count and switch to write mode\n4. Clear buffer count, set stream to write mode (flag 0x2)\n5. If no buffer allocated (flag 0x10c not set), allocate buffer via CRT_getbuf\n   - Special case: stdin/stdout check for terminal (CRT_isatty) before alloc\n6. If buffer exists (flag 0x108 set):\n   a. Calculate bytes to flush: current_ptr - base_ptr\n   b. Reset stream to base pointer, set count to buffer_size - 1\n   c. If bytes > 0, write buffer via CRT_write\n   d. Else if file handle valid and seek flag (0x20), reset position via CRT_lseek\n   e. Store new character at base pointer\n7. Else write single character directly via CRT_write\n8. If write succeeded (bytes written == expected), return character\n9. Else set error flag (0x20), return EOF (-1)\n\nParameters:\n- nChar: Character to write (int, low byte used)\n- pStream: Pointer to FILE structure (int *)\n\nReturns:\n- Character written (nChar & 0xFF) on success\n- EOF (-1) on error\n\nFILE Structure Layout (offset from pStream):\nOffset  Size  Field        Description\n0x00    4     ptr          Current buffer position\n0x04    4     cnt          Bytes remaining in buffer\n0x08    4     base         Buffer base address\n0x0C    4     flag         Stream flags\n0x10    4     file         File descriptor/handle\n0x14    4     charbuf      Single char buffer (unbuffered)\n0x18    4     bufsiz       Buffer size\n\nStream Flags:\n0x01 - _IOREAD    Read mode\n0x02 - _IOWRT     Write mode\n0x04 - _IONBF     Unbuffered\n0x08 - _IOMYBUF   Buffer allocated by malloc\n0x10 - _IOEOF     EOF reached\n0x20 - _IOERR     Error occurred\n0x40 - _IOSTRG    String stream (no I/O)\n0x80 - _IORW      Read/write mode\n\nGlobal References:\n- g_stdin (0x6fa1e118): Standard input FILE structure\n- g_stdout (0x6fa1e138): Standard output FILE structure\n- g_apIobBlocks (0x6fa3ffe0): Array of FILE structure block pointers\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CRT_getbuf: Allocate buffer for stream\n- CRT_isatty: Check if file descriptor is terminal\n- CRT_write: Low-level write to file descriptor\n- CRT_lseek: Seek file position",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:28393cf54a38bf1465f92d01d5d4df21",
