      "name": "ProcessFormatSpecifiers",
      "signature": "int ProcessFormatSpecifiers(int * pOutputContext, byte * pbFormatString, undefined4 * pVarArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Core printf-style format string processor implementing sprintf/vsprintf semantics.\nParses format specifiers and converts variadic arguments to formatted output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize parse state to 0, read first format character\n2. Main loop: for each character in format string until null or error\n3. Classify character using lookup table (0x6fa19380) to get character class\n4. Compute state transition from state machine table (0x6fa193a0)\n5. Switch on new state (0-7):\n   State 0: Output literal character (handle multi-byte lead chars)\n   State 1: Start new format spec (% seen), reset flags/width/precision\n   State 2: Parse flags: space(0x02), #(0x80), +(0x01), -(0x04), 0(0x08)\n   State 3: Parse field width (digit or * for arg-specified)\n   State 4: Start precision (. seen)\n   State 5: Parse precision value\n   State 6: Parse size modifier: h(short), l(long), I64(64-bit), w(wide)\n   State 7: Process conversion specifier:\n     - d/i: Signed decimal\n     - u: Unsigned decimal  \n     - o: Octal\n     - x/X: Hex (lowercase/uppercase)\n     - p: Pointer (8-digit hex)\n     - s/S: String (ANSI/wide)\n     - c/C: Character (ANSI/wide)\n     - e/E/f/g/G: Floating point\n     - n: Store char count\n     - Z: ANSI_STRING struct\n6. For numeric types: extract value, handle sign, convert digits\n7. Apply padding (space or zero) based on flags\n8. Write output via helper functions\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputContext: Format context struct (current pos, remaining chars, buffer start)\n- pbFormatString: Printf format string (null-terminated byte array)\n- pVarArgs: Pointer to variadic argument list on stack\n\nReturns:\n- Number of characters written on success\n- Negative value on error (buffer overflow, invalid format)\n\nFormat Flags (dwFormatFlags bitmask):\n- 0x0001: Force sign (+)\n- 0x0002: Pad with space for positive\n- 0x0004: Left justify (-)\n- 0x0008: Zero pad (0)\n- 0x0010: Long modifier (l)\n- 0x0020: Short modifier (h)\n- 0x0040: Signed conversion\n- 0x0080: Alternate form (#)\n- 0x0100: Negative value\n- 0x0200: Octal prefix (0)\n- 0x0800: Wide string/char\n- 0x8000: 64-bit integer (I64)\n\nHelper Functions:\n- FUN_6fa142b8: Write single character to output\n- FUN_6fa1431e: Write string to output\n- FUN_6fa142ed: Write repeated character (padding)\n- FUN_6fa14356: Get next 32-bit vararg\n- FUN_6fa14363: Get next 64-bit vararg\n- FUN_6fa14373: Get next wide char vararg\n- FUN_6fa1596b: Convert wide char to multi-byte\n\nGlobals:\n- g_pCharTypeTable (0x6fa1de1c): Character type classification table\n- PTR_DAT_6fa1dc44: Default ANSI null string \"(null)\"\n- PTR_DAT_6fa1dc48: Default wide null string L\"(null)\"",
