      "name": "WriteCharToFileBuffer",
      "signature": "void WriteCharToFileBuffer(uint dwChar, int * pFile, int * pnBytesWritten)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes a single character to a buffered FILE stream.\n\nThis is a low-level CRT function used by printf-family formatters to output\ncharacters. It manages buffer space and delegates to FlushFileBuffer when\nthe buffer is exhausted.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement buffer count at pFile+4\n2. If count becomes negative (buffer exhausted):\n   - Call FUN_6fa13a5f (FlushFileBuffer) to flush and refill\n   - Store result code\n3. Else (buffer has space):\n   - Write character byte to current buffer position (*pFile)\n   - Increment buffer pointer\n   - Result = character value (masked to byte)\n4. If result is -1 (0xFFFFFFFF - error):\n   - Set *pnBytesWritten to -1 (error indicator)\n   - Return\n5. Else (success):\n   - Increment *pnBytesWritten counter\n   - Return\n\nParameters:\n  dwChar         - uint - Character to write (only low byte used)\n  pFile          - int* - Pointer to FILE structure:\n                          [+0x0] Buffer pointer (current write position)\n                          [+0x4] Remaining count in buffer\n  pnBytesWritten - int* - Pointer to running byte count, set to -1 on error\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result communicated via pnBytesWritten:\n         Incremented on success, set to -1 on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Buffer full: Delegates to FlushFileBuffer for buffer management\n  - Write error: Sets pnBytesWritten to -1, callers check this to abort\n\nCalled By:\n  - FUN_6fa13b77 (printf formatter) for character output\n  - FUN_6fa142ed (RepeatWriteChar) for padding\n  - FUN_6fa1431e (WriteStringToFile) for string output",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:48de6fa61a4bf40c36c288aa452eb3ad",
