      "name": "RepeatWriteCharToFileBuffer",
      "signature": "void RepeatWriteCharToFileBuffer(uint dwChar, int nRepeatCount, int * pFile, int * pnBytesWritten)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes a character repeatedly to a buffered FILE stream.\n\nCRT helper function for printf-family formatters to output padding\ncharacters (spaces or zeros) for field width alignment.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nRepeatCount <= 0, return immediately (no-op)\n2. Loop nRepeatCount times:\n   a. Decrement loop counter\n   b. Call WriteCharToFileBuffer to output dwChar\n   c. If *pnBytesWritten == -1 (error), return early\n3. Return after all characters written\n\nParameters:\n  dwChar         - uint  - Character to write (only low byte used, typically 0x20 or 0x30)\n  nRepeatCount   - int   - Number of times to repeat the character\n  pFile          - int*  - Pointer to FILE structure for output\n  pnBytesWritten - int*  - Pointer to byte counter, set to -1 on error\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result communicated via pnBytesWritten\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - nRepeatCount <= 0: Returns immediately without writing\n  - Error during write: Returns early when *pnBytesWritten becomes -1\n\nCalled By:\n  ProcessFormatSpecifiers with:\n  - 0x20 (space) for right-align padding before content\n  - 0x30 (zero) for zero-padding numeric fields\n  - 0x20 (space) for left-align padding after content",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
