      "name": "WriteStringToFileBuffer",
      "signature": "void WriteStringToFileBuffer(char * lpszSourceString, int nCharCount, int * pOutputContext, int * pnCharsWritten)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes a sequence of characters from a source string to the file output buffer.\n\nClassification: Worker function (called by ProcessFormatSpecifiers)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nCharCount > 0, exit immediately if no characters to write\n2. Enter loop: decrement nCharCount, read current character from lpszSourceString\n3. Advance lpszSourceString pointer to next character\n4. Call WriteCharToFileBuffer to output the current character\n5. Check if *pnCharsWritten == -1 (error condition), exit early if error occurred\n6. Continue loop while nCharCount > 0\n7. Return after all characters written or on error\n\nParameters:\n  lpszSourceString - char* - Pointer to source character buffer to write from\n  nCharCount       - int   - Number of characters to write from buffer\n  pOutputContext   - int*  - Output buffer context/state pointer\n  pnCharsWritten   - int*  - Pointer to running character count, set to -1 on error\n\nReturns: void\n\nError Handling:\n  If *pnCharsWritten becomes -1 during any WriteCharToFileBuffer call, function\n  exits immediately to propagate error condition to caller.\n\nCallers:\n  ProcessFormatSpecifiers - writes prefix characters, converted values, and strings\n  during printf-style format processing\n\nRelated Functions:\n  WriteCharToFileBuffer       - writes single character to output\n  RepeatWriteCharToFileBuffer - repeats single character N times",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:afc6bf96e31e41127728e4d6585e174f",
