      "name": "GetNextVarArg32",
      "signature": "uint GetNextVarArg32(uint * * ppVarArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Retrieves the next 32-bit argument from a variadic argument list pointer.\n\nClassification: Leaf function / Helper utility\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference ppVarArgs to get current argument pointer\n2. Advance pointer by 4 bytes (sizeof uint)\n3. Store updated pointer back to ppVarArgs\n4. Return the 32-bit value at previous pointer position (before advance)\n\nParameters:\n- ppVarArgs: Pointer to variadic argument list pointer (uint **). On entry,\n  *ppVarArgs points to the next 32-bit argument to fetch. On exit, *ppVarArgs\n  is advanced by 4 bytes to point to the following argument.\n\nReturns:\n- uint: The 32-bit value at the current argument position\n\nMemory Model:\n- No allocation. Modifies *ppVarArgs in place.\n- Caller owns and manages the argument list memory.\n\nCallers:\n- ProcessFormatSpecifiers: Called 10+ times to fetch format arguments (field width,\n  precision, integer values, pointers, string pointers)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fa14363: GetNextVarArg64 - fetches 64-bit argument\n- FUN_6fa14373: GetNextVarArgWideChar - fetches wide char argument",
