      "name": "GetNextVarArg64",
      "signature": "ulonglong GetNextVarArg64(uint * * ppVarArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Retrieves the next 64-bit argument from a variadic argument list.\n\nClassification: Leaf helper function for ProcessFormatSpecifiers printf implementation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current vararg pointer from ppVarArgs\n2. Advance pointer by 8 bytes (64-bit argument size)\n3. Store updated pointer back to ppVarArgs\n4. Load low 32 bits from [ptr-8] into EAX\n5. Load high 32 bits from [ptr-4] into EDX\n6. Return 64-bit value in EDX:EAX\n\nParameters:\n- ppVarArgs: Pointer to vararg list pointer (uint **). Updated to point past consumed argument.\n\nReturns:\n- 64-bit unsigned value (ulonglong in EDX:EAX) from the vararg list.\n\nMemory Model:\n- Does not allocate; modifies caller's vararg pointer via ppVarArgs.\n- Assumes 4-byte aligned stack arguments.\n\nCalled By:\n- ProcessFormatSpecifiers: For I64 format specifier (64-bit integer conversions)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9696a1fa07b46e8a513683c75ff67fe3",
