      "name": "GetNextVarArgWideChar",
      "signature": "ushort GetNextVarArgWideChar(uint * * ppVarArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Retrieves the next 16-bit wide character (WCHAR) from a variadic argument list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Advance the varargs pointer by 4 bytes (sizeof uint)\n2. Read the WCHAR value from the previous position (before advancement)\n3. Return the 16-bit wide character\n\nParameters:\n- ppVarArgs: Pointer to the current varargs pointer position\n\nReturns:\n- ushort: The next wide character from the argument list\n\nNote: Due to x86 calling convention, WCHAR is passed as 32-bit value on stack,\nbut only the low 16 bits contain the actual character. The pointer advances\nby 4 bytes but the function reads a 16-bit value from offset -4.",
