      "name": "InitializeCrtCriticalSections",
      "signature": "void InitializeCrtCriticalSections(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes four C runtime critical sections for thread synchronization.\n\nClassification: Initialization function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load InitializeCriticalSection function pointer into ESI\n2. Initialize g_pCrtCritSection1 (preserved during cleanup)\n3. Initialize g_pCrtCritSection2 (preserved during cleanup)\n4. Initialize g_pCrtCritSection3 (preserved during cleanup)\n5. Initialize g_pCrtCritSection4 (preserved during cleanup)\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- These four critical sections are treated specially in the cleanup function\n  (FUN_6fa143aa) - they are deleted last, after all dynamically allocated\n  critical sections are freed\n- Order of initialization matches reverse order of deletion\n\nCaller Context:\n- Called once from FUN_6fa1448c during TLS initialization\n- Must complete before TlsAlloc is called\n\nGlobal Data:\n- g_pCrtCritSection1 (0x6fa1dc90): Pointer to CRITICAL_SECTION\n- g_pCrtCritSection2 (0x6fa1dc80): Pointer to CRITICAL_SECTION\n- g_pCrtCritSection3 (0x6fa1dc70): Pointer to CRITICAL_SECTION\n- g_pCrtCritSection4 (0x6fa1dc50): Pointer to CRITICAL_SECTION\n- g_pfnInitializeCriticalSection (0x6fa192b0): Import thunk for kernel32!InitializeCriticalSection",
