      "name": "CleanupCrtCriticalSections",
      "signature": "void CleanupCrtCriticalSections(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup function that deletes all CRT critical sections during module shutdown.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Destructor\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load DeleteCriticalSection function pointer into EDI\n2. Initialize loop pointer ESI to start of g_apCrtCriticalSections array (0x6fa1dc4c)\n3. Loop through critical section pointer array (48 slots, stride 4 bytes):\n   a. Skip if pointer is NULL\n   b. Skip if pointer equals any of the 4 reserved critical sections\n   c. For non-reserved entries: call DeleteCriticalSection, then free memory via CrtFreeMemory\n4. Increment pointer and continue until reaching 0x6fa1dd0c (end of array)\n5. Delete reserved critical sections in specific order:\n   - g_pCrtCritSection3 (0x6fa1dc70)\n   - g_pCrtCritSection2 (0x6fa1dc80)\n   - g_pCrtCritSection1 (0x6fa1dc90)\n   - g_pCrtCritSection4 (0x6fa1dc50)\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Four critical sections are treated as reserved and deleted last\n- Deletion order of reserved sections differs from initialization order\n- Non-reserved critical sections have their memory freed after deletion\n\nGlobal Data:\n- g_apCrtCriticalSections (0x6fa1dc4c): Array of CRITICAL_SECTION pointers (48 slots)\n- g_pCrtCritSection1 (0x6fa1dc90): Reserved CRT critical section\n- g_pCrtCritSection2 (0x6fa1dc80): Reserved CRT critical section\n- g_pCrtCritSection3 (0x6fa1dc70): Reserved CRT critical section\n- g_pCrtCritSection4 (0x6fa1dc50): Reserved CRT critical section\n\nCaller Context:\n- Called from FUN_6fa144e0 during module cleanup\n- Called before TlsFree releases the TLS slot",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a0707ad44a579985e4c3b985375d38cb",
