      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Acquires a CRT critical section by index, lazily initializing it if needed.\n\nThis function implements thread-safe lazy initialization of critical sections\nused by the C runtime. It uses double-checked locking with a global lock\n(index 0x11) to prevent race conditions during initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate pointer to critical section slot in global array\n2. Check if critical section at index is already initialized\n3. If not initialized:\n   a. Allocate 0x18 (24) bytes for CRITICAL_SECTION structure\n   b. If allocation fails, call __amsg_exit(0x11) to terminate\n   c. Acquire global CRT lock (index 0x11) for thread safety\n   d. Double-check if still uninitialized (race condition guard)\n   e. If still null: initialize and store new critical section\n   f. If another thread initialized it: free the duplicate allocation\n   g. Release global CRT lock\n4. Enter the critical section\n\nParameters:\n  dwCriticalSectionIndex (uint) - Index into g_apCrtCriticalSections array.\n      Index 0x11 (17) is the global lock used for initialization synchronization.\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return on allocation failure (calls __amsg_exit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Recursive call: Uses index 0x11 as global lock during initialization\n  - Allocation failure: Terminates via __amsg_exit(0x11)\n  - Race condition: If two threads try to initialize same index,\n    second thread frees its allocation and uses the first thread's\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x18 - sizeof(CRITICAL_SECTION) on Win32\n  0x11 - Global CRT lock index AND __amsg_exit error code for memory failure\n\nGlobal State:\n  g_apCrtCriticalSections - Array of LPCRITICAL_SECTION pointers indexed by dwCriticalSectionIndex",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5ba7875cbad7a3d5fce31ff25fd40455",
