      "name": "InitializeCrtThreadLocalStorage",
      "signature": "int InitializeCrtThreadLocalStorage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize CRT Thread Local Storage for the current thread\n\nThis initialization function allocates TLS storage for the CRT and sets up\nthe initial thread's data block. Called once during DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH by\nCrtDllMainHandler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize CRT critical sections (InitializeCrtCriticalSections)\n2. Allocate a TLS slot via TlsAlloc, store index in g_dwTlsIndex\n3. If TlsAlloc fails (returns 0xFFFFFFFF), return 0 (failure)\n4. Allocate 0x74 bytes (116 bytes) for thread-local data via FUN_6fa15c50\n5. If allocation fails, return 0 (failure)\n6. Associate the allocated block with TLS slot via TlsSetValue\n7. If TlsSetValue fails, return 0 (failure)\n8. Initialize the data block via FUN_6fa144fe (sets default values)\n9. Get current thread ID via GetCurrentThreadId\n10. Store thread ID at offset 0x00 of TLS data block\n11. Store 0xFFFFFFFF at offset 0x04 (invalid handle marker)\n12. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None - this is a void function called during CRT initialization\n\nReturns:\n  1 (TRUE) - TLS initialization succeeded\n  0 (FALSE) - TLS allocation or setup failed\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_dwTlsIndex - TLS slot index from TlsAlloc (DWORD at 0x6fa1dd0c)\n  g_DefaultTlsBlockData - Default data pointer stored at TLS block offset 0x50\n\nTLS Data Block Layout (116 bytes at offset):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    4     dwThreadId      Current thread ID from GetCurrentThreadId\n  0x04    4     dwHandleOrFlag  Initialized to 0xFFFFFFFF (invalid handle marker)\n  0x14    4     dwFlag          Set to 1 by FUN_6fa144fe\n  0x50    4     pDefaultData    Set to g_DefaultTlsBlockData by FUN_6fa144fe\n\nError Handling:\n  - TlsAlloc failure returns immediately with 0\n  - Memory allocation failure returns immediately with 0\n  - TlsSetValue failure returns immediately with 0\n  - No cleanup of partial initialization on failure\n\nSSA Temporaries (decompiler-generated, cannot be renamed):\n  lpTlsValue (pTlsData) - Pointer to allocated TLS data block (DWORD *)\n  BVar1 (fSetValueResult) - Return value from TlsSetValue (BOOL)\n  DVar2 (dwThreadId) - Current thread ID from GetCurrentThreadId (DWORD)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1563254ce315644019ac4e0b71caac74",
