      "name": "CleanupCrtTlsAndCriticalSections",
      "signature": "void CleanupCrtTlsAndCriticalSections(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleanup function that releases CRT critical sections and TLS slot during module shutdown.\n\nClassification: Cleanup/Destructor\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CleanupCrtCriticalSections to delete all CRT critical sections\n2. Load g_dwTlsIndex from 0x6fa1dd0c\n3. Compare against TLS_OUT_OF_INDEXES (0xFFFFFFFF)\n4. If TLS index is valid (!= 0xFFFFFFFF):\n   a. Push TLS index as parameter\n   b. Call TlsFree via import at 0x6fa19258 to release the TLS slot\n   c. Set g_dwTlsIndex = 0xFFFFFFFF to mark as invalid\n5. Return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nGlobal Data:\n  g_dwTlsIndex (0x6fa1dd0c): TLS slot index allocated by TlsAlloc during init\n    - Value 0xFFFFFFFF indicates no valid TLS slot (TLS_OUT_OF_INDEXES)\n    - Set to 0xFFFFFFFF after TlsFree to prevent double-free\n\nCaller Context:\n  Called from CrtDllMainHandler during DLL_PROCESS_DETACH (cleanup sequence)\n  Execution order: FUN_6fa14bc0 -> CleanupCrtTlsAndCriticalSections -> FUN_6fa1521e\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - TLS index check prevents TlsFree on invalid/already-freed slot\n  - Critical sections cleaned up before TLS to ensure proper shutdown order",
