      "name": "FreeCrtThreadLocalData",
      "signature": "void FreeCrtThreadLocalData(dword * pTlsBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Frees all dynamically allocated buffers in a CRT thread-local storage block\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwTlsIndex is valid (not 0xFFFFFFFF)\n2. If pTlsBlock is NULL, retrieve current thread's TLS block via TlsGetValue()\n3. If TLS block is NULL, skip to step 11 (just clear TLS slot)\n4. Free buffer at offset 0x24 if non-NULL (locale ctype data)\n5. Free buffer at offset 0x28 if non-NULL (locale collate data)\n6. Free buffer at offset 0x30 if non-NULL (locale numeric data)\n7. Free buffer at offset 0x38 if non-NULL (locale monetary data)\n8. Free buffer at offset 0x40 if non-NULL (locale time data)\n9. Free buffer at offset 0x44 if non-NULL (locale category string)\n10. Free buffer at offset 0x50 only if not pointing to g_DefaultTlsBlockData\n11. Free the TLS block structure itself\n12. Clear the thread's TLS slot by calling TlsSetValue(g_dwTlsIndex, NULL)\n\nParameters:\n  pTlsBlock (dword *) - Pointer to CRT TLS data block to free, or NULL to use\n                        current thread's TLS block from TlsGetValue()\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nTLS Block Layout (116 bytes total):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Description\n  0x00    4     dwThreadId          Owning thread ID\n  0x04    4     dwPrevHandle        Previous handle sentinel (-1)\n  0x14    4     dwInitializedFlag   Block initialization flag\n  0x24    4     pCtypeData          Locale ctype buffer (CrtFreeMemory)\n  0x28    4     pCollateData        Locale collate buffer (CrtFreeMemory)\n  0x30    4     pNumericData        Locale numeric buffer (CrtFreeMemory)\n  0x38    4     pMonetaryData       Locale monetary buffer (CrtFreeMemory)\n  0x40    4     pTimeData           Locale time buffer (CrtFreeMemory)\n  0x44    4     pCategoryStr        Locale category string (CrtFreeMemory)\n  0x50    4     pTlsBlockData       Default TLS data ptr or allocated data\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If TLS index is invalid (-1), function returns immediately\n  - If passed NULL, retrieves and frees current thread's TLS block\n  - Offset 0x50 pointer is only freed if not equal to g_DefaultTlsBlockData\n  - Always clears TLS slot to NULL after freeing, even if block was NULL\n\nCallers:\n  - CrtDllMainHandler: During DLL_THREAD_DETACH with NULL parameter",
