      "name": "StringLengthBounded",
      "signature": "int StringLengthBounded(char * lpszString, int nMaxLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Calculate string length with maximum bound (strnlen equivalent).\n\nScans input string for null terminator, stopping at either the null\ncharacter or after scanning nMaxLength bytes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer pszCurrent to string start\n2. Initialize counter nRemaining to nMaxLength\n3. If nMaxLength is 0, skip loop entirely\n4. Loop: decrement counter, check for null terminator\n   - If null found, break from loop early\n   - Otherwise advance pointer and continue while counter > 0\n5. After loop: if current character is null terminator:\n   - Return (pszCurrent - lpszString) = actual string length\n6. Otherwise string exceeds max, return nMaxLength\n\nParameters:\n  lpszString - Pointer to null-terminated ANSI string to measure\n  nMaxLength - Maximum number of bytes to scan\n\nReturns:\n  int - String length if null found within nMaxLength bytes\n        nMaxLength if string is longer or equal to max bound\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - nMaxLength == 0: Returns 0 immediately (no scanning)\n  - Empty string: Returns 0\n  - String length == nMaxLength: Returns nMaxLength (null at position nMaxLength counts as full)\n\nCalled by: FUN_6fa14618 (LocaleMapString) to get bounded string length\n           before passing to LCMapStringA/W",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
