      "name": "GetCharTypeWithMask",
      "signature": "uint GetCharTypeWithMask(int nCharCode, uint dwTypeMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Get character type flags masked by a specified bitmask.\n\nRetrieves Windows character type information for a character code and returns\nthe type flags ANDed with the provided mask. Optimized for ASCII characters\n(0x00-0xFF) using a cached lookup table; falls back to GetStringTypeW/A for\nextended characters via locale-aware string type conversion.\n\nClassification: Internal utility - locale-aware character classification helper\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if character is in ASCII range (nCharCode + 1 < 0x101)\n2. If ASCII: lookup type directly from g_pCharTypeTable[nCharCode * 2]\n3. If extended character: check lead byte marker in type table\n4. If lead byte has 0x80 flag: build 2-byte MBCS buffer (high byte, low byte)\n5. If no 0x80 flag: build 1-byte buffer (low byte only)\n6. Call FUN_6fa16538 (GetStringType wrapper) to get character type\n7. If type lookup fails: return 0\n8. Return character type ANDed with mask\n\nParameters:\n  nCharCode  - int: Character code to classify (allows negative/extended values)\n  dwTypeMask - uint: Bitmask to AND with retrieved character type flags\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Character type flags masked by dwTypeMask, or 0 if lookup fails\n\nCharacter Type Flags (CT_CTYPE1):\n  0x0001 - C1_UPPER    (uppercase)\n  0x0002 - C1_LOWER    (lowercase)\n  0x0004 - C1_DIGIT    (decimal digits)\n  0x0008 - C1_SPACE    (space characters)\n  0x0010 - C1_PUNCT    (punctuation)\n  0x0020 - C1_CNTRL    (control characters)\n  0x0040 - C1_BLANK    (blank characters)\n  0x0080 - C1_XDIGIT   (hexadecimal digits)\n  0x0100 - C1_ALPHA    (any linguistic character)\n\nGlobal Data:\n  g_pCharTypeTable (0x6fa1de1c) - Cached character type lookup table pointer\n\nCallers: ToUpperCharLocale, ToLowerCharLocale, StringToIntLocale, FUN_6fa16a8c",
