      "name": "Multiply64x64",
      "signature": "longlong Multiply64x64(uint dwOperandALow, int nOperandAHigh, uint dwOperandBLow, int nOperandBHigh)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Performs 64-bit multiplication of two 64-bit integers represented as low/high 32-bit pairs.\n\nThis is a compiler runtime helper equivalent to __allmul for 64-bit integer multiplication\non 32-bit x86 systems where native 64-bit multiplication is unavailable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if both high parts are zero (simple 32x32 case)\n2. If both high parts zero: return dwOperandALow * dwOperandBLow (MUL instruction gives 64-bit result)\n3. Otherwise compute full 64x64 multiplication using distributive property:\n   (A_lo + A_hi*2^32) * (B_lo + B_hi*2^32) =\n   A_lo*B_lo + A_lo*B_hi*2^32 + A_hi*B_lo*2^32 + A_hi*B_hi*2^64\n4. Since result is truncated to 64 bits, A_hi*B_hi*2^64 term is discarded\n5. Return low 32 bits from A_lo*B_lo, high 32 bits from sum of cross-products\n\nParameters:\n  dwOperandALow  - Low 32 bits of first 64-bit operand (unsigned)\n  nOperandAHigh  - High 32 bits of first 64-bit operand (signed for overflow handling)\n  dwOperandBLow  - Low 32 bits of second 64-bit operand (unsigned)\n  nOperandBHigh  - High 32 bits of second 64-bit operand (signed for overflow handling)\n\nReturns:\n  longlong - 64-bit product in EDX:EAX (high:low)\n\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (callee cleans 16 bytes from stack via RET 0x10)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - When both high parts are 0, uses fast path with single MUL instruction\n  - Overflow behavior: truncates to low 64 bits (no overflow detection)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d54b31472f74b078be31f20f65c7b2d3",
