      "name": "CRT_CleanupIobBlocks",
      "signature": "void CRT_CleanupIobBlocks(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleans up all CRT I/O buffer blocks during DLL unload, deleting critical sections and freeing memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize pointer to g_apIobBlocks array (64 entries from 0x6fa3ffe0 to 0x6fa400e0)\n2. For each block pointer in the array:\n   a. Skip if block pointer is NULL\n   b. Iterate through 32 IOB entries per block (stride 0x24 = 36 bytes, total 0x480 bytes)\n   c. For each entry, check if critical section is initialized (SpinCount at offset 0x8 != 0)\n   d. If initialized, call DeleteCriticalSection to release synchronization object\n   e. After processing all entries, call CrtFreeMemory to free the block\n   f. Zero the block pointer to mark as freed\n3. Advance to next block pointer and repeat until end of array\n\nParameters: None (void function)\n\nReturns: void\n\nRegister Usage:\n- ESI: pdwBlockPtr - pointer to current block pointer in g_apIobBlocks array\n- EDI: dwBlockBase - base address of current IOB block\n- EBX: pCriticalSection - pointer to CRITICAL_SECTION within current IOB entry\n\nVariable Mapping (decompiler names):\n- puVar1: pdwBlockPtr (uint *) - iterates through g_apIobBlocks array\n- uVar2: dwBlockBase (uint) - base address of current block for bounds checking\n- lpCriticalSection: pCriticalSection - pointer to CS at offset 0x0C in IOB entry\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Blocks may be uninitialized (NULL pointers) - safely skipped\n- Critical sections may be uninitialized (SpinCount == 0) - safely skipped\n- Called only during DLL_PROCESS_DETACH from CrtDllMainHandler\n\nStructure Layout (IOB Entry - 36 bytes each, 32 per block):\nOffset  Size  Field           Type                Description\n0x00    4     hFile           HANDLE              File handle (0xFFFFFFFF if unused)\n0x04    1     bFlags          byte                Status flags (0x81=initialized, etc.)\n0x05    1     bLineEnd        byte                Line ending type (0x0A = LF)\n0x08    4     dwSpinCount     uint                Critical section spin count (0 if uninitialized)\n0x0C    24    CriticalSection CRITICAL_SECTION    Per-handle synchronization\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480: Block size (32 entries * 36 bytes)\n- 0x24: IOB entry stride (36 bytes)\n- 0x0C: Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION within IOB entry\n- 0x6fa400e0: End address of g_apIobBlocks array (start + 64*4)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b7026c232ba5b32b3521a3c7482af720",
