      "name": "CrtSetupEnvironmentArray",
      "signature": "void CrtSetupEnvironmentArray(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "CrtSetupEnvironmentArray - Builds NULL-terminated array of environment variable strings\n\nConverts the raw environment block (contiguous null-terminated strings) into a \nstandard C-style array of string pointers (char** environ format).\n\nClassification: Initialization function (CRT startup)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If environment block not initialized, call FUN_6fa16a59 to fetch it\n2. Count valid environment variables (those not starting with '=')\n   - System variables like \"=C:=C:\\path\" are skipped\n3. Allocate pointer array: (count + 1) * 4 bytes for NULL terminator\n4. If allocation fails, call __amsg_exit(9) - out of memory\n5. Iterate environment block again, for each non-'=' prefixed string:\n   a. Allocate buffer for string copy (strlen + 1)\n   b. If allocation fails, call __amsg_exit(9)\n   c. Copy string using FUN_6fa15ee0 (strcpy equivalent)\n   d. Store pointer in array, advance array pointer\n6. Free original environment block via CrtFreeMemory\n7. Clear g_pEnvironmentStrings to NULL\n8. NULL-terminate the array\n9. Set g_fEnvironmentArrayInitialized = 1\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void (modifies global state)\n\nLocal Variables (SSA temporaries - cannot be renamed in decompiler):\n  iVar5 (nEnvVarCount): int - Count of valid environment variables\n  puVar6 (pszEnvBlockIter): char * - Iterator through environment block strings\n  puVar3 (ppszEnvArrayEntry): char ** - Current write position in environ array\n  sVar2 (dwStringLength): uint - Length returned by _strlen\n  pvVar4 (pszEnvStringCopy): char * - Allocated buffer for individual env string\n  cVar1 (chCurrentChar): char - First char of current string for null check\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_ppEnvironmentArray (0x6fa3ea20) - Pointer to allocated environ array\n  g_pEnvironmentStrings (0x6fa3ea48) - Cleared to NULL after processing\n  g_fEnvironmentArrayInitialized (0x6fa400f4) - Set to 1 on completion\n\nError Handling:\n  Calls __amsg_exit(9) on allocation failure - terminates process\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Environment strings starting with '=' are internal Windows markers\n    (e.g., \"=C:=C:\\Windows\") and are excluded from the array\n  - Empty environment block results in single-element NULL array\n\nCalled From: CrtDllMainHandler (DLL initialization)",
