      "name": "CRT_ParseCommandLineArgs",
      "signature": "void CRT_ParseCommandLineArgs(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "CRT_ParseCommandLineArgs - Initialize argc/argv for the C runtime library\n\nParses the command line string into an array of argument strings, storing\nthe result in global variables g_nArgc and g_ppszArgv. Called during CRT\ninitialization from CrtDllMainHandler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if environment is initialized (g_fCrtEnvInitialized), call FUN_6fa16a59 if not\n2. Call GetModuleFileNameA to populate g_szModuleFileName buffer (260 bytes)\n3. Store pointer to module filename in g_pszModulePath\n4. Select source: use g_lpszCommandLine if non-empty, else g_szModuleFileName\n5. First pass: call FUN_6fa14d66 with NULL output buffers to count args/chars\n6. Allocate memory: nCharCount + (nArgCount * sizeof(char*)) bytes via malloc\n7. If allocation fails, call __amsg_exit(8) to abort with out-of-memory error\n8. Second pass: call FUN_6fa14d66 to populate argv array and argument strings\n9. Store result in g_ppszArgv and g_nArgc (argc is count minus 1)\n\nParameters:\n  None (void)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_szModuleFileName (0x6fa3eae8) - 260-byte buffer filled with module path\n  g_pszModulePath (0x6fa3ea30) - Pointer to module filename buffer\n  g_ppszArgv (0x6fa3ea18) - Pointer to argv array (allocated)\n  g_nArgc (0x6fa3ea14) - Argument count minus 1 (argc-1)\n\nGlobals Read:\n  g_fCrtEnvInitialized (0x6fa400f8) - Environment initialization flag\n  g_lpszCommandLine - Command line string pointer\n\nMemory:\n  Allocates: (nCharCount + nArgCount*4) bytes for argv array and strings\n  Layout: [argv[0]|argv[1]|...|argv[n]|NULL|str0\\0|str1\\0|...|strn\\0]\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_lpszCommandLine is empty (first byte is 0), uses module filename\n  - malloc failure triggers __amsg_exit(8) - fatal CRT error, does not return\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH, maximum length for GetModuleFileNameA buffer\n  8 - __amsg_exit code for R6008 \"not enough space for arguments\"",
