      "name": "ParseCommandLineToArgv",
      "signature": "void ParseCommandLineToArgv(byte * pbCmdLine, byte * * ppbArgv, byte * pbBuffer, int * pnArgc, int * pnBytesNeeded)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Parses a command-line string into argc/argv format with Windows-style quoting rules.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize *pnBytesNeeded=0, *pnArgc=1 (program name counts as first arg)\n2. If ppbArgv not NULL, store pbBuffer as first argv entry\n3. Parse first argument (program name/path):\n   a. If starts with 0x22 (double-quote): copy until closing quote or NUL\n   b. Else: copy until space (0x20), tab (0x09), or NUL\n   c. Handle MBCS lead bytes (bit 4 in g_abCharTypeTable) - copy both bytes\n4. NUL-terminate first argument in buffer if pbBuffer not NULL\n5. Main parsing loop for remaining arguments:\n   a. Skip whitespace (space/tab)\n   b. If end of string, exit loop\n   c. Record new argv pointer, increment argc\n   d. Parse argument with backslash/quote escaping:\n      - Count consecutive backslashes\n      - On quote: if even backslashes, toggle quote mode; if odd, quote is literal\n      - Output backslashCount/2 backslashes\n      - Handle MBCS lead bytes\n   e. NUL-terminate argument\n6. Set final argv entry to NULL if ppbArgv not NULL\n7. Increment argc once more (for NULL terminator slot)\n\nParameters:\n  pbCmdLine      - Input command line string to parse\n  ppbArgv        - Output array of argument pointers (NULL to just count)\n  pbBuffer       - Output buffer for parsed argument strings (NULL to just count)\n  pnArgc         - Output: number of arguments (includes program name)\n  pnBytesNeeded  - Output: total bytes needed for all argument strings\n\nReturns: void (results via output parameters)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - First call with ppbArgv=NULL, pbBuffer=NULL measures required sizes\n  - Second call allocates buffer and fills actual data\n  - Backslash escaping: 2n backslashes before quote = n backslashes\n  - Backslash escaping: 2n+1 backslashes before quote = n backslashes + literal quote\n  - MBCS: characters with bit 4 set in g_abCharTypeTable are lead bytes\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x22 - Double-quote character (\")\n  0x5c - Backslash character (\\)\n  0x20 - Space character\n  0x09 - Tab character\n  0x04 - MBCS lead byte flag in character type table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:50cd6b6fd69b78c0380659763fce7ea0",
