      "name": "CRT_GetEnvironmentStrings",
      "signature": "LPSTR CRT_GetEnvironmentStrings(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "CRT_GetEnvironmentStrings - Retrieve process environment block as ANSI string\n\nObtains the process environment strings, converting from Unicode to ANSI if necessary.\nCaches the API mode (Unicode vs ANSI) in g_dwEnvStringsApiMode for subsequent calls.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwEnvStringsApiMode for cached API mode (0=unknown, 1=Unicode, 2=ANSI)\n2. If mode is unknown (0):\n   a. Try GetEnvironmentStringsW() first\n   b. If Unicode API succeeds, set g_dwEnvStringsApiMode = 1, goto Unicode path\n   c. If Unicode fails, try GetEnvironmentStringsA()\n   d. If ANSI API succeeds, set g_dwEnvStringsApiMode = 2, goto ANSI path\n   e. If both fail, return NULL\n3. Unicode path (mode 1):\n   a. Call GetEnvironmentStringsW() to get wide string block\n   b. Calculate block length by scanning for double-null terminator\n   c. Call WideCharToMultiByte with NULL buffer to get required size\n   d. Allocate buffer with _malloc()\n   e. Call WideCharToMultiByte to convert Unicode to ANSI\n   f. If conversion fails, free buffer and set result to NULL\n   g. Call FreeEnvironmentStringsW() to release system buffer\n   h. Return converted ANSI buffer (caller owns memory)\n4. ANSI path (mode 2):\n   a. Call GetEnvironmentStringsA() to get ANSI block\n   b. Calculate block length by scanning for double-null terminator\n   c. Allocate buffer with _malloc()\n   d. Copy block via FUN_6fa15fd0 (memcpy)\n   e. Call FreeEnvironmentStringsA() to release system buffer\n   f. Return copied buffer (caller owns memory)\n\nParameters:\n  None - this function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  LPSTR - Pointer to allocated environment block (caller must free), or NULL on failure\n\nGlobals:\n  g_dwEnvStringsApiMode (0x6fa3ebec) - Cached API mode: 0=unknown, 1=Unicode, 2=ANSI\n\nMemory Management:\n  - Returns newly allocated buffer owned by caller\n  - Caller responsible for freeing with CrtFreeMemory()\n\nSSA Temporaries:\n  lpWideCharStr (pwszEnvBlock) - Wide char environment block from GetEnvironmentStringsW\n  pCVar9 (lpszAnsiEnvBlock) - ANSI environment block from GetEnvironmentStringsA\n  WVar2 (wchCurrent) - Current wide character during Unicode scan\n  pWVar3, pWVar4 (pwszScan, pwszPrev) - Wide string scan pointers\n  cVar1 (chCurrent) - Current ANSI character during scan\n  pcVar7, pcVar8 (lpszScan, lpszPrev) - ANSI string scan pointers\n  iVar5 (nWideCharCount) - Wide character count including null terminator\n  _Size (cbRequiredSize) - Required buffer size from WideCharToMultiByte\n  pCVar6 (lpszAllocBuffer) - Allocated output buffer pointer",
