      "name": "CRT_GetModuleOSVersion",
      "signature": "void CRT_GetModuleOSVersion(ushort * pwOSVersion)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Extracts the minimum required OS version from the current module's PE header.\n\nClassification: Leaf function - called only from heap selection initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output to 0 (no version info)\n2. Call GetModuleHandleA(NULL) to get base address of current executable\n3. Verify DOS signature \"MZ\" (0x5A4D) at module base\n4. Read PE header offset from DOS header offset 0x3C (e_lfanew field)\n5. If PE offset is non-zero, navigate to PE Optional Header\n6. Extract MajorOperatingSystemVersion (offset 0x1A from PE signature)\n7. Extract MinorOperatingSystemVersion (offset 0x1B from PE signature)\n8. Store combined version as ushort (major in low byte, minor in high byte)\n\nParameters:\n  pwOSVersion - Pointer to ushort receiving OS version (major | minor << 8)\n                Set to 0 if PE header invalid or missing\n\nReturns: void\n\nPE Header Structure Reference:\n  DOS Header offset 0x00: \"MZ\" signature (0x5A4D)\n  DOS Header offset 0x3C: e_lfanew (offset to PE header)\n  PE Optional Header + 0x18: MajorOperatingSystemVersion (offset 0x1A from PE sig)\n  PE Optional Header + 0x19: MinorOperatingSystemVersion (offset 0x1B from PE sig)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 if module base lacks \"MZ\" DOS signature\n  - Returns 0 if e_lfanew PE offset is NULL/zero\n  - Assumes PE32 format (32-bit Optional Header offsets)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
