      "name": "CRT_InitializeHeapSystem",
      "signature": "int CRT_InitializeHeapSystem(int nSerialize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT Heap System Initialization - Creates and configures the CRT heap\n\nThis initialization function creates the primary CRT heap using Windows HeapCreate,\nthen selects and initializes the appropriate heap implementation based on OS version\nand environment configuration. Called during DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create Windows heap via HeapCreate with serialization based on nSerialize\n   - If nSerialize==0: Use HEAP_NO_SERIALIZE flag (single-threaded)\n   - If nSerialize!=0: Use serialized heap (thread-safe)\n2. Store heap handle in g_hCrtHeap global\n3. If HeapCreate fails (returns NULL), return 0 (failure)\n4. Call CRT_SelectHeapImplementation to determine heap type\n5. Store heap type in g_dwCrtHeapType (1=Windows, 2=Small Block, 3=Old Small Block)\n6. If heap type is 3 (old small block heap):\n   - Call FUN_6fa16d20(0x3f8) to initialize old SBH structures\n   - 0x3f8 = 1016 bytes, likely max block size for old SBH\n7. Else if heap type is 2 (small block heap):\n   - Call FUN_6fa17571() to initialize SBH with VirtualAlloc\n8. Else (heap type 1 or other):\n   - Return 1 immediately (use Windows heap directly)\n9. Check if heap-specific initialization succeeded (non-NULL return)\n10. If initialization failed, destroy the heap and return 0\n11. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n  nSerialize (int) - Heap serialization flag\n    0: Create non-serialized heap (HEAP_NO_SERIALIZE flag set)\n    1: Create serialized/thread-safe heap (no special flags)\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Heap initialization succeeded\n  0 - Heap initialization failed (HeapCreate or heap-specific init failed)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_hCrtHeap (HANDLE @ 0x6fa3ffc4) - Primary CRT heap handle\n  g_dwCrtHeapType (uint @ 0x6fa3ffc8) - Heap implementation type selector\n\nHeap Type Values:\n  1 = Windows heap only (direct HeapAlloc/HeapFree)\n  2 = Small Block Heap (SBH) with VirtualAlloc backing\n  3 = Old Small Block Heap with HeapAlloc backing\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1000 - Initial heap size (4KB)\n  0x0 - Maximum heap size (growable, no limit)\n  0x3f8 (1016) - Old SBH max block size parameter\n\nSSA Temporaries:\n  ppuVar1 (void**): Decompiler SSA temp holding return value from SBH init functions.\n  Represents EAX return value, not an actual stack local. Cannot be renamed.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Non-zero nSerialize from caller indicates thread-safe mode needed\n  - Heap type 1 requires no additional initialization\n  - SBH failure causes full cleanup (HeapDestroy) before failure return",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
