      "name": "InvokeCrtExitCallbackWithMessages",
      "signature": "void InvokeCrtExitCallbackWithMessages(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Invokes CRT exit callback with pre/post messages during abnormal termination.\n\nCalled by __amsg_exit to display runtime error messages and invoke registered\nexit callback before process termination. Part of MSVC CRT error handling.\n\nClassification: Internal utility - CRT exit sequence helper\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if console mode (g_dwCrtAppType == 1) OR\n   if no app type but console handle mode (g_dwCrtAppType == 0 AND g_dwCrtOutputHandleMode == 1)\n2. If not console mode, return immediately (GUI apps skip message output)\n3. Call FUN_6fa152ff with 0xFC (pre-callback message marker)\n4. Check if exit callback registered (g_pfnCrtExitCallback != NULL)\n5. If callback exists, invoke it via indirect call\n6. Call FUN_6fa152ff with 0xFF (post-callback/termination message marker)\n7. Return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xFC - Pre-callback message code passed to FUN_6fa152ff\n  0xFF - Post-callback/termination message code  \n  0x01 - Console application type\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_dwCrtAppType (0x6fa3ea50) - CRT application type (1=console, 0=GUI/unknown)\n  g_dwCrtOutputHandleMode (0x6fa3ea54) - Output handle mode flag\n  g_pfnCrtExitCallback (0x6fa3ebf0) - Registered exit callback function pointer\n\nCross-References:\n  Called only by __amsg_exit during runtime error handling",
