      "name": "DisplayCrtRuntimeErrorMessage",
      "signature": "void DisplayCrtRuntimeErrorMessage(dword dwErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Displays CRT runtime error message based on error code lookup table.\n\nClassification: Internal utility - CRT error message display helper\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter to 0 and table pointer to g_adwRuntimeErrorTable\n2. Search runtime error table for matching error code:\n   - Compare dwErrorCode against table entry at current position\n   - If match found, break out of loop\n   - Otherwise advance pointer by 8 bytes (stride of 2 DWORDs per entry)\n   - Increment counter and continue until reaching g_pRuntimeErrorTableEnd\n3. Verify error code was found in table (compare against table entry at calculated index)\n4. If not found, exit function immediately\n5. Check application mode for output method:\n   a. Console mode (g_dwCrtAppType == 1) OR\n      (g_dwCrtAppType == 0 AND g_dwCrtOutputHandleMode == 1):\n      - Get error message string pointer from table[index*8 + 4]\n      - Calculate message length via strlen\n      - Get standard error handle (STD_ERROR_HANDLE = -12 = 0xFFFFFFF4)\n      - Write message to stderr via WriteFile\n   b. GUI mode (not console) AND error code != 0xFC:\n      - Get module filename via GetModuleFileNameA\n      - If GetModuleFileNameA fails, use \"<program name unknown>\"\n      - Truncate path to last 60 chars if > 60, prepend \"...\"\n      - Build message box string via FUN_6fa15ee0/FUN_6fa15ef0:\n        \"Runtime Error!\n\nProgram: <path>\n\n<error message>\"\n      - Display message box via FUN_6fa17b95 with MB_ICONERROR|MB_TASKMODAL (0x12010)\n   c. Error code 0xFC in GUI mode: skip display (pre-callback marker)\n6. Return\n\nParameters:\n  dwErrorCode (DWORD) - Runtime error code to look up and display.\n                        Values: 0x02, 0x08-0x13, 0x18-0x1C, 0x78-0x7A, 0xFC, 0xFF\n                        0xFC = Pre-callback marker (skipped in GUI mode)\n                        0xFF = Post-callback/termination marker\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8 - Stride of runtime error table entries (code + string pointer)\n  0x3C (60) - Maximum path length before truncation\n  0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH buffer size for GetModuleFileNameA\n  0xFFFFFFF4 (-12) - STD_ERROR_HANDLE for GetStdHandle\n  0x12010 - MB_ICONERROR (0x10) | MB_TASKMODAL (0x2000) | MB_SETFOREGROUND (0x10000)\n  0xFC - Pre-callback message code (skipped in GUI mode)\n  0xFF - Post-callback termination message code\n\nError Table Structure (g_adwRuntimeErrorTable):\n  Offset 0x0: DWORD dwErrorCode\n  Offset 0x4: char* pszErrorMessage\n  Stride: 8 bytes per entry\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_dwCrtAppType (0x6fa3ea50) - Application type (1=console, 0=GUI)\n  g_dwCrtOutputHandleMode (0x6fa3ea54) - Output handle mode flag\n  g_adwRuntimeErrorTable (0x6fa1e068) - Runtime error code/message table\n  g_pRuntimeErrorTableEnd (0x6fa1e0f8) - End of error table\n\nCross-References:\n  Called by: __amsg_exit, InvokeCrtExitCallbackWithMessages",
