      "name": "CRT_lseek",
      "signature": "dword CRT_lseek(uint dwFileHandle, long lOffset, dword dwOrigin)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT_lseek - Reposition file pointer with thread-safe locking\n\nWorker function providing POSIX-style lseek() for the CRT file I/O system.\nCalled by CRT_flsbuf to seek within buffered file streams.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file handle is within valid range (< g_dwMaxIobHandles)\n2. Calculate IOB block index: bucket = handle >> 5, slot = handle & 0x1F\n3. Check IOB entry flags at offset +4: bit 0 must be set (file is open)\n4. If invalid handle or file not open, set errno=9 (EBADF), doserrno=0, return -1\n5. Lock the file handle via CRT_LockFileHandle (per-handle critical section)\n6. Call CRT_lseek_nolock to perform actual SetFilePointer operation\n7. Unlock the file handle via CRT_UnlockFileHandle\n8. Return new file position or -1 on error\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileHandle (uint) - CRT file descriptor index into IOB table\n  lOffset (long) - Byte offset for seek operation (signed)\n  dwOrigin (dword) - Seek origin: 0=FILE_BEGIN, 1=FILE_CURRENT, 2=FILE_END\n\nReturns:\n  New file position on success\n  0xFFFFFFFF (-1) on error with errno set to EBADF (9)\n\nIOB Entry Structure (stride 0x24 = 36 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  +0x00   4     (unknown)     Reserved\n  +0x04   1     bFlags        Status flags (bit 0 = file open)\n  +0x08   4     dwLockInit    Critical section initialized flag\n  +0x0C   24    CritSection   CRITICAL_SECTION for thread safety\n\nIOB Bucket Addressing:\n  g_apIobBlocks[handle >> 5] gives base of 32-entry bucket\n  (handle & 0x1F) * 0x24 gives offset within bucket\n  Total: base + slot*36 + field_offset\n\nError Codes:\n  errno = 9 (EBADF) - Bad file descriptor",
