      "name": "CRT_lseek_nolock",
      "signature": "DWORD CRT_lseek_nolock(uint dwFileHandle, long lOffset, DWORD dwOrigin)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT_lseek_nolock - Reposition file pointer without locking (nolock variant)\n\nInternal worker function for lseek that performs file pointer positioning\nwithout acquiring the file handle lock. Must only be called when caller\nalready holds the lock (e.g., from CRT_lseek).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert CRT file descriptor to Win32 HANDLE via FUN_6fa17d22\n2. If invalid handle (returns -1), set errno=EBADF (9), return -1\n3. Call Win32 SetFilePointer(hFile, lOffset, NULL, dwOrigin)\n4. If SetFilePointer fails (returns -1), call GetLastError\n5. If error occurred, translate Windows error to errno via FUN_6fa17c1e, return -1\n6. On success, clear \"text mode CR pending\" flag (bit 1) at IOB entry offset +4\n   - IOB address = g_apIobBlocks[dwFileHandle >> 5] + (dwFileHandle & 0x1F) * 0x24 + 4\n7. Return new file position from SetFilePointer\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileHandle (uint) - CRT file descriptor index into IOB table\n  lOffset (LONG) - Signed byte offset for seek operation\n  dwOrigin (DWORD) - Seek origin: 0=FILE_BEGIN, 1=FILE_CURRENT, 2=FILE_END\n\nReturns:\n  New file position (DWORD) on success\n  0xFFFFFFFF (-1) on error with errno set\n\nIOB Entry Flags (offset +4, byte):\n  Bit 0 (0x01) - File is open\n  Bit 1 (0x02) - Text mode CR pending (cleared by seek)\n\nIOB Bucket Addressing:\n  Bucket index = dwFileHandle >> 5 (divide by 32)\n  Slot within bucket = dwFileHandle & 0x1F (mod 32)\n  Entry stride = 0x24 (36 bytes)\n\nError Codes:\n  errno = 9 (EBADF) - Bad file descriptor (invalid handle)\n  errno = varies - Mapped from Windows error via FUN_6fa17c1e\n\nCallers:\n  CRT_lseek - Thread-safe wrapper that locks before calling\n  FUN_6fa1558f - Direct caller (likely internal CRT operation)",
