      "name": "CRT_write",
      "signature": "int CRT_write(int nFileHandle, char * lpszBuffer, uint dwCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT_write - Write data to a file handle with thread safety\n\nWrites bytes from a buffer to the specified file handle. This is the public\nCRT write interface that provides thread-safe access by locking the handle\nbefore performing I/O and unlocking after completion.\n\nClassification: Public API / Worker function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file handle is within valid range (< g_dwMaxIobHandles)\n2. Calculate IOB block index: bucket = handle >> 5, offset = (handle & 0x1F) * 0x24\n3. Check IOB entry flags byte at offset +4 for valid bit (0x01)\n4. If invalid handle: set errno=EBADF (9), _doserrno=0, return -1\n5. Lock file handle via CRT_LockFileHandle for thread safety\n6. Call CRT_write_nolock to perform actual write operation\n7. Unlock file handle via CRT_UnlockFileHandle\n8. Return bytes written or -1 on error\n\nParameters:\nnFileHandle (int)    - CRT file handle (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr, etc.)\nlpszBuffer (char *)  - Pointer to buffer containing data to write\ndwCount (uint)       - Number of bytes to write from buffer\n\nReturns:\n>= 0  Number of bytes successfully written\n-1    Error occurred (errno set to EBADF=9 for invalid handle)\n\nError Handling:\nEBADF (9): Bad file descriptor - handle out of range or not open\n\nIOB Block Structure Access:\nOffset  Size  Field         Description\n0x00    4     hOsHandle     OS file handle (HANDLE)\n0x04    1     bFlags        Status flags (bit 0 = open/valid)\n\nHandle Calculation:\nbucket_index = nFileHandle >> 5  (divide by 32)\nentry_offset = (nFileHandle & 0x1F) * 0x24  (mod 32 * 36 bytes per entry)\nflags_ptr = g_apIobBlocks[bucket_index] + entry_offset + 4\n\nCallers: CRT_flsbuf, FUN_6fa17e94",
