      "name": "CRT_write_nolock",
      "signature": "int CRT_write_nolock(int nFileHandle, char * lpszBuffer, uint dwByteCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT_write_nolock - Write buffer to file handle without locking\n\nLow-level CRT write function that writes bytes to a file descriptor without\nacquiring the file lock (caller must hold lock via CRT_LockFileHandle).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 immediately if dwByteCount is 0\n2. Calculate IOB block index: nBucketIndex = nFileHandle >> 5\n3. Calculate entry offset: nIobEntryOffset = (nFileHandle & 0x1F) * 0x24\n4. Get IOB entry from g_apIobBlocks[nBucketIndex] + nIobEntryOffset\n5. If FAPPEND flag (0x20) set at offset+4, seek to end via CRT_lseek_nolock\n6. Check FTEXT flag (0x80) at offset+4 for text/binary mode:\n\n   BINARY MODE (flag clear):\n   7a. Call WriteFile with raw buffer and count\n   7b. On success, store bytes written; on failure, get last error\n   7c. If bytes written > 0, return dwBytesWritten - nCrLfConversions\n\n   TEXT MODE (flag set):\n   7d. Initialize source cursor to input buffer\n   7e. Loop while bytes remain:\n       - Copy chars to 1024-byte local buffer\n       - Convert LF (0x0A) to CR+LF (0x0D 0x0A), incrementing nCrLfConversions\n       - When local buffer full (0x400 bytes), call WriteFile\n       - Accumulate bytes written; on WriteFile failure, goto error handling\n       - If partial write or all input consumed, exit loop\n   7f. After text conversion loop completes with no error, check FCTRLZ flag\n\n8. Error handling at LAB_6fa15677:\n   - If dwBytesWritten > 0, return dwBytesWritten - nCrLfConversions\n   - If no error (dwLastError == 0), goto FCTRLZ check\n   - If ACCESS_DENIED (0x5), set errno=EBADF(9), _doserrno=5\n   - Otherwise call CRT_MapDosErrorToErrno to map DOS error\n\n9. At LAB_6fa156e9 (zero bytes written, no error):\n   - If FCTRLZ flag (0x40) set and first char is Ctrl+Z (0x1A), return 0\n   - Otherwise set errno=ENOSPC(0x1C), _doserrno=0, return -1\n\nParameters:\n  nFileHandle (int): CRT file descriptor (not Win32 HANDLE). Used to index\n                     into g_apIobBlocks table: bucket = fd >> 5, entry = fd & 0x1F\n  pchBuffer (char *): Source buffer containing bytes to write\n  dwByteCount (uint): Number of bytes to write from buffer\n\nReturns:\n  >= 0: Number of bytes actually written to underlying file (excludes CR bytes\n        added during text mode LF->CRLF conversion)\n  -1: Error occurred, errno and _doserrno set appropriately\n\nIOB Entry Structure (size 0x24 = 36 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x00    4     hFile         Win32 HANDLE for file\n  0x04    1     bFlags        File mode flags\n                              0x20 = FAPPEND (append mode)\n                              0x40 = FCTRLZ (Ctrl+Z handling)\n                              0x80 = FTEXT (text mode, LF->CRLF)\n\nFlag Bits (offset +4 in IOB entry):\n  0x20 - FAPPEND: Append mode, seek to EOF before each write\n  0x40 - FCTRLZ: Stop read at Ctrl+Z (0x1A), treat as logical EOF for text files\n  0x80 - FTEXT: Text mode, convert LF to CR+LF on write\n\nError Codes:\n  errno=9 (EBADF): Bad file descriptor (ACCESS_DENIED from WriteFile)\n  errno=0x1C (ENOSPC): No space left on device (no bytes written, no error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero byte count returns 0 immediately without accessing IOB\n  - Ctrl+Z (0x1A) at start with FCTRLZ flag returns 0 (logical EOF marker)\n  - Partial WriteFile results exit early with accumulated count\n  - Text mode uses 1024-byte intermediate buffer for CR insertion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
