      "name": "CRT_isatty",
      "signature": "byte CRT_isatty(uint dwFileHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Checks if a file handle refers to a TTY (terminal/console) device.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate handle is within valid range (< g_dwMaxIobHandles)\n2. If out of range, return 0 (not a TTY)\n3. Calculate IOB block index: bucket = handle >> 5, offset = handle & 0x1F\n4. Index into g_apIobBlocks array to get the IOB entry block pointer\n5. Calculate entry address: block + (offset * 0x24) + 4\n6. Read the file flags byte from the IOB entry\n7. Return bit 6 (0x40) - the FDEV flag indicating device/TTY\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileHandle (uint) - File descriptor/handle to check\n\nReturns:\n  byte - 0x40 if handle is a TTY device, 0 otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 for handles >= g_dwMaxIobHandles (invalid range)\n  - Returns 0 for files that are not character devices\n\nStructure Layout (IOB Entry, 0x24 bytes per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n  0x00    4     osHandle    uint    OS file handle\n  0x04    1     flags       byte    File status flags (bit 6 = FDEV/TTY)\n  ...\n\nFlag Bits (flags byte at offset +4):\n  0x40 - FDEV: File is a character device (TTY/console)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1F - Mask for within-bucket index (32 entries per bucket)\n  0x05 - Shift for bucket index calculation (>> 5 = / 32)\n  0x24 - IOB entry stride (36 bytes per file descriptor entry)\n  0x40 - FDEV flag mask for TTY detection",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
