      "name": "CrtLockFileStream",
      "signature": "void CrtLockFileStream(uint dwFileStreamPtr)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Acquires lock on a file stream for thread-safe access.\n\nThis function implements CRT file stream locking by selecting the appropriate\nlocking mechanism based on whether the stream is in the static IOB table\nor is a dynamically allocated stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pFileStream is within the static IOB table range [0x6fa1e0f8, 0x6fa1e358)\n2. If in IOB table range:\n   a. Calculate index: (pFileStream - 0x6fa1e0f8) >> 5 (divide by 32-byte stride)\n   b. Add 0x1c (28) to get critical section index\n   c. Call CrtEnterCriticalSection with calculated index\n3. If outside IOB table (dynamic stream):\n   a. The stream has an embedded CRITICAL_SECTION at offset +0x20\n   b. Call EnterCriticalSection directly on that embedded lock\n\nParameters:\n  pFileStream (uint) - Pointer to file stream structure (FILE/IOB).\n      For static streams: address within g_aIobTable [0x6fa1e0f8, 0x6fa1e358)\n      For dynamic streams: pointer to heap-allocated stream with lock at +0x20\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Static IOB streams use indexed CRT critical sections (lazy-initialized)\n  - Dynamic streams have their own embedded CRITICAL_SECTION at offset +0x20\n  - The IOB table holds 19 entries (0x260 bytes / 32 bytes per entry)\n  - Critical section indices for IOB start at 0x1c (28)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6fa1e0f8 - g_aIobTable start address (g_pRuntimeErrorTableEnd label)\n  0x6fa1e358 - g_aIobTable end address (exclusive)\n  0x905e1f08 - Two's complement of 0x6fa1e0f8 for subtraction via addition\n  0x5 - Shift amount for dividing by 32 (IOB entry size)\n  0x1c - Base critical section index (28) for IOB stream locks\n  0x20 - Offset to embedded CRITICAL_SECTION in dynamic streams\n\nRelated Functions:\n  CrtUnlockFileStream (FUN_6fa15895) - Companion unlock function\n  CrtEnterCriticalSection - Acquires indexed CRT lock\n  EnterCriticalSection - Win32 API for direct lock acquisition",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
