      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Acquires a lock on a file stream for thread-safe I/O operations.\n\nThis function provides locking for CRT file streams. It selects the appropriate\nlocking mechanism based on whether the stream index is in the internal stream\ntable (indices 0-19) or is a dynamically allocated stream (indices >= 20).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if stream index is less than 0x14 (20)\n2. If index < 20 (internal stream):\n   a. Calculate critical section index as (nStreamIndex + 0x1c)\n   b. Call CrtEnterCriticalSection to acquire the internal lock\n3. If index >= 20 (dynamic stream):\n   a. Use embedded critical section at offset 0x20 in stream context\n   b. Call EnterCriticalSection directly on the embedded lock\n\nParameters:\n  nStreamIndex (int) - Index of the file stream in the CRT stream table.\n      Values 0-19 use internal critical sections; values >= 20 use embedded locks.\n  pStreamContext (int) - Pointer to stream context structure containing embedded\n      CRITICAL_SECTION at offset 0x20. Only used when nStreamIndex >= 20.\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function acquires lock and returns; does not indicate success/failure.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Internal streams (index 0-19): Use g_apCrtCriticalSections[index + 0x1c]\n  - Dynamic streams (index >= 20): Use pStreamContext->CriticalSection at +0x20\n  - Paired with CrtUnlockFileStreamByIndex to release the acquired lock\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14 (20) - Threshold between internal and dynamic streams\n  0x1c (28) - Offset added to stream index for critical section array lookup\n  0x20 (32) - Offset to embedded CRITICAL_SECTION in stream context structure\n\nRelated Functions:\n  CrtUnlockFileStreamByIndex - Releases lock acquired by this function\n  CrtEnterCriticalSection - Internal CRT lock acquisition with lazy init",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
