      "name": "CrtUnlockFileStream",
      "signature": "void CrtUnlockFileStream(void * pFileStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Unlocks the critical section associated with a file stream.\n\nThis is a CRT internal utility function that releases the lock acquired by\nCrtLockFileStream. It handles both internal CRT streams (using indexed critical\nsections) and external streams (using embedded CRITICAL_SECTION).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load stream address from stack parameter\n2. Compare against internal stream table bounds (0x6fa1e0f8 - 0x6fa1e358)\n3. If address within internal table range:\n   a. Calculate critical section index: ((addr - 0x6fa1e0f8) >> 5) + 0x1c\n   b. Call CrtLeaveCriticalSection with calculated index\n   c. Return\n4. If address outside internal table (external stream):\n   a. Add 0x20 offset to get embedded CRITICAL_SECTION address\n   b. Call Windows LeaveCriticalSection API\n   c. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pFileStream (void *) - Address of the file stream structure. Can be either:\n    - Internal CRT stream (within 0x6fa1e0f8 - 0x6fa1e358 range)\n    - External stream with embedded CRITICAL_SECTION at +0x20\n    Note: void* used because CRT internal stream type is opaque\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x6fa1e0f8 - Start of internal CRT stream table (g_CrtIobTable)\n  0x6fa1e358 - End of internal CRT stream table (exclusive)\n  0x20       - Offset to embedded CRITICAL_SECTION in external stream structure\n  0x1c (28)  - Base critical section index for internal streams\n  >> 5       - Divide by 32 (internal stream entry size is 32 bytes)\n\nControl Flow:\n  Entry -> Range check -> [Internal path: calc index, CrtLeaveCriticalSection]\n                      -> [External path: LeaveCriticalSection at +0x20]\n\nRelated Functions:\n  CrtLockFileStream - Companion lock function\n  CrtLeaveCriticalSection - Internal CRT critical section leave (index-based)\n  LeaveCriticalSection - Windows API for external streams",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
