      "name": "CrtUnlockFileStreamByIndex",
      "signature": "void CrtUnlockFileStreamByIndex(int nStreamIndex, int nStreamContextPtr)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Unlocks a file stream's critical section by stream index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if stream index is less than 0x14 (20 - standard CRT stream count)\n2. If standard stream (index < 20):\n   - Calculate critical section index: nStreamIndex + 0x1c (28)\n   - Call CrtLeaveCriticalSection with the calculated index\n   - Return immediately after unlocking\n3. If extended stream (index >= 20):\n   - Calculate embedded critical section address: pStreamContext + 0x20\n   - Call Win32 LeaveCriticalSection directly on the embedded CRITICAL_SECTION\n   - Return after unlocking\n\nParameters:\n- nStreamIndex (int): Zero-based index into the CRT file stream table.\n  Values 0-19 use the static critical section table (g_apCrtCriticalSections).\n  Values >= 20 indicate dynamically allocated streams with embedded locks.\n- pStreamContext (int): Pointer to the stream context structure (FILE-like).\n  Only used when nStreamIndex >= 20. Contains embedded CRITICAL_SECTION at offset +0x20.\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value. Function always succeeds if called with valid parameters.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Must be paired with CrtLockFileStreamByIndex for proper lock/unlock semantics\n- Standard streams (stdin=0, stdout=1, stderr=2) use indices in the 0-19 range\n- The offset 0x1c (28) maps stream indices to critical section indices in the global table\n- The offset 0x20 (32) is the location of CRITICAL_SECTION in dynamic stream structures\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Maximum count of standard CRT file streams\n- 0x1c (28): Base offset into g_apCrtCriticalSections for stream locking\n- 0x20 (32): Offset of embedded CRITICAL_SECTION in dynamic stream context\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CrtLockFileStreamByIndex: Corresponding lock function (must be called first)\n- CrtUnlockFileStream: Unlocks by stream pointer instead of index\n- CrtLeaveCriticalSection: Internal wrapper for static critical sections",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
