      "name": "CrtWideCharToMultiByteLocale",
      "signature": "char * CrtWideCharToMultiByteLocale(char * lpszDest, short sWideChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Thread-safe wrapper for wide character to multibyte conversion using locale settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment locale lock reference count (InterlockedIncrement on g_nLocaleLockRefCount)\n2. Check if multi-threaded locale mode is active (g_fLocaleMultiThreaded != 0)\n3. If multi-threaded: decrement ref count and enter critical section 0x13\n4. Call CrtWideCharToMultiByteInternal to perform actual conversion\n5. If multi-threaded: leave critical section 0x13\n6. If single-threaded: decrement ref count (InterlockedDecrement)\n7. Return converted string pointer\n\nParameters:\n  lpszDest (char *) - Destination buffer for multibyte output\n  sWideChar (short) - Wide character to convert\n\nReturns:\n  char * - Pointer to converted multibyte string in lpszDest\n           NULL on conversion failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Critical section 0x13 protects locale data in multi-threaded mode\n  Reference counting prevents locale changes during conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
