      "name": "CrtWideCharToMultiByteInternal",
      "signature": "char * CrtWideCharToMultiByteInternal(char * lpszDest, short nWideChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a wide character to multi-byte string using locale settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if destination buffer is NULL, return NULL if so\n2. Check if locale code page (g_dwLocaleCodePage) is set\n3. If no locale (code page == 0):\n   a. Check if character fits in single byte (< 0x100)\n   b. If fits, write directly to destination and return 1\n   c. If doesn't fit, fall through to error\n4. If locale is set:\n   a. Clear local flag variable for default char detection\n   b. Call WideCharToMultiByte with WC_NO_BEST_FIT_CHARS | WC_COMPOSITECHECK (0x220)\n   c. If conversion succeeded and no default char was used, return byte count\n   d. Otherwise fall through to error\n5. On error: Set errno to ERANGE (0x2a) and return -1\n\nParameters:\n- lpszDest (char *): Destination buffer for multi-byte output\n- nWideChar (short): Wide character to convert (treated as wchar_t)\n\nReturns:\n- NULL (0): If lpszDest is NULL\n- 1: Single-byte character written directly\n- >0: Number of bytes written by WideCharToMultiByte\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): Conversion failed, errno set to ERANGE (0x2a)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL destination returns NULL immediately without error\n- Characters < 0x100 written directly when no locale set\n- Uses WC_NO_BEST_FIT_CHARS (0x200) | WC_COMPOSITECHECK (0x20) = 0x220\n- Default char usage detection via lpUsedDefaultChar parameter\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n- g_dwLocaleCodePage (0x6fa3eacc): Locale code page flag (0 = no locale)\n- g_dwDefaultCodePage (0x6fa3eadc): Code page for WideCharToMultiByte\n- g_nLocaleVersion (0x6fa1e028): Buffer size for conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:12dead7d93dd2763acf5540fd9895c41",
