      "name": "CrtFreeMemory",
      "signature": "void CrtFreeMemory(void * pMemory)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Deallocates memory from CRT heap based on heap type configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return immediately if pMemory is NULL (null pointer check)\n2. If g_dwCrtHeapType == 3 (region-based heap):\n   a. Enter critical section 9 for thread safety\n   b. Call FindHeapRegion to locate memory region containing pMemory\n   c. If region found, call FreeRegionBlock to coalesce and free block\n   d. Exit critical section\n   e. If region found, return (freed via region allocator)\n3. If g_dwCrtHeapType == 2 (small block heap):\n   a. Enter critical section 9 for thread safety\n   b. Call FindSmallBlockHeader to locate block in small block heap\n   c. If block found, call FreeSmallBlock to return block to pool\n   d. Exit critical section (via CrtUnlockHeapCriticalSection2)\n   e. If block found, return (freed via small block allocator)\n4. Fall through to HeapFree for default heap deallocation\n\nParameters:\n  pMemory - Pointer to memory block to free (void *)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer: Returns immediately without error\n  - Type 3 heap: Uses region-based coalescing allocator\n  - Type 2 heap: Uses small block pooled allocator\n  - Default: Uses Win32 HeapFree on g_hCrtHeap\n\nSEH Frame:\n  Uses structured exception handling with scope table at 0x6fa19758\n  and filter function at 0x6fa16460\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwCrtHeapType @ 0x6fa3ffc8 - Heap implementation type (2 or 3)\n  g_hCrtHeap @ 0x6fa3ffc4 - Win32 heap handle for fallback",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
