      "name": "CrtUnlockHeapCriticalSection",
      "signature": "void CrtUnlockHeapCriticalSection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Releases the CRT heap critical section lock.\n\nWrapper function that calls CrtLeaveCriticalSection with hardcoded index 9\n(heap critical section). Called after heap memory operations complete to\nrelease exclusive access to internal heap tracking structures.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - wraps CrtLeaveCriticalSection(9)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push critical section index 9 onto stack\n2. Call CrtLeaveCriticalSection to release the lock\n3. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nCaller Context:\n- CrtFreeMemory: Called after heap tracking structure updates complete\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CrtEnterCriticalSection(9): Acquires this same lock before heap operations\n- CrtLeaveCriticalSection: Generic critical section release function\n- CrtUnlockHeapCriticalSection2: Similar wrapper for alternate heap type\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 9: Heap critical section index in g_apCrtCriticalSections array\n\nThread Safety:\n- Must be called only after CrtEnterCriticalSection(9) was called\n- Releases exclusive access to heap tracking data structures",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
