      "signature": "void CrtUnlockHeapCriticalSection2(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Releases the CRT heap critical section lock for heap type 2 code path.\n\nThunk/Wrapper function that calls CrtLeaveCriticalSection with hardcoded index 9\n(heap critical section). Called after heap memory operations complete in the\nheap type 2 (g_dwCrtHeapType == 2) code path to release exclusive access.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - wraps CrtLeaveCriticalSection(9)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push critical section index 9 onto stack\n2. Call CrtLeaveCriticalSection to release the lock\n3. Clean up stack (POP ECX) and return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nCaller Context:\n- CrtFreeMemory: Called after FUN_6fa17824 completes when g_dwCrtHeapType == 2\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CrtEnterCriticalSection(9): Acquires this same lock before heap operations\n- CrtLeaveCriticalSection: Generic critical section release function\n- CrtUnlockHeapCriticalSection: Identical wrapper used in heap type 3 path\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 9: Heap critical section index in g_apCrtCriticalSections array\n- 0x9 at 6fa15aef: PUSH immediate for critical section index\n\nThread Safety:\n- Must be called only after CrtEnterCriticalSection(9) was called\n- Releases exclusive access to heap tracking data structures\n- Failure to call after lock acquisition causes deadlock",
