      "name": "CrtAllocateMemory",
      "signature": "void CrtAllocateMemory(uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT Memory Allocator - Multi-Strategy Heap Allocation\n\nAllocates memory using one of three strategies based on g_dwCrtHeapType:\n- Type 3: Uses custom block allocator via FUN_6fa170bc for small allocations\n- Type 2: Uses 16-byte aligned small block heap via FUN_6fa17869\n- Fallback: Uses HeapAlloc with g_hCrtHeap handle\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup SEH frame for exception handling\n2. Check g_dwCrtHeapType value (3, 2, or other)\n3. If type 3 and size <= g_dwType3MaxAllocSize:\n   a. Enter critical section 9\n   b. Call FUN_6fa170bc with raw size\n   c. Unlock heap section\n   d. Return if allocation succeeded\n4. If type 2 and size <= g_dwType2MaxAllocSize:\n   a. Align size to 16-byte boundary (min 16)\n   b. Enter critical section 9  \n   c. Call FUN_6fa17869 with aligned_size/16\n   d. Unlock heap section 2\n   e. Return if allocation succeeded\n5. Fallback path: align size to 16 bytes (min 1), call HeapAlloc\n6. Restore SEH frame and return\n\nParameters:\n  dwSize (uint) - Number of bytes to allocate\n\nReturns:\n  Result stored in EAX from sub-allocators or HeapAlloc (void discarded by prototype)\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwCrtHeapType (0x6fa3ffc8) - Heap strategy selector (2=small block, 3=block)\n  g_hCrtHeap (0x6fa3ffc4) - Win32 heap handle for fallback\n  g_dwType3MaxAllocSize (0x6fa3ed70) - Max size for type 3 allocator\n  g_dwType2MaxAllocSize (0x6fa20554) - Max size for type 2 allocator\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero-size requests: Type 2 uses 16 bytes minimum, fallback uses 1 byte minimum\n  - All strategies align to 16-byte boundary except type 3 raw pass-through\n\nSEH Frame Layout:\n  Offset  Field               Purpose\n  -0x14   pPrevExceptionList  Saved FS:[0] exception chain\n  -0x10   Exception handler   LAB_6fa16460\n  -0x0C   Exception data      DAT_6fa19770\n  -0x08   nSehTryLevel        Try level (-1=none, 0=type3, 1=type2)",
