      "name": "CrtUnlockHeapAllocSection",
      "signature": "void CrtUnlockHeapAllocSection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases the heap allocation critical section lock (index 9).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CrtLeaveCriticalSection with index 9 to release the lock\n2. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Must be called after CrtEnterCriticalSection(9) / CrtLockHeapAllocSection\n- Used by CrtAllocateMemory to protect heap type 3 (small block) allocations\n- Pairs with CrtLockHeapAllocSection which acquires the same lock\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 9: Critical section index for heap allocation protection (g_apCrtCriticalSections[9])\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CrtLockHeapAllocSection: Acquires this same lock\n- CrtLeaveCriticalSection: Generic critical section release\n- CrtAllocateMemory: Caller that uses this for thread-safe heap operations",
