      "name": "CrtUnlockHeapAllocSection2",
      "signature": "void CrtUnlockHeapAllocSection2(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases the heap allocation critical section lock (section index 9).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push critical section index 9 onto stack\n2. Call CrtLeaveCriticalSection to release the lock\n3. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Must be called after CrtLockHeapAllocSection2 to release the lock\n  - Called by CrtAllocateMemory after heap operations complete\n  - Critical section 9 is the heap allocation synchronization primitive\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - CrtLockHeapAllocSection2: Acquires this lock\n  - CrtAllocateMemory: Caller that uses lock/unlock pair\n  - CrtLeaveCriticalSection: Underlying lock release implementation",
