      "name": "CrtCallocMemory",
      "signature": "void * CrtCallocMemory(uint nElementCount, uint nElementSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT calloc implementation - allocates zero-initialized memory for array of elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute total allocation size: nElementCount * nElementSize\n2. Check for overflow (result >= 0xFFFFFFE1 indicates overflow)\n3. If size is zero, allocate minimum 1 byte\n4. Align allocation size to 16-byte boundary: (size + 15) & ~15\n5. Enter allocation loop (for new handler retry support)\n6. If heap type 3 (small block heap) and size <= g_dwType3MaxAllocSize:\n   a. Enter critical section\n   b. Allocate from small block heap via FUN_6fa170bc\n   c. Leave critical section\n   d. If successful, zero memory and return\n7. Else if heap type 2 (region heap) and aligned size <= g_dwType2MaxAllocSize:\n   a. Enter critical section\n   b. Allocate from region heap via FUN_6fa17869 using (size >> 4) as block count\n   c. Leave critical section\n   d. If successful, zero memory and return\n8. Fall back to HeapAlloc with HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag (0x8)\n9. If allocation failed and new handler registered (g_pfnNewHandler != 0):\n   a. Call new handler FUN_6fa17fa6\n   b. If handler returns success, retry allocation from step 5\n10. Return allocated pointer or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n  nElementCount (uint) - Number of elements to allocate\n  nElementSize (uint) - Size of each element in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  void * - Pointer to zero-initialized memory block, or NULL on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Overflow check: size >= 0xFFFFFFE1 returns NULL\n  - Zero size: allocates minimum 1 byte\n  - All allocations are 16-byte aligned\n  - Uses SEH for heap operation protection\n\nHeap Type Strategy:\n  Type 3: Small block allocator for allocations <= g_dwType3MaxAllocSize\n  Type 2: Region allocator for allocations <= g_dwType2MaxAllocSize\n  Fallback: Standard HeapAlloc with HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
