      "name": "CrtUnlockHeapType3",
      "signature": "void CrtUnlockHeapType3(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases the CRT heap type 3 allocator critical section (index 9).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push critical section index 9 onto stack\n2. Call CrtLeaveCriticalSection to release lock\n3. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n  None - Uses hardcoded critical section index 9\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  SEH Cleanup Handler - Called through SEH filter mechanism in CrtCallocMemory\n  when local_8 = 0 (heap type 3 path) to ensure lock release on exceptions.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  9 - Critical section index for heap type 3 allocator (SBHEAP)\n      Acquired by CrtEnterCriticalSection(9) in CrtCallocMemory heap type 3 path\n\nRelated Functions:\n  CrtEnterCriticalSection(9) - Acquires this lock\n  CrtLeaveCriticalSection - Generic unlock wrapper\n  CrtCallocMemory - Caller that uses this for SEH-safe unlock",
