      "name": "CrtLeaveType2CriticalSection",
      "signature": "void CrtLeaveType2CriticalSection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases critical section 9 used for type 2 CRT heap allocations.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Dedicated cleanup function for type 2 allocation critical section.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CrtLeaveCriticalSection with hardcoded index 9\n2. Return to caller\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nCaller Context:\nCalled exclusively from CrtCallocMemory after type 2 allocation operations complete.\nCritical section 9 protects type 2 heap allocation pool (g_dwCrtHeapType == 2).\nMust be called after CrtEnterCriticalSection(9) to avoid deadlock.\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CrtEnterCriticalSection(9): Acquires this same lock before type 2 allocations\n- FUN_6fa15ce9: Equivalent function for type 3 allocation critical section cleanup\n- CrtLeaveCriticalSection: Generic wrapper that performs actual LeaveCriticalSection call",
