      "name": "StrCSpn",
      "signature": "int StrCSpn(char * lpszString, char * lpszCharset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "StrCSpn - Returns length of initial segment of string not containing any charset characters\n\nImplementation of C runtime strcspn function. Scans lpszString returning the index\nof the first character found in lpszCharset, or string length if none found.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 32-byte (256-bit) bitmap on stack, initialize all bits to 0\n2. Build charset bitmap: for each char in lpszCharset, set bit at position char_code\n   - BTS [ESP], EAX sets bit EAX in the 256-bit bitmap\n3. Scan string: for each char in lpszString starting at index 0\n   - BT [ESP], EAX tests if bit EAX is set in bitmap\n   - If bit set (char in charset), return current index\n   - If null terminator, return current index\n   - Otherwise increment index and continue\n4. Return index (count of characters not in charset)\n\nParameters:\n  lpszString - Pointer to null-terminated string to scan\n  lpszCharset - Pointer to null-terminated set of characters to find\n\nReturns:\n  int - Index of first character in lpszString that exists in lpszCharset,\n        or length of lpszString if no match found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty charset (lpszCharset[0] == 0): Returns length of entire string\n- Empty string (lpszString[0] == 0): Returns 0\n- Null character never in charset: Null terminator always stops scan\n\nBit Operations:\n- Bitmap index: char_code >> 3 (byte index 0-31)\n- Bit position: char_code & 7 (bit 0-7 within byte)\n- BTS: Bit Test and Set - atomically test and set bit\n- BT: Bit Test - test bit without modification\n\nNo callers detected - orphan function (possibly dead code or called via pointer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
