      "name": "CrtStrPbrk",
      "signature": "byte * CrtStrPbrk(byte * pbString, byte * pbControlChars)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT strpbrk - Find first occurrence of any control character in string.\n\nScans pbString for the first byte that matches any byte in pbControlChars.\nUses a 256-bit bitmap (32 bytes) on stack for O(1) character lookup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 32-byte bitmap on stack to zero (8 PUSH EAX = 32 bytes)\n2. Loop through pbControlChars, set bit for each character using BTS instruction\n   - Bit index = character value (0-255)\n   - BTS [ESP], EAX sets bit EAX in bitmap\n3. Loop through pbString, test each character against bitmap using BT instruction\n   - BT [ESP], EAX tests if bit EAX is set\n   - If set (CF=1), character matches - return pointer to it\n   - If clear (CF=0), continue scanning\n4. If null terminator reached in pbString, return NULL (0)\n\nParameters:\n  pbString - Input string to search (null-terminated)\n  pbControlChars - Control characters to find (null-terminated)\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to first matching character in pbString\n  NULL (0) if no match found\n\nPerformance:\n  O(n+m) where n=len(pbString), m=len(pbControlChars)\n  Uses 32 bytes stack for bitmap lookup table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
