      "comment": "CRT strcpy implementation - Copy null-terminated string to destination buffer.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - Entry point that jumps into copy loop of CrtStrcat.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EDI register (caller-saved)\n2. Load destination pointer (lpszDest) into EDI from stack\n3. Jump directly to copy loop at 0x6fa15f51 (shared with CrtStrcat)\n4. Copy loop handles DWORD-aligned fast copy with null terminator detection\n5. Return original destination pointer in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  lpszDest (char *) - Destination buffer, must be large enough for source + null\n  lpcszSrc (char *) - Source null-terminated string to copy\n\nReturns:\n  char * - Returns lpszDest (original destination pointer)\n\nImplementation Notes:\n- Shares copy loop code with CrtStrcat (FUN_6fa15ef0) starting at 0x6fa15f51\n- Uses DWORD-at-a-time copy with magic constant 0x7efefeff for null detection\n- Byte-by-byte copy used for alignment and final bytes\n- Classic Microsoft CRT strcpy optimization pattern\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7efefeff - Null byte detection constant for DWORD scanning\n  0x81010100 - Mask for detecting null byte in any position of DWORD\n\nCallers:\n  DisplayCrtRuntimeErrorMessage - Error message string copying\n  CrtSetupEnvironmentArray - Environment string duplication",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
