      "name": "CRT_strcat",
      "signature": "uint * CRT_strcat(char * lpszDest, char * lpcszSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT_strcat - String concatenation (ANSI)\n\nAppends the source string to the end of the destination string. Uses optimized\nDWORD-aligned reading with null-byte detection magic for performance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align destination pointer to DWORD boundary, scanning byte-by-byte\n2. Scan destination DWORD-at-a-time using null detection: (val ^ ~0 ^ val + 0x7efefeff) & 0x81010100\n3. When null detected, determine exact byte position (byte 0-3 in DWORD)\n4. Set pszEnd to null terminator position in destination\n5. Align source pointer to DWORD boundary, copying byte-by-byte\n6. Copy source DWORD-at-a-time until null detected\n7. Copy final partial DWORD including null terminator\n\nParameters:\n  lpszDest - Destination string buffer (must have space for concatenated result)\n  lpcszSrc - Source string to append (null-terminated)\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to destination string (lpszDest)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x7efefeff - Null byte detection constant (causes carry propagation on null)\n  0x81010100 - Mask to detect carry bits indicating null byte presence\n  0x3 - Alignment mask for DWORD boundary check\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty source string: Only null terminator copied\n  - Source shorter than 4 bytes: Handles 1-3 byte copies correctly\n  - Unaligned pointers: Falls back to byte-by-byte until aligned",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:845fc5044ff181fe96e2ae868d3aa1f6",
