      "name": "CRT_memmove",
      "signature": "void * CRT_memmove(void * pDest, void * pSrc, uint nCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT_memmove - Copy memory with overlapping region handling\n\nStandard C library memmove implementation. Copies nCount bytes from pSrc to pDest,\ncorrectly handling the case where source and destination memory regions overlap.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check for overlap: If (pSrc < pDest < pSrc + nCount), regions overlap with dest after src\n2. For overlapping regions (backward copy needed):\n   a. Start from end of both buffers (pSrc + nCount - 4, pDest + nCount - 4)\n   b. Align destination to 4-byte boundary by copying 1-3 trailing bytes\n   c. Copy aligned DWORDs in reverse using REP MOVSD with STD (direction flag set)\n   d. Copy remaining 0-3 bytes at front\n3. For non-overlapping or dest < src (forward copy safe):\n   a. Align destination to 4-byte boundary by copying 1-3 leading bytes\n   b. Copy aligned DWORDs forward using REP MOVSD\n   c. Copy remaining 0-3 bytes at end\n4. Small copies (< 8 DWORDs) use unrolled switch-case copy for efficiency\n5. Return original pDest pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pDest  - void *: Destination buffer pointer\n  pSrc   - void *: Source buffer pointer (may overlap with pDest)\n  nCount - uint: Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n  void * - Original pDest pointer (for chaining)\n\nOptimization Notes:\n- Uses 4-byte alignment for DWORD-aligned copies via REP MOVSD\n- Unrolled Duff's device style switch for small counts (0-7 DWORDs)\n- STD/CLD direction flag manipulation for backward copies\n- Jump tables at 0x6fa16118, 0x6fa160ac, 0x6fa16030, 0x6fa16128 for dispatch\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero-length copy: Returns pDest immediately\n- Non-overlapping: Uses faster forward copy\n- Overlapping with dest > src: Uses reverse copy to preserve data",
