      "name": "SaveSehUnwindContext",
      "signature": "void SaveSehUnwindContext(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Saves SEH exception handler context to global structure for local unwinding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EBX and ECX registers (caller-save preservation)\n2. Load base address of g_SehUnwindContext into EBX\n3. Store scope table pointer [EBP+8] to g_SehUnwindContext.pScopeTable (offset +8)\n4. Store handler context (EAX) to g_SehUnwindContext.pHandlerContext (offset +4)\n5. Store frame pointer (EBP) to g_SehUnwindContext.pFramePointer (offset +0xC)\n6. Restore EBX and ECX, return with stack cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT in_EAX - Exception handler context pointer passed from __local_unwind2\n  IMPLICIT [EBP+8] - Scope table pointer from caller's stack frame\n  IMPLICIT EBP - Frame pointer of exception handler being unwound\n\nReturns:\n  void - Context saved to g_SehUnwindContext global structure\n\nStructure Layout (SehUnwindContext at 0x6fa1e420):\n  Offset  Size  Field            Type    Description\n  0x00    4     dwReserved       uint    Reserved/unused\n  0x04    4     pHandlerContext  void*   Exception handler context (from EAX)\n  0x08    4     pScopeTable      void*   Scope table pointer (from [EBP+8])\n  0x0C    4     pFramePointer    void*   Frame pointer (from EBP)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Called only during SEH local unwinding by __local_unwind2\n  - Uses caller's EBP frame to access scope table at [EBP+8]\n  - RET 0x4 cleans 4 bytes from stack (stdcall with hidden param)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ed17ad9d511f6e330c2b6a62378d83cf",
