      "name": "SehLocalUnwindHandler",
      "signature": "void SehLocalUnwindHandler(void * pExceptionRecord)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "SEH Local Unwind Handler - Performs local stack frame unwinding during exception handling.\n\nClassification: Internal callback - invoked by SEH runtime during exception unwinding\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Receive pointer to exception registration record on stack\n2. Load EBP from exception record base ([pExceptionRecord])\n3. Extract scope table pointer from offset +0x18\n4. Extract target trylevel from offset +0x1c\n5. Call __local_unwind2 with scope table and target trylevel\n6. Return to exception dispatcher\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionRecord (void *) - Pointer to EXCEPTION_REGISTRATION_RECORD structure\n    +0x00: Saved EBP frame pointer\n    +0x18: Scope table pointer for local unwind\n    +0x1c: Target trylevel to unwind to\n\nReturns:\n  void - Control returns to exception dispatcher\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Called during exception unwinding phase, not normal execution\n  - No direct callers - referenced via exception registration table\n  - EBP is restored from exception record to access local variables\n\nStructure Layout (EXCEPTION_REGISTRATION_RECORD extended):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n  0x00    4     SavedEBP        uint    Saved frame pointer\n  0x18    4     pScopeTable     int*    Scope table for __try blocks\n  0x1c    4     nTargetTrylevel int     Target __try level to unwind to",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:89d1b619054116ad559c7c543db397fd",
