      "name": "GetStringTypeWithCodePage",
      "signature": "BOOL GetStringTypeWithCodePage(DWORD dwInfoType, LPCSTR lpszSrcStr, int nSrcLen, LPWORD pwCharType, UINT dwCodePage, LCID dwLocaleId, int nComposeCheck)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Get string type information with automatic Unicode/ANSI mode detection.\n\nWrapper for GetStringTypeW/GetStringTypeA that automatically detects and caches\nwhether the system supports Unicode or ANSI string type APIs. On first call,\nprobes GetStringTypeW with empty string; if that fails, falls back to GetStringTypeA.\nThe detected mode is cached globally for subsequent calls.\n\nClassification: Internal CRT utility - locale-aware string type classification\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check cached g_nStringTypeMode (0=unknown, 1=Unicode, 2=ANSI)\n2. If unknown (first call):\n   a. Probe GetStringTypeW(CT_CTYPE1, L\"\", 1, &temp) for Unicode support\n   b. If Unicode supported: set mode=1\n   c. If Unicode failed: probe GetStringTypeA(0, CT_CTYPE1, \"\", 1, &temp)\n   d. If ANSI supported: set mode=2\n   e. If both fail: return FALSE\n3. Cache detected mode in g_nStringTypeMode\n4. If mode==2 (ANSI):\n   a. Default locale if dwLocaleId==0\n   b. Call GetStringTypeA directly with original parameters\n5. If mode==1 (Unicode):\n   a. Default code page if dwCodePage==0\n   b. Calculate wide char buffer size with MultiByteToWideChar\n   c. Allocate stack buffer via __alloca_probe\n   d. Zero-initialize buffer with _memset\n   e. Convert MBCS to Unicode with MultiByteToWideChar\n   f. Call GetStringTypeW on converted string\n6. Return API result or FALSE on failure\n\nParameters:\n  dwInfoType     - DWORD: Character type flags to retrieve (CT_CTYPE1=0x1, CT_CTYPE2=0x2, CT_CTYPE3=0x4)\n  lpszSrcStr     - LPCSTR: Multi-byte source string to analyze\n  nSrcLen        - int: Length of source string in bytes (-1 for null-terminated)\n  pwCharType     - LPWORD: Output buffer for character type flags (one WORD per character)\n  dwCodePage     - UINT: Code page for MBCS conversion (0 = use g_dwDefaultCodePage)\n  dwLocaleId     - LCID: Locale ID for ANSI mode (0 = use g_dwLocaleCodePage)\n  nComposeCheck  - int: If non-zero, use MB_COMPOSITE flag (0x8) in conversion\n\nReturns:\n  BOOL - TRUE if character types retrieved successfully, FALSE on failure\n\nGlobal Data:\n  g_nStringTypeMode   (0x6fa3ec5c) - Cached API mode: 0=unknown, 1=Unicode, 2=ANSI\n  g_dwDefaultCodePage (0x6fa3eadc) - Default code page for Unicode mode\n  g_dwLocaleCodePage  (0x6fa3eacc) - Default locale for ANSI mode\n\nCallers: GetCharTypeWithMask (character classification), FUN_6fa168d4 (char type table init)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a7046d73bbd286a50d5e7204509858d2",
