      "signature": "uint ResolveCodePageSpecifier(int nCodePageSpecifier)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Resolves special code page specifier constants to actual Windows code page values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear g_fCodePageIsDefault flag to 0\n2. Check if specifier is CP_OEMCP (-2):\n   - Set g_fCodePageIsDefault = 1\n   - Tail-call GetOEMCP() via IAT and return result\n3. Check if specifier is CP_ACP (-3):\n   - Set g_fCodePageIsDefault = 1\n   - Tail-call GetACP() via IAT and return result\n4. Check if specifier is CP_THREAD_ACP (-4):\n   - Load g_dwDefaultCodePage as resolved value\n   - Set g_fCodePageIsDefault = 1\n   - Return resolved code page\n5. Otherwise return specifier unchanged (explicit code page number)\n\nParameters:\n  nCodePageSpecifier - Code page specifier:\n                       -2 (CP_OEMCP): Use OEM code page\n                       -3 (CP_ACP): Use ANSI code page\n                       -4 (CP_THREAD_ACP): Use thread default code page\n                       >0: Explicit code page number (passed through)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Resolved Windows code page identifier (e.g., 437, 1252, 65001)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - g_fCodePageIsDefault set to 1 when using system defaults (-2, -3, -4)\n  - g_fCodePageIsDefault remains 0 when explicit code page is specified\n  - Tail-call optimization via indirect JMP for GetOEMCP/GetACP\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  -2 (0xFFFFFFFE): CP_OEMCP - OEM code page constant\n  -3 (0xFFFFFFFD): CP_ACP - ANSI code page constant\n  -4 (0xFFFFFFFC): CP_THREAD_ACP - Thread ANSI code page constant\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_fCodePageIsDefault (0x6fa3ec60): Flag indicating system default was used\n  g_dwDefaultCodePage (0x6fa3eadc): Thread default code page value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
