      "name": "GetLocaleIdFromCodePage",
      "signature": "uint GetLocaleIdFromCodePage(uint dwCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Maps East Asian code page numbers to Windows Locale Identifiers (LCIDs).\n\nA lookup table function that converts CJK (Chinese-Japanese-Korean) code page\nnumbers to their corresponding Windows locale IDs. Returns 0 for unrecognized\ncode pages, indicating no LCID mapping available.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare input code page against 932 (Japanese Shift-JIS)\n2. If match, return LCID 0x411 (Japanese)\n3. Compare against 936 (Simplified Chinese GB2312)\n4. If match, return LCID 0x804 (Chinese PRC)\n5. Compare against 949 (Korean EUC-KR)\n6. If match, return LCID 0x412 (Korean)\n7. Compare against 950 (Traditional Chinese Big5)\n8. If match, return LCID 0x404 (Chinese Taiwan)\n9. Return 0 for unknown code pages\n\nParameters:\n  dwCodePage [uint, in]: Code page identifier to look up\n    932 (0x3a4): Japanese Shift-JIS\n    936 (0x3a8): Simplified Chinese GB2312\n    949 (0x3b5): Korean EUC-KR\n    950 (0x3b6): Traditional Chinese Big5\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Windows Locale ID (LCID) for the code page\n    0x411 (1041): Japanese\n    0x804 (2052): Chinese (PRC)\n    0x412 (1042): Korean\n    0x404 (1028): Chinese (Taiwan)\n    0: Unknown/unsupported code page\n\nCode Page to LCID Mapping Table:\n  Code Page | Name              | LCID  | Locale\n  ----------+-------------------+-------+----------------\n  932       | Shift-JIS         | 0x411 | Japanese\n  936       | GB2312            | 0x804 | Chinese (PRC)\n  949       | EUC-KR            | 0x412 | Korean\n  950       | Big5              | 0x404 | Chinese (Taiwan)\n\nCalled By:\n  SetCodePageCharacterTypeTable - to get LCID for character type initialization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f31c6439952ca9c3e10694cce3d833df",
