      "name": "ClearCodePageCharacterTypeTable",
      "signature": "void ClearCodePageCharacterTypeTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Clears the code page character type table and resets all associated globals.\n\nCalled by SetCodePageCharacterTypeTable before setting up a new code page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero-fill 257 bytes (0x40 DWORDs + 1 byte) of g_abCharTypeTable at 0x6fa3eea0\n2. Clear g_dwCurrentCodePage at 0x6fa3ed74\n3. Clear g_dwCodePageLCID at 0x6fa3ed80\n4. Clear g_dwCodePageParam1 at 0x6fa3ed84\n5. Clear g_dwCodePageParam2 at 0x6fa3ed88\n6. Clear g_dwCodePageParam3 at 0x6fa3ed8c\n7. Clear g_fMultiByteCodePage at 0x6fa3efa4\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nMemory Layout Cleared:\n  0x6fa3eea0: g_abCharTypeTable[257] - Character type lookup table (0x101 bytes)\n  0x6fa3ed74: g_dwCurrentCodePage - Active code page ID\n  0x6fa3ed80: g_dwCodePageLCID - Locale ID for code page\n  0x6fa3ed84: g_dwCodePageParam1 - Code page parameter 1\n  0x6fa3ed88: g_dwCodePageParam2 - Code page parameter 2\n  0x6fa3ed8c: g_dwCodePageParam3 - Code page parameter 3  \n  0x6fa3efa4: g_fMultiByteCodePage - Multi-byte code page flag\n\nCaller: SetCodePageCharacterTypeTable (0x6fa16681)",
