      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT strtol implementation - converts string to signed long integer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push 0 (flags=0 for signed mode) as 5th parameter\n2. Push nBase, pplpszEndPtr, lpszString parameters\n3. Call CRT_StrToLongInternal with flags=0\n4. Clean up stack (16 bytes) and return result\n\nParameters:\n  lpszString (char *) - Input string to convert\n  pplpszEndPtr (char **) - Optional output pointer to first unconverted character\n  nBase (int) - Number base (0=auto-detect, 2-36 valid)\n\nReturns:\n  long - Converted value, or 0 on error with errno set to ERANGE on overflow\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - wraps CRT_StrToLongInternal with flags=0 for signed conversion\n\nCalled By:\n  CRT_SelectHeapImplementation - parses heap type number from environment variable",
