      "signature": "int CRT_StrToLongInternal(void * this, byte * pbInputStr, byte * * ppbEndPtr, int nRadix, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "CRT_StrToLongInternal - Internal string-to-long conversion with radix detection and overflow handling\n\nClassification: Internal utility - CRT worker function called by CRT_StrToLong\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace using locale-aware character type check (mask 0x08 = space)\n2. Parse optional sign character ('+' 0x2B or '-' 0x2D), set flag bit 2 if negative\n3. Validate radix: reject if < 0, == 1, or > 36 (0x24); return 0 with endptr = input\n4. Auto-detect radix if nRadix == 0:\n   - If first char '0' followed by 'x'/'X' -> hex (16)\n   - If first char '0' (not followed by x/X) -> octal (8)\n   - Otherwise -> decimal (10)\n5. Skip hex prefix \"0x\"/\"0X\" if radix is 16 and string starts with it\n6. Calculate maximum safe value before overflow: dwMaxSafe = 0xFFFFFFFF / nRadix\n7. Parse digit loop:\n   a. Check if character is digit (mask 0x04)\n   b. If digit: value = char - '0'\n   c. If not digit, check if hex letter (mask 0x103):\n      - If hex letter: convert to uppercase, value = char - 'A' + 10 (= char - 0x37)\n      - If neither: exit loop\n   d. If digit value >= radix: exit loop (invalid digit for base)\n   e. Overflow check: if accumulator > maxSafe or at boundary with overflow, set flag 4\n   f. Otherwise: accumulator = accumulator * radix + digitValue, set flag 8 (valid digit parsed)\n8. Finalize:\n   - Decrement pointer (went one past last valid)\n   - If no digits parsed (flag 8 not set): reset result to 0, set endptr to input start\n   - If overflow detected (flag 4) or result exceeds range: set errno = ERANGE (0x22)\n     - For unsigned (flag 1): return 0xFFFFFFFF\n     - For signed positive: return 0x7FFFFFFF (INT_MAX)\n     - For signed negative: return 0x80000000 (INT_MIN)\n9. Store final position to ppbEndPtr if not NULL\n10. If negative (flag 2 set): negate result before return\n\nParameters:\n  this         - Unused ECX (thiscall convention artifact)\n  pbInputStr   - Input string to parse\n  ppbEndPtr    - OUT: pointer to first unparsed character (may be NULL)\n  nRadix       - Number base (0 = auto-detect, 2-36 valid)\n  dwFlags      - Control flags:\n                 Bit 0 (0x01): Unsigned mode (return UINT_MAX on overflow)\n                 Bit 1 (0x02): Negative sign encountered\n                 Bit 2 (0x04): Overflow detected during accumulation\n                 Bit 3 (0x08): At least one valid digit parsed\n\nReturns:\n  Parsed integer value, or 0 if no valid digits\n  On overflow: returns range limit (INT_MAX, INT_MIN, or UINT_MAX)\n  Sets errno to ERANGE (0x22) on overflow\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty string or no digits: returns 0, endptr = start of string\n  - Leading whitespace: skipped\n  - Invalid radix (<0, ==1, >36): returns 0\n  - Overflow: errno = ERANGE, returns clamped value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2B = '+' character\n  0x2D = '-' character\n  0x30 = '0' character\n  0x37 = 'A' - 10 (for hex conversion: 'A'=0x41, 0x41-0x37=10)\n  0x58 = 'X' character\n  0x78 = 'x' character\n  0x22 = ERANGE errno value\n  0x04 = Character type mask for digit\n  0x08 = Character type mask for whitespace\n  0x103 = Character type mask for hex letter (alpha + xdigit)\n  0x24 = 36 (max valid radix)\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_nLocaleVersion - Locale system version (< 2 uses table lookup)\n  g_pCharTypeTable - Character classification table (locale-dependent)",
