      "name": "CRT_InitializeOldSBH",
      "signature": "int CRT_InitializeOldSBH(uint dwMaxBlockSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT Old Small Block Heap Initialization\n\nInitializes the Old Small Block Heap (SBH Type 3) data structures. Allocates\nthe heap region descriptor array from the CRT heap and sets initial state.\nCalled only when CRT_SelectHeapImplementation returns type 3.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x140 (320) bytes from g_hCrtHeap for region descriptor array\n2. If allocation fails, return 0 (failure)\n3. Initialize g_dwHeapRegionField64 to 0 (unknown purpose field)\n4. Initialize g_nHeapRegionCount to 0 (no regions allocated yet)\n5. Set g_pHeapRegionCursor to point to start of region array\n6. Store dwMaxBlockSize in g_dwType3MaxAllocSize (typically 0x3f8 = 1016 bytes)\n7. Set g_dwHeapRegionCapacity to 0x10 (16 initial region slots)\n8. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  dwMaxBlockSize (uint) - Maximum allocation size for Old SBH blocks\n    Typically 0x3f8 (1016 bytes) passed from CRT_InitializeHeapSystem\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Initialization succeeded, Old SBH ready for use\n  0 - HeapAlloc failed, caller should fall back or abort\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_pHeapRegionArray @ 0x6fa3ed6c - Pointer to heap region descriptor array\n  g_dwHeapRegionField64 @ 0x6fa3ed64 - Unknown field, cleared to 0\n  g_nHeapRegionCount @ 0x6fa3ed68 - Count of active heap regions (set to 0)\n  g_pHeapRegionCursor @ 0x6fa3ed60 - Current position in region array\n  g_dwType3MaxAllocSize @ 0x6fa3ed70 - Max block size for this heap type\n  g_dwHeapRegionCapacity @ 0x6fa3ed58 - Capacity of region array (16 slots)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x140 (320) - Size of heap region descriptor array allocation\n  0x10 (16) - Initial capacity for heap region descriptors\n  0x3f8 (1016) - Typical max block size passed by caller\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - HeapAlloc failure causes immediate return without cleanup (heap exists)\n  - Capacity of 16 regions can be expanded by FUN_6fa173c5 when exhausted",
