      "name": "FindHeapRegion",
      "signature": "void * FindHeapRegion(void * pAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Searches heap region array for region containing specified address.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Start with first region entry (pCurrentRegion = g_pHeapRegionArray)\n2. Calculate array end: base + count * 0x14 (20-byte stride per region)\n3. Loop through region entries:\n   a. If pCurrentRegion >= array end, address not found in any region\n   b. Get region base address from offset +0xc in current entry\n   c. Calculate offset: pAddress - regionBase\n   d. If offset < 0x100000 (1MB), address is within this region\n   e. Otherwise advance to next region entry (+0x14 bytes)\n4. Return matching region pointer or NULL (0) if not found\n\nParameters:\n  pAddress - Memory address to locate within heap regions (void *)\n\nReturns:\n  void * - Pointer to 20-byte region entry containing address\n  NULL (0) - Address not found in any tracked heap region\n\nStructure Layout (Region Entry - 0x14 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x00    4     (unknown)       Region field 0\n  0x04    4     (unknown)       Region field 1\n  0x08    4     (unknown)       Region field 2\n  0x0C    4     dwRegionBase    Base address of 1MB region\n  0x10    4     (unknown)       Region field 4\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_pHeapRegionArray @ 0x6fa3ed6c - Base pointer to region entry array\n  g_nHeapRegionCount @ 0x6fa3ed68 - Number of active heap regions\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14 (20)      - Size of each region entry in bytes\n  0x100000 (1MB) - Size of each heap region (address range check)\n  0x0C (12)      - Offset to region base address field",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
