      "name": "FreeRegionBlock",
      "signature": "void FreeRegionBlock(dword * pHeapRegion, int nBlockAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Frees a memory block and coalesces with adjacent free blocks in the custom heap.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate heap descriptor base (pHeapRegion[4]) and region index from block address\n2. Compute free list array pointer for this region (base + 0x144 + regionIndex * 0x204)\n3. Read block header and check if block is free (low bit clear)\n4. If next adjacent block is free:\n   a. Calculate bucket index from next block size (size >> 4) - 1, clamped to 0x3F\n   b. If block is alone in its free list bucket, clear bitmap bit\n   c. Coalesce: add next block size to current block size\n   d. Unlink next block from its free list (prev->next = next, next->prev = prev)\n5. Calculate new bucket index for coalesced block\n6. If previous adjacent block is free:\n   a. Move free block pointer back by previous block size\n   b. Calculate old bucket index from previous block size\n   c. If bucket changed and block alone in list, clear old bucket bitmap\n   d. Add previous block size to coalesced total\n   e. Unlink previous block from its free list\n7. Insert final coalesced block into appropriate free list bucket\n8. Update bucket bitmap and counter if block is first in bucket\n9. Store coalesced size in block header and footer\n10. Decrement region block count\n11. If region becomes empty:\n    a. Release previous cached empty region's virtual memory (VirtualFree with MEM_DECOMMIT)\n    b. Mark region as decommitted in region bitmap\n    c. If all region pages decommitted, release entire region (VirtualFree with MEM_RELEASE)\n    d. Free heap descriptor (HeapFree)\n    e. Remove region entry from array (memmove)\n    f. Cache this empty region for next potential release\n\nParameters:\n  pHeapRegion (param_1): Pointer to heap region descriptor array entry (5 DWORDs)\n    [0]: Low bucket bitmap (buckets 0-31)\n    [1]: High bucket bitmap (buckets 32-63)\n    [2]: Decommitted page bitmap\n    [3]: Base address of region memory\n    [4]: Pointer to heap descriptor structure\n  nBlockAddress (param_2): Address of user data being freed (points past block header)\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Block already in use (low bit set): Early return, no action\n  - Region empty after free: Virtual memory decommitted, descriptor may be freed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x8000 - Region page size (32KB)\n  0xF - Shift amount for region index (15 bits = 32KB pages)\n  0x204 - Size of per-region free list structure (64 buckets * 8 bytes + 4 byte count)\n  0x144 - Offset to first region's free list array in heap descriptor\n  0x44 - Offset to low bucket bitmaps array in heap descriptor\n  0xC4 - Offset to high bucket bitmaps array in heap descriptor\n  0x3F - Maximum bucket index (63, for 64 buckets)\n  0x20 - Bucket threshold for low/high bitmap (32)\n  0x80000000 - High bit for bitmap operations\n\nFree List Structure:\n  Each free block contains:\n    Offset 0: Size with flags (low bit = in-use)\n    Offset 4: Next pointer in free list\n    Offset 8: Previous pointer in free list\n    Footer at (block + size - 4): Copy of size for backward coalescing\n\nHeap Descriptor Layout:\n  Offset 0x04-0x43: Bucket counters (64 bytes, one per bucket)\n  Offset 0x44: Low bucket bitmaps per region\n  Offset 0xC4: High bucket bitmaps per region\n  Offset 0x144+: Per-region free list arrays",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
