      "name": "AllocateSmallBlockHeap",
      "signature": "void * AllocateSmallBlockHeap(uint dwRequestedSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Small Block Heap Allocator - Segregated Free List with Bitmap Management\n\nAllocates memory from a segregated free list heap organized by size classes (buckets).\nEach bucket contains blocks of sizes from 16 to 1024 bytes in 16-byte increments (64 buckets).\nUses two 32-bit bitmaps per region to track which size classes have free blocks available.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Round up requested size to 16-byte aligned allocation size: (size + 0x17) & 0xFFFFFFF0\n2. Calculate bucket index from aligned size: (aligned_size >> 4) - 1, capped at 63\n3. Create bitmask pair (low/high 32-bit) for bucket search based on index\n4. Search Phase A: Scan from g_pHeapRegionCursor to end of region array for matching bitmask\n5. Search Phase B: If not found, scan from array start to cursor position\n6. Search Phase C: If no suitable block found, scan for regions with expandable space (field[2] != 0)\n7. Search Phase D: If still not found, scan from start for expandable regions\n8. If all searches fail: call CreateHeapRegion() to allocate new 1MB virtual region\n9. If new region needed: call InitializeBucketGroup() to initialize free lists and bitmaps\n10. Within selected region, find bucket group containing free blocks matching size class\n11. Search bucket bitmaps to find first non-empty bucket >= requested size\n12. Remove block from free list; if bucket becomes empty, clear bitmap bit\n13. Calculate leftover size after splitting block for allocation\n14. If leftover > 0: reinsert remainder into appropriate smaller bucket, update bitmaps\n15. Write allocation header (size | 0x1 marker) at both ends of allocated block\n16. Update region cursor for next allocation locality\n17. Return pointer to usable memory (header + 4)\n\nParameters:\n  dwRequestedSize (uint) - Number of bytes to allocate\n\nReturns:\n  void * - Pointer to allocated memory block, or NULL on failure\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_pHeapRegionArray (0x6fa3ed6c) - Array of heap region descriptors (20 bytes each)\n  g_nHeapRegionCount (0x6fa3ed68) - Number of active heap regions\n  g_pHeapRegionCursor (0x6fa3ed60) - Current position for allocation locality\n  g_pLastFreedHeapRegion (0x6fa3ed64) - Last region where block was freed\n  g_nLastFreedBucketIndex (0x6fa3ed5c) - Bucket index of last freed block\n\nHeap Region Descriptor Layout (20 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field\n  0x00    4     dwLowBitmask - Bits 0-31 indicate buckets 0-31 have free blocks\n  0x04    4     dwHighBitmask - Bits 0-31 indicate buckets 32-63 have free blocks\n  0x08    4     dwExpandableFlag - Non-zero if region has uninit bucket groups\n  0x0C    4     pVirtualMemory - Base address of 1MB virtual allocation\n  0x10    4     pBucketData - Pointer to bucket management structure (0x41C4 bytes)\n\nBucket Data Structure Layout:\n  Offset    Size    Field\n  0x00      4       nCurrentBucketGroup - Active bucket group index (-1 = uninitialized)\n  0x04      64      abBucketRefCounts[64] - Reference count per bucket\n  0x44      32*4    adwGroupLowBitmaps[32] - Per-group low bitmask (buckets 0-31)\n  0xC4      32*4    adwGroupHighBitmaps[32] - Per-group high bitmask (buckets 32-63)\n  0x144+    0x204   Bucket groups (free list heads for 64 buckets, 8 bytes each)\n\nFree Block Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field\n  0x00    4     dwBlockSize - Size of free block (16-byte aligned)\n  0x04    4     pNext - Pointer to next free block in bucket\n  0x08    4     pPrev - Pointer to previous free block (or sentinel)\n  ...\n  -0x04   4     dwBlockSize - Size duplicated at end for coalescing\n\nAllocated Block Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field\n  0x00    4     dwSizeWithFlag - Aligned size | 0x1 (allocation marker)\n  0x04    ...   User data (returned pointer)\n  ...\n  -0x04   4     dwSizeWithFlag - Size duplicated at end for free validation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Bucket index 0x3F (63) handles all allocations 1008+ bytes up to 1024\n  - Empty region search prioritizes recently freed regions for cache locality\n  - Bitmap operations use 0x80000000 >> bit_index for MSB-first ordering",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
