      "name": "CreateHeapRegion",
      "signature": "void * CreateHeapRegion(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Creates a new heap region for small block heap allocation.\n\nThis function expands the heap region array if necessary, then allocates a new\nHeapRegionDescriptor (0x41c4 bytes) and reserves 1MB virtual memory for the region.\nCalled by AllocateSmallBlockHeap when no existing regions have space.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare g_nHeapRegionCount with g_dwHeapRegionCapacity\n2. If equal (array full), reallocate array with HeapReAlloc:\n   - New size = (capacity * 5 + 0x50) * 4 bytes (capacity + 16 entries)\n   - Return NULL on failure\n   - Update g_dwHeapRegionCapacity += 0x10\n   - Store new array pointer in g_pHeapRegionArray\n3. Calculate region descriptor pointer: base + count * 0x14 (20-byte stride)\n4. Allocate descriptor with HeapAlloc (0x41c4 bytes, HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag 0x8)\n5. Store descriptor pointer at region[4] (offset +0x10)\n6. Return NULL if HeapAlloc fails\n7. Reserve virtual memory with VirtualAlloc:\n   - Size: 0x100000 (1MB)\n   - Type: MEM_RESERVE (0x2000)\n   - Protection: PAGE_READWRITE (0x4)\n8. Store virtual memory at region[3] (offset +0xC)\n9. If VirtualAlloc fails, free descriptor and return NULL\n10. Initialize region structure:\n    - region[2] = 0xFFFFFFFF (offset +0x8, free block mask)\n    - region[0] = 0 (offset +0x0, low bits)\n    - region[1] = 0 (offset +0x4, high bits)\n11. Increment g_nHeapRegionCount\n12. Initialize descriptor first dword to 0xFFFFFFFF (sentinel/bucket index)\n13. Return pointer to region descriptor\n\nParameters:\n  None - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  void * - Pointer to new HeapRegionDescriptor (20-byte structure in array)\n           NULL on allocation failure\n\nStructure Layout (HeapRegionDescriptor, 0x14 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x00    4     dwLowBitMask       Low 32 bits of free block bitmap\n  0x04    4     dwHighBitMask      High 32 bits of free block bitmap  \n  0x08    4     dwFreeMask         Available block mask (init 0xFFFFFFFF)\n  0x0C    4     pVirtualMemory     1MB reserved virtual memory region\n  0x10    4     pDescriptor        Heap descriptor (0x41c4 bytes)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x14     - HeapRegionDescriptor stride (20 bytes)\n  0x10     - Capacity growth increment (16 regions)\n  0x50     - Base size constant for realloc calculation\n  0x41c4   - Descriptor allocation size (16836 bytes)\n  0x100000 - Virtual memory reservation (1MB)\n  0x2000   - MEM_RESERVE flag\n  0x8      - HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag\n  0x4      - PAGE_READWRITE protection\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_nHeapRegionCount     - Current count of heap regions\n  g_dwHeapRegionCapacity - Maximum capacity of region array\n  g_pHeapRegionArray     - Array of HeapRegionDescriptor entries\n  g_hCrtHeap             - CRT heap handle (at 0x6fa3ffc4)\n\nSSA Variables (puVar1, pvVar2):\n  puVar1 - Region descriptor pointer (ESI), undefined4 * type\n  pvVar2 - Temporary for API return values (HeapReAlloc/HeapAlloc/VirtualAlloc)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
