      "signature": "void SBH_FreeHeapHeader(void * * ppHeapHeader)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Frees a Small Block Heap (SBH) header structure and releases its associated virtual memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Release the virtual memory region at ppHeapHeader[4] using VirtualFree with MEM_RELEASE (0x8000)\n2. If this header is the list head (PTR_g_SmallBlockHeapListHead_6fa20550), update head pointer to next element\n3. If this is the static sentinel node (g_SmallBlockHeapListHead at 0x6fa1e530), reset g_dwSbhFirstAllocation to -1 (sentinel) and return\n4. For dynamically allocated headers, unlink from doubly-linked list:\n   a. Set next->prev to prev (ppHeapHeader[1]->pPrev = ppHeapHeader->pPrev)\n   b. Set prev->next to next (ppHeapHeader[0]+4 = ppHeapHeader[1])\n5. Free the header structure using HeapFree on g_hCrtHeap\n\nParameters:\n  ppHeapHeader - Pointer to SBH header structure to free. Structure layout:\n                 +0x00: pPrev (prev node in list)\n                 +0x04: pNext (next node in list)  \n                 +0x10: pVirtualMemory (virtual memory region to release)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Static sentinel node (g_SmallBlockHeapListHead) is not heap-freed; only its allocation flag is reset\n  - Function always succeeds; VirtualFree/HeapFree failures are not checked\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  - PTR_g_SmallBlockHeapListHead_6fa20550: Updated if freeing the head node\n  - g_dwSbhFirstAllocation: Set to 0xFFFFFFFF when freeing sentinel node\n\nCalled By:\n  - FUN_6fa1770b (SBH page reclamation) when all pages in a heap region are freed",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:54ffff5ceafbb1247d2270b70dfe4f31",
