      "name": "SBH_ReclaimDeferredPages",
      "signature": "void SBH_ReclaimDeferredPages(int nMaxPagesToReclaim)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Reclaims deferred (unused) pages from the Small Block Heap to reduce memory usage.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Start from g_pSmallBlockHeapListTail and iterate through heap headers\n2. Skip headers with no allocated virtual memory (pVirtualMemory == -1)\n3. Scan page descriptors from highest to lowest offset (0x3FF000 down to 0)\n4. For each page descriptor with state 0xF0 (deferred/unused):\n   a. Call VirtualFree with MEM_DECOMMIT (0x4000) to release the 4KB page\n   b. If successful, mark descriptor as -1 (freed)\n   c. Decrement global g_nSbhDeferredPageCount\n   d. Update pFirstFreeDescriptor if this is lower address\n   e. Decrement nMaxPagesToReclaim; exit if quota reached\n5. After scanning region, if pages were freed and first page slot is free (-1):\n   a. Check if all 1024 page descriptors are freed\n   b. If so, call SBH_FreeHeapHeader to release entire heap region\n6. Move to next heap header (ppHeapHeader[1])\n7. Exit when returning to list tail or nMaxPagesToReclaim exhausted\n\nParameters:\n  nMaxPagesToReclaim - Maximum number of 4KB pages to reclaim (0 = none)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Called when g_nSbhDeferredPageCount reaches 32 (0x20 threshold)\n  - Early exit if nMaxPagesToReclaim becomes 0 or negative\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3FF000 - Initial page offset (page 1023 * 0x1000)\n  0x1000   - Page size (4KB)\n  0x804    - Offset to last page descriptor in header (element 0x402 = 1026)\n  0x4000   - MEM_DECOMMIT flag for VirtualFree\n  0xF0     - Page state: all blocks free (240 free small blocks)\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Page descriptor state: freed/decommitted\n  0x400    - Number of page descriptors per heap region (1024)\n\nHeap Header Structure (partial):\n  Offset  Size  Field                Description\n  +0x00   4     pPrev                Previous header in linked list\n  +0x04   4     pNext                Next header in linked list\n  +0x0C   4     pFirstFreeDescriptor Pointer to first free page descriptor\n  +0x10   4     pVirtualMemory       Base address of virtual memory region\n  +0x18   4     dwFirstPageState     State of first page descriptor\n  +0x20   8*N   pageDescriptors[]    Array of 1024 page descriptor pairs",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4356a93c484fa354f7841c9d1d714a19",
