      "name": "SBH_AllocateBlockFromPage",
      "signature": "void * SBH_AllocateBlockFromPage(int * pnPageHeader, dword dwAvailableBlocks, dword dwRequestedSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates a block of requested size from a Small Block Heap page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current free pointer from pnPageHeader[0] and page end boundary (pnPageHeader + 0xF8)\n2. If remaining space (pnPageHeader[1]) >= requested size, allocate from current position (fast path)\n3. Otherwise, search for a free block by scanning block headers:\n   a. Start from current position or skip to first non-zero block\n   b. Walk through blocks using size byte at each block start\n   c. When zero byte found, count consecutive zero bytes (free run)\n   d. If free run >= requested size, use this block\n   e. Decrement available blocks counter; if exhausted, return NULL\n4. When suitable block found, update page header:\n   - Set new free pointer to block + requested size\n   - Set remaining space to free run - requested size\n   - If at page boundary, reset to data start (pnPageHeader + 8)\n5. Write block size to first byte of allocated block\n6. Return pointer computed as: (block_ptr + 8) * 16 - pnPageHeader * 15\n\nParameters:\n  pnPageHeader - Pointer to page header structure:\n    [0x00] int: Current free block pointer\n    [0x04] int: Remaining contiguous free space\n    [0x08] byte[]: Block data area start\n    [0xF8] byte: End of usable page space (boundary marker)\n  dwAvailableBlocks - Total available blocks to search before giving up\n  dwRequestedSize - Number of bytes to allocate (truncated to byte for header)\n\nReturns:\n  void* - Computed pointer to allocated block data area (after 8-byte header)\n          NULL (0) if allocation failed (no suitable free block found)\n\nStructure Layout (Page Header, 0x100 bytes total):\n  Offset  Size  Field          Description\n  0x00    4     pFreePtr       Current free block pointer\n  0x04    4     dwRemaining    Remaining contiguous free bytes\n  0x08    0xF0  abBlockData    Block data area (240 bytes)\n  0xF8    8     abBoundary     Page boundary/sentinel area\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Fast path when current free pointer has enough contiguous space\n  - Wraparound search from page start if initial search hits boundary\n  - Zero bytes indicate free space; non-zero byte is block size\n  - Return pointer calculation normalizes block address to heap-relative offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4f3543287939943021eaf1632a1582f1",
