      "name": "ShowMessageBoxWithActiveWindow",
      "signature": "int ShowMessageBoxWithActiveWindow(char * lpszText, char * lpszCaption, dword dwType)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Displays a message box using the current active window as owner.\n\nLazily loads user32.dll and resolves MessageBoxA, GetActiveWindow, and\nGetLastActivePopup function pointers on first call. Caches resolved\npointers in global variables for subsequent calls.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pfnMessageBoxA already resolved\n2. If not resolved, load user32.dll via LoadLibraryA\n3. If library loaded, resolve MessageBoxA via GetProcAddress\n4. If MessageBoxA resolved, also resolve GetActiveWindow and GetLastActivePopup\n5. Get active window handle via GetActiveWindow if available\n6. Get last active popup of active window via GetLastActivePopup if both available\n7. Call MessageBoxA with resolved owner window handle\n8. Return MessageBoxA result (IDOK, IDCANCEL, etc.) or 0 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  lpszText    - char *  - Message text to display in the message box\n  lpszCaption - char *  - Caption/title for the message box window\n  dwType      - uint    - Message box type flags (MB_OK, MB_YESNO, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n  int - MessageBoxA return value (button ID) or 0 if library/function load fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 if user32.dll cannot be loaded\n  - Returns 0 if MessageBoxA cannot be resolved\n  - Uses NULL owner window if GetActiveWindow not resolved\n  - Uses active window directly if GetLastActivePopup not resolved\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n  g_pfnMessageBoxA       - Cached FARPROC for MessageBoxA\n  g_pfnGetActiveWindow   - Cached FARPROC for GetActiveWindow\n  g_pfnGetLastActivePopup - Cached FARPROC for GetLastActivePopup\n\nCalled By:\n  DisplayCrtRuntimeErrorMessage - CRT error display handler",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:f59c01a33eca433430cfbab05d487108",
