      "name": "CRT_GetErrnoPtr",
      "signature": "uint * CRT_GetErrnoPtr(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Returns pointer to thread-local errno value in CRT data structure.\n\nClassification: Leaf function, Public API accessor\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetThreadLocalCrtData() to get thread-local CRT data base pointer\n2. Add offset +8 (2 DWORDs) to reach errno field\n3. Return pointer to errno\n\nReturns:\n- uint * - Pointer to errno value in thread-local storage (offset +8 from TLS base)\n\nCallers:\n- CRT_MapDosErrorToErrno, CRT_StrToLongInternal, CRT_lseek, CRT_write\n- Various CRT functions that need to set/get errno for error reporting\n\nStructure Layout (Thread-Local CRT Data):\nOffset  Size  Field       Description\n0x00    4     field_0     Unknown/reserved\n0x04    4     field_4     Unknown/reserved  \n0x08    4     errno       C runtime errno value (this function returns pointer here)\n\nNotes:\n- Simple accessor function with no error conditions\n- Returns offset +8 into thread-local data (pDVar1 + 2 in pointer arithmetic)\n- Used by CRT functions to report POSIX-style error codes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
