      "name": "CRT_GetDosErrnoPtr",
      "signature": "uint * CRT_GetDosErrnoPtr(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Returns pointer to DOS errno field within thread-local CRT data block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetThreadLocalCrtData() to get/allocate thread's CRT TLS block\n2. Add 0xC (12 bytes = 3 DWORDs) to base pointer to reach DOS errno field\n3. Return pointer to DOS errno (offset 0x0C in TLS block)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  DWORD* - Pointer to DOS errno field at TLS block offset 0x0C\n           Used by CRT functions to store DOS error codes from system calls\n\nTLS Block Layout (relevant fields):\n  Offset  Size  Field          Description\n  0x00    4     dwThreadId     Owning thread ID\n  0x04    4     dwPrevHandle   Previous handle sentinel (-1)\n  0x08    4     dwErrno        C errno value\n  0x0C    4     dwDosErrno     DOS/Win32 error code (THIS FIELD)\n\nCallers:\n  CRT_MapDosErrorToErrno - Maps Win32 error to errno, stores both\n  CRT_lseek - Sets DOS errno on seek failure\n  CRT_write, CRT_write_nolock - Sets DOS errno on write failure\n  FUN_6fa17ca3, FUN_6fa17d22, FUN_6fa1814e, FUN_6fa181e1",
