      "name": "CRT_FreeIobHandle",
      "signature": "int CRT_FreeIobHandle(uint dwFileHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Frees/invalidates a CRT file handle in the IOB (I/O Block) table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nFileHandle is within bounds (< g_dwMaxIobHandles)\n2. Calculate bucket index (nFileHandle >> 5) and slot offset ((nFileHandle & 0x1f) * 0x24)\n3. Get pointer to IOB entry from g_apIobBlocks[bucket] + offset\n4. Verify handle is in-use: check flags byte bit 0 set AND OS handle != -1\n5. If g_dwCrtOutputHandleMode == 1 (console mode), clear standard handles:\n   - Handle 0 (stdin): SetStdHandle(STD_INPUT_HANDLE, NULL)\n   - Handle 1 (stdout): SetStdHandle(STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE, NULL)\n   - Handle 2 (stderr): SetStdHandle(STD_ERROR_HANDLE, NULL)\n6. Mark handle invalid by setting OS handle field to -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n7. Return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\n  nFileHandle (uint): CRT file descriptor index to free (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr)\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -1 on error (sets errno=EBADF=9, _doserrno=0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns -1 if handle >= g_dwMaxIobHandles (invalid index)\n  - Returns -1 if handle not in-use (flags bit 0 clear or OS handle already -1)\n  - Standard handles 0-2 get SetStdHandle(NULL) only when g_dwCrtOutputHandleMode==1\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x24 = 36 bytes per IOB entry stride\n  0x1f = 31 = mask for slot index within bucket (32 entries per bucket)\n  0xfffffff6 = STD_INPUT_HANDLE (-10)\n  0xfffffff5 = STD_OUTPUT_HANDLE (-11)\n  0xfffffff4 = STD_ERROR_HANDLE (-12)\n  9 = EBADF (Bad file descriptor)",
