      "name": "CRT_FdToHandle",
      "signature": "void * CRT_FdToHandle(uint dwFileDescriptor)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT_FdToHandle - Convert CRT file descriptor to Win32 HANDLE\n\nWorker function that validates a CRT file descriptor index and returns\nthe associated Win32 HANDLE from the IOB (I/O Block) table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Bounds check: Verify dwFileDescriptor < g_dwMaxIobHandles\n2. Calculate IOB entry address using bucket/slot addressing:\n   - Bucket index = dwFileDescriptor >> 5 (divide by 32)\n   - Slot within bucket = dwFileDescriptor & 0x1F (mod 32)\n   - Entry address = g_apIobBlocks[bucket] + slot * 0x24\n3. Test if file is open: Check bit 0 of flags byte at offset +4\n4. If valid (in bounds AND bit 0 set):\n   - Return HANDLE from IOB entry offset 0\n5. If invalid:\n   - Set errno = 9 (EBADF - Bad file descriptor)\n   - Set doserrno = 0\n   - Return -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileDescriptor (uint) - CRT file descriptor index into IOB table\n                            Valid range: 0 to g_dwMaxIobHandles-1\n\nReturns:\n  void * - Win32 HANDLE on success\n  0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Invalid file descriptor (errno set to EBADF)\n\nIOB Entry Layout (36 bytes / 0x24 stride):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n  0x00    4     hFile           HANDLE  Win32 file handle\n  0x04    1     bFlags          byte    Status flags\n                                        Bit 0: File is open\n\nIOB Table Addressing:\n  g_apIobBlocks[] is array of pointers to IOB buckets\n  Each bucket holds 32 IOB entries (fd & 0x1F selects slot)\n  Bucket selected by fd >> 5\n\nError Codes:\n  errno = 9 (EBADF) - File descriptor out of range or not open\n  doserrno = 0 - Cleared on error (no Windows error)\n\nCallers:\n  CRT_lseek_nolock - File seek operation\n  FUN_6fa1814e - File flush operation (FlushFileBuffers)\n  FUN_6fa1823e - Additional CRT I/O operation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
