      "name": "CRT_LockFileHandle",
      "signature": "void CRT_LockFileHandle(uint dwFileHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Acquires the critical section lock for a CRT file handle (IOB entry).\n\nUses double-checked locking to lazily initialize the per-handle critical section\non first access. The IOB array is organized as buckets of 32 entries, with each\nentry being 0x24 (36) bytes containing file state and a CRITICAL_SECTION.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute bucket index: dwFileHandle >> 5 (divide by 32)\n2. Compute slot index within bucket: dwFileHandle & 0x1f (mod 32)\n3. Compute byte offset: slot * 0x24 (36-byte stride per IOB entry)\n4. Get pointer to IOB entry from g_apIobBlocks[bucket] + offset\n5. Check if critical section initialized (offset +0x8 flag)\n6. If not initialized:\n   a. Enter global CRT critical section (index 0x11)\n   b. Double-check initialization flag\n   c. If still uninitialized, call InitializeCriticalSection on entry+0xc\n   d. Increment initialization flag at entry+0x8\n   e. Leave global CRT critical section\n7. Enter the per-handle critical section at entry+0xc\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileHandle (uint) - CRT file handle index (0-based), used to compute bucket/slot\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function acquires lock but does not return status\n\nIOB Entry Structure Layout (0x24 bytes per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field                Description\n  0x00    8     (file state)         File descriptor state fields\n  0x08    4     dwInitialized        Critical section init flag (0=uninitialized)\n  0x0c    24    criticalSection      CRITICAL_SECTION for per-handle locking\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1f - Mask for slot index within bucket (32 entries per bucket)\n  0x5  - Shift count for bucket index (2^5 = 32)\n  0x24 - IOB entry stride (36 bytes)\n  0x11 - Global CRT critical section index for IOB initialization\n  0x8  - Offset to initialization flag within IOB entry\n  0xc  - Offset to CRITICAL_SECTION within IOB entry\n\nCallers:\n  CRT_lseek, CRT_write, FUN_6fa1814e, FUN_6fa181e1\n\nRelated:\n  CRT_UnlockFileHandle - Releases the lock acquired by this function\n  g_apIobBlocks - Global array of pointers to IOB bucket arrays",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:89c8ec97483b3d89b792dc7acc8a9af7",
