      "name": "CRT_UnlockFileHandle",
      "signature": "void CRT_UnlockFileHandle(uint dwFileHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Releases the per-file-handle critical section lock for CRT I/O synchronization.\n\nClassification: Internal utility - paired with CRT_LockFileHandle for thread-safe file operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate bucket index from file handle (dwFileHandle >> 5)\n2. Calculate slot index within bucket (dwFileHandle & 0x1F)\n3. Compute IOB entry address: g_apIobBlocks[bucket] + (slot * 0x24) + 0x0C\n4. Call LeaveCriticalSection on the IOB entry's embedded CRITICAL_SECTION\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileHandle (uint) - CRT file descriptor (0-based). Used to locate IOB entry.\n                        Upper 27 bits = bucket index, lower 5 bits = slot index.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Critical section is released unconditionally.\n\nStructure Layout (IOB Entry - 0x24 bytes per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field                Type              Description\n  0x00    4     hOsHandle            HANDLE            OS file handle\n  0x04    4     dwFlags              uint              File state flags\n  0x08    4     nCritSectInitialized int               Lock initialized flag\n  0x0C    24    critSect             CRITICAL_SECTION  Per-handle lock\n\nAddress Calculation:\n  bucket = dwFileHandle >> 5 (divide by 32)\n  slot = dwFileHandle & 0x1F (modulo 32)\n  pEntry = g_apIobBlocks[bucket] + slot * 0x24 + 0x0C\n\nCallers: CRT_lseek, CRT_write, FUN_6fa1814e, FUN_6fa181e1\n\nRelated Functions:\n  CRT_LockFileHandle - Acquires the lock (lazy-initializes critical section)\n  g_apIobBlocks - Global array of IOB block pointers at 0x6fa3ffe0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
