      "name": "CrtFlushFileStream",
      "signature": "int CrtFlushFileStream(int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CrtFlushFileStream - Flush a CRT file stream buffer to disk\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call CrtFlushWriteBuffer to flush internal write buffer to OS file handle\n2. If buffer flush failed, return -1 immediately\n3. Check stream flags at offset +0xD for FCOMMMIT flag (0x40)\n4. If FCOMMIT set, call CrtCommitFileHandle to force OS-level flush\n5. Return 0 on success, -1 if commit failed\n\nParameters:\n  pStream [int *] - Pointer to CRT FILE stream structure\n    +0x00: Current buffer position\n    +0x08: Base buffer pointer  \n    +0x0C: Flags (low byte: mode, high byte: extended flags)\n    +0x0D: Extended flags (0x40 = FCOMMIT - commit on flush)\n    +0x10: OS file descriptor handle\n\nReturns:\n  0  - Success (buffer flushed, optionally committed)\n  -1 - Failure (buffer flush or commit failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If FCOMMIT flag not set, only buffer is flushed without OS commit\n  - Return uses NEG+SBB pattern: -(uint)(result != 0) yields 0 or -1\n\nRelated Functions:\n  FUN_6fa17e94 - CrtFlushWriteBuffer - flushes write buffer using _write\n  FUN_6fa1814e - CrtCommitFileHandle - calls FlushFileBuffers on handle",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0db91ea76f5c7c9fd0bef446c106db61",
