      "name": "CrtWriteBufferToFile",
      "signature": "int CrtWriteBufferToFile(int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes the write buffer of a CRT file stream to disk.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if stream is open for writing (mode & 3 == 2)\n2. Check if stream has buffering enabled (flags & 0x108)\n3. Calculate bytes to write: current position - buffer base\n4. If bytes > 0, call CRT_write to write buffer contents\n5. On success, clear dirty flag (0x02) if stream is text mode (0x80)\n6. On failure, set error flag (0x20) and return -1\n7. Reset buffer: clear count, reset position to buffer base\n\nParameters:\n  pStream - Pointer to CRT FILE stream structure:\n    [0x00] pCurrentPos  - Current buffer position pointer\n    [0x04] nCount       - Bytes remaining in buffer\n    [0x08] pBufferBase  - Base address of buffer\n    [0x0C] dwFlags      - Stream flags/mode bits\n    [0x10] nFileDesc    - File descriptor for write\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -1 on write error (error flag 0x20 set)\n\nFlag Bits (offset 0x0C):\n  0x02 - Dirty/needs flush (cleared on successful text mode flush)\n  0x03 - Mode mask (2 = write mode)\n  0x20 - Error flag (set on write failure)\n  0x80 - Text mode flag\n  0x108 - Buffering enabled mask\n\nClassification: Worker function (CRT stream I/O)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4c053343a65baac58fac65c0d3534b2b",
