      "name": "CrtFlushAllFileStreams",
      "signature": "int CrtFlushAllFileStreams(int nFlushMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes all active CRT file streams with mode-dependent behavior.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize success counter (EBX=0) and error flag (EDI=0)\n2. Acquire CRT critical section 2 (stream table lock)\n3. Loop through all streams (ESI=0 to g_nCrtStreamCount):\n   a. Get stream pointer from g_apCrtFileStreams[index]\n   b. Skip if NULL or stream flags at +0xC missing bits 0x83 (read/write/active)\n   c. Lock the individual stream via CrtLockFileStreamByIndex\n   d. Re-fetch stream pointer and verify flags still valid\n   e. If nFlushMode==1 (count mode): flush and increment counter on success\n   f. If nFlushMode==0 (error mode) and write flag (0x02) set: flush and set error on failure\n   g. Unlock stream via CrtUnlockFileStreamByIndex\n4. Release CRT critical section 2\n5. Return counter (mode 1) or error flag (mode 0)\n\nParameters:\n  nFlushMode (int) - Flush operation mode:\n    0 = Flush write streams, return -1 on any failure, 0 on success\n    1 = Flush all active streams, return count of successfully flushed streams\n\nReturns:\n  int - Mode 1: Count of successfully flushed streams\n        Mode 0: 0 on success, -1 if any flush failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty stream table (g_nCrtStreamCount <= 0): Returns 0\n  - NULL stream entries: Silently skipped\n  - Inactive streams (flags & 0x83 == 0): Skipped\n  - Stream state change during iteration: Re-checks flags after lock\n\nFlag Bits at stream+0xC:\n  0x01 - Read mode active\n  0x02 - Write mode active (checked in mode 0)\n  0x80 - Stream allocated/in use\n  0x83 - Combined mask for active readable/writable streams\n\nRelated Functions:\n  CrtFlushAllFileStreamsCount - Wrapper that calls this with nFlushMode=1\n  CrtFlushFileStream - Flushes individual stream\n  CrtLockFileStreamByIndex - Acquires per-stream lock\n  CrtUnlockFileStreamByIndex - Releases per-stream lock",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e7b052927c73f8415c227814d8219b82",
