      "name": "CrtInvokeNewHandler",
      "signature": "int CrtInvokeNewHandler(uint dwRequestedSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CRT New Handler Invocation - Invokes user-registered new handler for memory allocation retry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if new handler function pointer (g_pfnCrtNewHandler) is registered\n2. If handler exists, call it with the requested allocation size\n3. Return 1 (TRUE) if handler succeeds (non-zero return), enabling allocation retry\n4. Return 0 (FALSE) if no handler registered or handler returns failure\n\nParameters:\n  dwRequestedSize (uint) - Size of failed allocation request in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 if new handler succeeded and caller should retry allocation\n        0 if no handler registered or handler returned failure\n\nFunction Classification: Internal utility - C runtime new handler wrapper\n\nCaller Analysis:\n  Called by CrtCallocMemory and __nh_malloc when HeapAlloc fails\n  Both callers use return value to decide whether to retry allocation loop\n\nMemory Model:\n  Reads global g_pfnCrtNewHandler function pointer\n  Handler callback may attempt to free memory or throw exception\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If g_pfnCrtNewHandler is NULL, immediately returns 0 (no retry)\n  Handler may throw C++ bad_alloc exception instead of returning",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
