      "signature": "int CompareStringsLocaleAwareN(byte * pbString1, byte * pbString2, uint nMaxCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Case-insensitive string comparison with locale awareness and length limit.\nSimilar to _strnicmp - compares at most nMaxCount characters.\n\nCLASSIFICATION: Worker function - length-limited variant of CompareStringsLocaleAware\n\nALGORITHM:\n1. If nMaxCount is 0, return 0 immediately (empty comparison)\n2. Check g_dwLocaleCodePage to determine comparison mode\n3. ASCII mode (code page == 0):\n   a. Loop through both strings up to nMaxCount characters\n   b. Load bytes from pbString1 (AH) and pbString2 (AL)\n   c. Check for null terminator in either string\n   d. Convert uppercase A-Z (0x41-0x5A) to lowercase by adding 0x20\n   e. Compare lowercase versions; if unequal, compute result\n   f. Decrement nMaxCount counter; continue if not exhausted\n   g. Return -1 if string1 < string2, +1 if string1 > string2\n4. Locale mode (code page != 0):\n   a. Increment g_nLocaleLockRefCount atomically (LOCK prefix)\n   b. If g_fLocaleMultiThreaded > 0, enter critical section 0x13\n   c. Loop through both strings up to nMaxCount characters\n   d. Call ToLowerCharLocale for each character\n   e. Compare lowercase versions; if equal, continue loop\n   f. Return -1 if string1 < string2, +1 if string1 > string2\n5. Release lock: decrement ref count or leave critical section\n6. Return 0 if strings are equal within nMaxCount characters\n\nPARAMETERS:\n  pbString1 - First null-terminated string to compare\n  pbString2 - Second null-terminated string to compare\n  nMaxCount - Maximum number of characters to compare\n\nRETURNS:\n  int - Comparison result:\n    -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): pbString1 < pbString2\n     0: pbString1 == pbString2 (case-insensitive, up to nMaxCount)\n    +1: pbString1 > pbString2\n\nSPECIAL CASES:\n  - nMaxCount == 0: Returns 0 immediately\n  - Null terminator before nMaxCount: Comparison stops, result computed\n  - ASCII path: Uses inline uppercase conversion (0x41-0x5A range check)\n  - Locale path: Uses ToLowerCharLocale for proper locale handling\n\nMAGIC NUMBERS:\n  0x40 (64)  - One less than ASCII 'A' (for > comparison)\n  0x5A (90)  - ASCII 'Z' character (for < comparison)\n  0x5B (91)  - One more than ASCII 'Z' (for boundary check)\n  0x20 (32)  - ASCII case difference (lowercase = uppercase + 0x20)\n  0x13 (19)  - Critical section index for locale operations\n\nGLOBALS ACCESSED:\n  g_dwLocaleCodePage (0x6fa3eacc) - Current locale code page (0 = ASCII)\n  g_nLocaleLockRefCount (0x6fa400e8) - Locale lock reference count\n  g_fLocaleMultiThreaded (0x6fa400e4) - Multi-threaded locale flag\n\nTHREAD SAFETY:\n  Uses LOCK prefix for atomic increment/decrement of ref count.\n  Enters critical section 0x13 when multi-threaded locale is enabled.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:662566ebcde3842108cf876001e2ae79",
