      "name": "CrtFlushFileStreamLocked",
      "signature": "int CrtFlushFileStreamLocked(int * pFileStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes a file stream with thread-safe locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result to -1 (error state)\n2. Check if stream flag byte at offset +0xC has bit 0x40 set (no-lock flag)\n3. If flag set: Clear flags at offset +0xC and return -1 (early exit)\n4. If flag not set: Lock stream with CrtLockFileStream\n5. Call CrtFlushAndCloseStream to perform actual flush\n6. Unlock stream with CrtUnlockFileStream\n7. Return flush result\n\nParameters:\n  pFileStream - Pointer to CRT file stream structure (int *)\n                Offset +0xC contains stream state flags\n\nReturns:\n  int - 0 on success, -1 on error or if stream marked as no-lock\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  If bit 0x40 is set in flags, bypasses locking and clears flags\n\nFlag Bits (offset +0xC):\n  0x40 - Stream requires no locking (single-threaded or already locked)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e9b7e334c31a0ed876fb0ca3fc54ed48",
