      "name": "CrtFlushAndCloseStream",
      "signature": "int CrtFlushAndCloseStream(int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes and closes a CRT file stream (internal close worker).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result to -1 (error)\n2. Check if stream needs flushing (flags & 0x83 != 0)\n3. If needs flush:\n   a. Write buffer to file via CrtWriteBufferToFile\n   b. Free temporary stream buffer via CrtFreeStreamBuffer\n   c. Close underlying file descriptor via CrtCloseFileDescriptor\n   d. If close failed, set result to -1\n   e. If close succeeded and user buffer exists (pStream[7] != NULL):\n      - Free user buffer via CrtFreeMemory\n      - Clear user buffer pointer\n4. Clear stream flags (pStream[3] = 0)\n5. Return result (0 on success, -1 on error)\n\nParameters:\n  pStream - Pointer to CRT FILE stream structure:\n    [0x00] pCurrentPos  - Current buffer position pointer\n    [0x04] nCount       - Bytes remaining in buffer\n    [0x08] pBufferBase  - Base address of buffer\n    [0x0C] dwFlags      - Stream flags/mode bits\n    [0x10] nFileDesc    - File descriptor\n    [0x1C] pUserBuffer  - User-allocated buffer (freed on close)\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -1 on error (write or close failure)\n\nFlag Bits (offset 0x0C):\n  0x01 - Read mode\n  0x02 - Write mode / dirty flag\n  0x80 - Text mode\n  0x83 - Mask for flush-required states\n\nClassification: Worker function (CRT stream I/O internals)\nCalled by: FUN_6fa180d1 (stream close wrapper with locking)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
