      "name": "CrtCommitFileHandle",
      "signature": "DWORD CrtCommitFileHandle(uint dwFileDescriptor)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "CrtCommitFileHandle - Commits a CRT file descriptor by flushing OS buffers to disk\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file descriptor is within valid range (< g_dwMaxIobHandles)\n2. If invalid, set errno to EBADF (9) and return -1\n3. Calculate IOB block index (fd >> 5) and slot offset ((fd & 0x1F) * 0x24)\n4. Check if file handle is open (flags byte at offset +4 has bit 0 set)\n5. If handle not open, set errno to EBADF and return -1\n6. Lock the file handle via CRT_LockFileHandle for thread safety\n7. Re-check handle is still open after acquiring lock (race condition guard)\n8. If handle closed during lock wait, set errno and return -1\n9. Convert file descriptor to OS handle via CRT_FdToHandle\n10. Call FlushFileBuffers on the OS handle to commit pending writes\n11. If flush fails, get Windows error via GetLastError\n12. If error occurred, store in DOS errno via CRT_GetDosErrnoPtr\n13. On error, set errno to EBADF and return -1\n14. Unlock file handle via CRT_UnlockFileHandle\n15. Return 0 on success, -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileDescriptor [uint] - CRT file descriptor index (0-based)\n    Used to index into g_apIobBlocks array of IOB structures\n\nReturns:\n  0         - Success, file buffers committed to disk\n  0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - Failure, errno set to EBADF (9)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Thread-safe: Acquires file lock before operations\n  - Double-checks handle validity after lock acquisition (race guard)\n  - EBADF (9) set for: invalid fd, closed handle, or flush failure\n\nStructure Layout (IOB entry, stride 0x24 = 36 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Type   Description\n  +0x00   4     osHandle     HANDLE OS file handle\n  +0x04   1     flags        byte   Status flags (bit 0 = open)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1F - Mask for slot index within IOB block (32 slots per block)\n  0x24 - IOB entry stride (36 bytes per entry)\n  0x9  - EBADF errno value (bad file descriptor)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  CRT_LockFileHandle   - Acquire thread lock on file descriptor\n  CRT_UnlockFileHandle - Release thread lock on file descriptor\n  CRT_FdToHandle       - Convert CRT fd to Windows HANDLE\n  FlushFileBuffers     - Windows API to flush file buffers",
