      "name": "CrtCloseFileDescriptor",
      "signature": "int CrtCloseFileDescriptor(uint dwFileDescriptor)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Closes a CRT file descriptor with validation and locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file descriptor is within IOB handle range (< g_dwMaxIobHandles)\n2. Calculate IOB block bucket (fd >> 5) and offset within bucket (fd & 0x1f)\n3. Check IOB entry flags at offset +4 in structure (stride 0x24 bytes)\n4. If flag bit 0x01 set (handle is open/valid):\n   a. Lock the file handle via CRT_LockFileHandle\n   b. Call internal close worker FUN_6fa1823e to close OS handle\n   c. Unlock the file handle via CRT_UnlockFileHandle\n   d. Return close result (0 success, -1 error)\n5. If validation fails:\n   a. Set errno to 9 (EBADF - bad file descriptor)\n   b. Set dos_errno to 0\n   c. Return -1\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileDescriptor - CRT file descriptor index (0-based, uint)\n\nReturns:\n  0 on successful close\n  -1 on error (invalid descriptor or close failure)\n\nError Handling:\n  EBADF (9) - File descriptor out of range or not open\n\nIOB Block Structure (stride 0x24 = 36 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x00    4     hOsHandle   OS file handle (HANDLE)\n  0x04    1     bFlags      Status flags (bit 0 = open)\n  ...     ...   ...         Other fields\n\nGlobal References:\n  g_dwMaxIobHandles (0x6fa400e0) - Max file descriptors\n  g_apIobBlocks (0x6fa3ffe0) - Array of IOB block pointers\n\nClassification: Worker function (CRT file I/O)\nCalled by: CrtFlushAndCloseStream",
