      "name": "CrtCloseHandleInternal",
      "signature": "int CrtCloseHandleInternal(uint dwFileDescriptor)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Internal worker function to close a file descriptor's OS handle and free its IOB entry.\nCalled by CrtCloseFileDescriptor after acquiring the file handle lock.\n\nClassification: Worker function - performs actual close operation while caller manages locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert file descriptor to OS handle via CRT_FdToHandle\n2. If handle is invalid (0xFFFFFFFF), skip to cleanup (handle already closed or never opened)\n3. For stdout (fd=1) or stderr (fd=2), check if they share the same handle\n   - If stdout and stderr point to same handle, skip CloseHandle to avoid double-close\n4. Call CloseHandle on the OS handle\n5. If CloseHandle fails, capture error via GetLastError\n6. Free the IOB handle entry via CRT_FreeIobHandle\n7. Clear the flags byte in the IOB block entry (offset +4 in 0x24-byte stride structure)\n8. If error occurred, map DOS error to errno via CRT_MapDosErrorToErrno, return -1\n9. On success, return 0\n\nParameters:\n  dwFileDescriptor (uint) - CRT file descriptor number (0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr, 3+ user files)\n\nReturns:\n  0 on success\n  -1 on failure (errno set via CRT_MapDosErrorToErrno)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Invalid handle (0xFFFFFFFF): Treated as success, only frees IOB entry\n  Shared stdout/stderr: Only closes once to prevent double-free\n  Standard streams (fd 1,2): Special handling to check handle sharing\n\nStructure Layout (IOB Block Entry, 0x24 bytes per entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field       Description\n  0x00    4     hOsHandle   OS file handle (HANDLE)\n  0x04    1     bFlags      File descriptor flags (bit 0 = in use)\n\nGlobal Access:\n  g_apIobBlocks - Array of pointers to IOB block pages, indexed by (fd >> 5)\n  Each page contains 32 IOB entries at 0x24 byte stride\n  Entry index within page: (fd and 0x1F)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:13d93ac20184bc58361cf8520dc0da42",
