      "name": "CrtFreeStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "void CrtFreeStreamBuffer(int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Frees the buffer associated with a CRT FILE stream structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check stream is active: (flags & 0x83) != 0 tests read/write/text modes\n2. Check buffer is allocated: (flags & 0x08) != 0 tests buffer-allocated flag\n3. If both conditions pass:\n   a. Free buffer memory via CrtFreeMemory(pStream[2])\n   b. Clear buffer flags: AND with 0xFBF7 clears bits 0x08 and 0x0400\n   c. Reset buffer position pointer pStream[0] to NULL\n   d. Reset buffer base pointer pStream[2] to NULL\n   e. Reset byte count pStream[1] to 0\n4. Return (void function, no error indication)\n\nParameters:\n  pStream - Pointer to CRT FILE stream structure:\n    [0x00] pCurrentPos  - Current buffer read/write position\n    [0x04] nBytesInBuf  - Bytes remaining/available in buffer\n    [0x08] pBufferBase  - Allocated buffer base address\n    [0x0C] dwFlags      - Stream state flags (low word used)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Function silently succeeds.\n  Buffer is freed only if both conditions are met; otherwise no action taken.\n\nFlag Bits (offset 0x0C):\n  0x01 - Read mode active\n  0x02 - Write mode active / buffer dirty\n  0x08 - Buffer dynamically allocated (freed by this function)\n  0x80 - Text mode (CR/LF translation)\n  0x83 - Mask: any active stream mode\n  0x0400 - Buffer state flag (cleared with 0x08)\n  0xFBF7 - Clear mask for bits 0x08 and 0x0400\n\nClassification: Cleanup function (CRT stream I/O internals)\nCalled by: CrtFlushAndCloseStream",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:f38bb98de0cae7e771d97b2937aba094",
