      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.11": 62,
        "LoD/1.11b": 62,
        "LoD/1.12a": 62,
        "LoD/1.13c": 62,
        "LoD/1.13d": 62
      },
      "name": "ConvertUnsignedToRadixString",
      "signature": "void ConvertUnsignedToRadixString(uint radix, int isNegative)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Converts an unsigned integer to a string representation in a specified radix (base).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if value is negative (param_2 != 0); if so, prepend '-' sign and negate value\n2. Initialize buffer pointer at ECX (buffer start)\n3. Iterate through digits by repeatedly dividing by radix:\n   - Get remainder (digit value) via DIV instruction\n   - Convert digit: 0-9 become '0'-'9' (add 0x30), 10+ become 'A'+ (add 0x57)\n   - Store digit at current buffer position\n   - Increment buffer pointer\n   - Continue while quotient is non-zero\n4. Null-terminate string at current buffer position\n5. Reverse string in-place by swapping characters from both ends until pointers meet\n\nParameters:\n- EAX (implicit): Unsigned integer value to convert\n- ECX (implicit): Pointer to output buffer (must have sufficient space)\n- radix: Base for conversion (2-36; typically 10 for decimal, 16 for hex)\n- isNegative: Sign indicator (non-zero if value should be treated as negative)\n\nReturns:\n- void; output string written to buffer pointed to by ECX\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative numbers: Leading '-' character added if isNegative != 0\n- Digit offsets: Remainder 0-9 use offset 0x30 ('0'), 10-35 use offset 0x57 ('A'-'Z')\n- String reversal: Digits stored in reverse during conversion, then reversed in-place\n- Null termination: String properly null-terminated after conversion and reversal",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:cf846ceddb7679dcf445e4b7493b026d",
